Object.assign(window.IND_FEED_BODY, {"hp-fk.island-of-tongues-2":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.island-of-tongues:2","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Bazaar of Many Tongues","text":"\"उनका बचपन आपस में एक चोटी की तरह गूँथ गया। अंडमान के किसी बच्चे का आज नाम भले बांग्ला हो, उसका सबसे पक्का दोस्त तमिल हो सकता है, अध्यापिका मलयाली, और पसंदीदा गाना किसी तेलुगु फ़िल्म का — और स्कूल के फाटक से बस तक पहुँचते-पहुँचते वह बिना जाने ही तीन बार अपनी भाषा बदल लेती है।\"","lang":"hi","body":"Their childhoods braided together. An Andaman child today might have a Bengali name, a Tamil best friend, a Malayali teacher, and a favourite Telugu film song — and switch languages three times between the school gate and the bus without noticing she has done it.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-island-of-tongues.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.island-of-tongues|h2","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","East & the Islands"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.island-of-tongues-3":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.island-of-tongues:3","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Bazaar of Many Tongues","text":"\"लेकिन इन द्वीपों में ऐसी भाषाएँ भी बसी हैं जो इन सबसे कहीं ज़्यादा पुरानी हैं — इतनी पुरानी कि शायद ही कोई चीज़ उनके जितनी पुरानी हो। अंडमान के सबसे पहले बाशिंदे — ग्रेट अंडमानी, ओंगे, जारवा, सेंटिनली — यहाँ कई हज़ार सालों से रहते आए हैं, और उनकी भाषाएँ धरती के किसी भी अन्य भाषा-परिवार से मेल नहीं खातीं। निकोबार में भी, निकोबारी और शोम्पेन लोग इसी तरह अपनी बिल्कुल अनोखी भाषाएँ बोलते हैं।\"","lang":"hi","body":"But the islands hold languages far older than any of these — older than almost anything. The first peoples of the Andamans — the Great Andamanese, the Onge, the Jarawa, the Sentinelese — have lived here for many thousands of years, and their languages belong to no other family of languages on Earth. In the Nicobars, the Nicobarese and the Shompen likewise speak languages all their own.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-island-of-tongues.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.island-of-tongues|h3","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","East & the Islands"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.island-of-tongues-4":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.island-of-tongues:4","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Bazaar of Many Tongues","text":"\"उन पुरानी आवाज़ों में से कुछ अब बहुत धीमी पड़ चुकी हैं। ग्रेट अंडमानी लोगों की कभी कई भाषाएँ हुआ करती थीं, पर आज उन्हें बोलने वाले मुट्ठी भर ही रह गए हैं, और बुज़ुर्गों ने भाषा-वैज्ञानिकों के साथ मिलकर शब्दों, गीतों और नामों को लिख कर सहेजा है ताकि जो कुछ बचा है, उसका मान रखा जा सके। जब कोई बुज़ुर्ग बोलने वाला दुनिया से जाता है, तो मानो एक पूरी लाइब्रेरी ही बंद हो जाती है। इसीलिए यह काम इतना ज़रूरी है।\"","lang":"hi","body":"Some of those ancient voices have grown very quiet. The languages of the Great Andamanese peoples, once many, now have only a handful of speakers, and elders have worked with linguists to write down words, songs and names so that what remains is kept with honour. When an old speaker dies, a whole library closes. That is why the work matters.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-island-of-tongues.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.island-of-tongues|h4","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","East & the Islands"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.island-of-tongues-5":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.island-of-tongues:5","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Bazaar of Many Tongues","text":"\"जारवा और सेंटिनेली लोग आज भी हर दिन अपनी भाषाएँ बोलते हैं, अपने जंगलों में और अपने द्वीप पर, जैसे वे हमेशा से बोलते आए हैं। बाहर का कोई भी इंसान उन भाषाओं को नहीं जानता — और ऐसा ही होना भी चाहिए। भारत उनकी ज़मीन और शांति से जीने के उनके फ़ैसले की हिफ़ाज़त करता है। यहाँ आदर का मतलब है दूरी बनाए रखना।\"","lang":"hi","body":"The Jarawa and the Sentinelese still speak their languages every day, in their own forests and on their own island, as they always have. Nobody outside knows those languages — and that is as it should be. India protects their lands and their choice to be left in peace. Respect, here, means distance.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-island-of-tongues.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.island-of-tongues|h5","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","East & the Islands"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.island-of-tongues-6":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.island-of-tongues:6","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Bazaar of Many Tongues","text":"\"पोर्ट ब्लेयर की एक अध्यापिका ने अपनी कक्षा को कुछ यूँ समझाया: \\\"हमारे द्वीपों की बोली में कई परतें हैं। सबसे नई परतें जहाज़ों से आईं, और तुम उन्हें बाज़ार में सुन सकते हो। सबसे पुरानी परतें जहाज़ों के बनने से भी पहले से हैं, और वहाँ जाना हमारा काम नहीं है। दोनों ही तुमसे बस एक चीज़ चाहती हैं — परवाह।\\\"\"","lang":"hi","body":"A schoolteacher in Port Blair puts it to her class like this: \"Our islands speak in layers. The newest layers came by ship, and you can hear them in the bazaar. The oldest layers came before ships existed, and they are not ours to visit. Both deserve the same thing from you — care.\"","art":"art/story/sm/fk-island-of-tongues.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.island-of-tongues|h6","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","East & the Islands"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.island-of-tongues-7":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.island-of-tongues:7","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Bazaar of Many Tongues","text":"\"तो बाज़ार की चहल-पहल यूँ ही चलती रहती है: बंगाली, तमिल, हिंदी, तेलुगु, मलयालम, निकोबारी, सब एक ही चमकदार मछली का मोल-भाव करते हुए। और आखिरी सड़क के पार, घने जंगल में, द्वीपों की सबसे पुरानी भाषाएँ आज भी उन्हीं लोगों के बीच गूँज रही हैं जिनकी वे हैं।\"","lang":"hi","body":"So the market hums on: Bengali, Tamil, Hindi, Telugu, Malayalam, Nicobarese, all bargaining over the same bright fish. And beyond the last road, in the deep forest, the oldest languages of the islands go on being spoken to the people they belong to.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-island-of-tongues.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.island-of-tongues|h7","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","East & the Islands"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.first-dance-0":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.first-dance:0","title":"Read it in Hindi · How the First Evening Got Its Dance","text":"\"झारखंड के संथाली लोग अपने पूरे इतिहास को गाकर सुनाते हैं, दुनिया की बिल्कुल शुरुआत से — और यह उसी कहानी के शुरुआती दिनों का एक किस्सा है, पहले पुरखों के बाद का, जब उनके बच्चों और नाती-पोतों के पास गाँव थे, खेत थे, और वह सब कुछ था जो किसी बस्ती को चाहिए होता है। लगभग सब कुछ।\"","lang":"hi","body":"The Santhals of Jharkhand sing their whole history, from the very beginning of the world — and this is one of the tellings from early in that story, after the first ancestors, when their children and grandchildren had villages, and fields, and everything a people needs. Almost everything.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-first-dance.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.first-dance|h0","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","East & the Islands"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.first-dance-1":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.first-dance:1","title":"Read it in Hindi · How the First Evening Got Its Dance","text":"क्योंकि पुरानी कहानियाँ बताती हैं कि सबसे पहले बसे गाँवों में शामें कुछ अधूरी सी होती थीं। दिन तो पूरी तरह काम से भरा रहता था — ज़मीन साफ़ करना, बीज बोना, मवेशी चराना, घर बनाना। लेकिन जब सूरज ढल जाता और काम रुक जाता, तो लोग बस यूँ ही बैठे रहते। आग चटकती रहती। कोई जम्हाई लेता। शाम में मानो एक खालीपन था, ठीक उस चीज़ की शक्ल का जिसे अभी किसी ने बनाया ही नहीं था।","lang":"hi","body":"Because in the first villages, the tellings say, the evenings were wrong. The day was full — clearing, sowing, herding, building. But when the sun went down and the work stopped, people just sat. The fire crackled. Somebody yawned. There was a hole in the evening exactly the shape of something nobody had invented yet.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-first-dance.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.first-dance|h1","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","East & the Islands"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.first-dance-2":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.first-dance:2","title":"Read it in Hindi · How the First Evening Got Its Dance","text":"पहला टुकड़ा अचानक ही हाथ लग गया। धान कूटती एक औरत के मूसल से एक ताल बन रही थी — धुम, धुम, धुम — और छत की मरम्मत कर रहे एक आदमी के हाथ भी उसी ताल पर थिरकने लगे। मूसल की आवाज़ का जवाब देने के लिए किसी ने एक खोखले तने पर चमड़ा मढ़ दिया, और बस, अचानक ढोल बन गया।","lang":"hi","body":"The first piece arrived by accident. A woman husking rice kept a rhythm with her pestle — thum, thum, thum — and a man mending a roof found his hands tapping along. Somebody stretched a skin over a hollow log to answer the pestle back, and there, suddenly, was the drum.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-first-dance.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.first-dance|h2","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","East & the Islands"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.first-dance-3":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.first-dance:3","title":"Read it in Hindi · How the First Evening Got Its Dance","text":"और जैसा कि सबको तुरंत पता चल गया, ढोल की थाप पर कोई भी शांत नहीं बैठ सकता। यह कानों से भीतर उतरती है और पैरों से बाहर फूट पड़ती है। बच्चे सबसे पहले उठ खड़े हुए — बच्चे तो हमेशा ही ऐसे होते हैं — आग की रोशनी में कूदते-फांदते हुए, बिना यह जाने कि वे क्या कर रहे हैं और रुकने का तो उनका कोई इरादा ही नहीं था।","lang":"hi","body":"And a drum, as everyone instantly discovered, does not let you sit still. It goes in at the ears and comes out at the feet. The children were up first — children always are — hopping in the firelight with no idea what they were doing and no interest in stopping.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-first-dance.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.first-dance|h3","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","East & the Islands"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.first-dance-4":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.first-dance:4","title":"Read it in Hindi · How the First Evening Got Its Dance","text":"फिर वह सवाल उठा जिसने इसे संथाली पहचान दी। बीच में अकेला नाचता हुआ एक नर्तक बड़ा प्यारा लग रहा था, पर थोड़ा अकेला भी। हर कोई उसमें शामिल होना चाहता था — लेकिन इतने सारे लोग आपस में टकराए बिना एक साथ कैसे नाचें?","lang":"hi","body":"Then came the question that made it Santhal. One dancer alone in the middle looked wonderful and a little lonely. Everyone wanted to join — but how do many people dance together without becoming a herd of collisions?","art":"art/story/sm/fk-first-dance.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.first-dance|h4","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","East & the Islands"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.first-dance-5":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.first-dance:5","title":"Read it in Hindi · How the First Evening Got Its Dance","text":"यही वह नाच है जिसे आप आज भी देख सकते हैं: नर्तकों की एक लंबी कतार, एक-दूसरे की बाँहों में बाँहें डाले, एक साथ क़दम बढ़ाते और झूमते हुए, जबकि नीचे ढोल अपनी बातें करते रहते हैं — बड़ा तमक और लंबा तुमदाक', वे दो ढोल जिनके नाम हर संथाल बच्चा जानता है। यह कतार नाच के मैदान में एक धीमी, खुशहाल नदी की तरह बलखाती चलती है।","lang":"hi","body":"That is the dance you can still see: the long line of dancers, arms linked, stepping and swaying together while the drums talk underneath — the big tamak and the long tumdak', the two drums whose names every Santhal child knows. The line curls around the dancing ground like a slow, happy river.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-first-dance.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.first-dance|h5","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","East & the Islands"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.first-dance-6":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.first-dance:6","title":"Read it in Hindi · How the First Evening Got Its Dance","text":"इस ताल में ढलने के लिए नए गीत भी बनते गए — बुआई और फ़सल कटाई के गीत, शादियों के गीत, वसंत में बाहा और फ़सल के बाद सोहराय के त्योहारों के गीत। अलग-अलग दिनों के लिए अलग-अलग नाच, हर एक के अपने क़दम और अपने गीत, मानो पूरा साल ही नाचना सीख गया हो।","lang":"hi","body":"The songs grew to fit it — songs for planting and harvest, for weddings, for the festivals of Baha in the spring and Sohrai after the harvest. Different dances for different days, each with its own step and its own songs, so the year itself learned to dance.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-first-dance.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.first-dance|h6","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","East & the Islands"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.first-dance-7":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.first-dance:7","title":"Read it in Hindi · How the First Evening Got Its Dance","text":"और शाम का खालीपन भर गया। बुज़ुर्ग कहते हैं, दिन भर पड़ोसियों के साथ मिलकर अपने हाथों से काम करो, और फिर शाम को उन्हीं हाथों में हाथ डालकर कदम से कदम मिलाओ — और जो गाँव एक कतार में नाचता है, वह मुश्किल दिनों में भी एक होकर खिंचता है।","lang":"hi","body":"And the hole in the evening was filled. Work all day with your hands beside your neighbours, the elders say, and then in the evening, link those same hands and step together — and a village that dances in one line will pull in one line too, when the hard days come.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-first-dance.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.first-dance|h7","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","East & the Islands"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.singbonga-furnaces-0":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.singbonga-furnaces:0","title":"Read it in Hindi · Sing Bonga and the Smoke That Hid the Sky","text":"झारखंड के मुंडा लोग और उनके पड़ोसी असुर — जो सदियों तक लोहा गलाने में उस्ताद थे, सचमुच के माहिर, जिनकी पुरानी भट्ठियों के टीले आज भी उस पठार पर बिखरे पड़े हैं — सृष्टि की बिल्कुल शुरुआत की एक कहानी सुनाते हैं, जो लोहे, धुएँ और खुद सूरज की है।","lang":"hi","body":"The Munda people of Jharkhand, and their neighbours the Asur — who were master iron-smelters for centuries, real ones, whose old furnace mounds still dot the plateau — tell a story from the deep beginning of things, about iron, smoke, and the sun himself.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-singbonga-furnaces.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.singbonga-furnaces|h0","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","East & the Islands"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.singbonga-furnaces-1":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.singbonga-furnaces:1","title":"Read it in Hindi · Sing Bonga and the Smoke That Hid the Sky","text":"उस कहानी में पहले-पहल लोहा गलाने वालों को एक बड़ा भेद पता चला: कि एक खास लाल मिट्टी को चूल्हे की आग से कहीं तेज़ भट्ठी में तपाने पर, उसमें से चमकता हुआ लोहा बह निकलता है। कुल्हाड़ियाँ! हल के फाल! तीरों की नोकें! यह अब तक का सबसे काम का जादू था, और उन्हें इस पर सही मायनों में गर्व था।","lang":"hi","body":"In that story the first smelters learned a mighty secret: that certain red earth, cooked in a furnace hotter than any cooking fire, weeps out shining iron. Axes! Ploughshares! Arrowheads! It was the most useful magic anyone had ever found, and they were rightly proud of it.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-singbonga-furnaces.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.singbonga-furnaces|h1","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","East & the Islands"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.singbonga-furnaces-2":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.singbonga-furnaces:2","title":"Read it in Hindi · Sing Bonga and the Smoke That Hid the Sky","text":"लेकिन घमंड आग को और हवा देता रहा। एक भट्ठी से कई भट्ठियाँ बन गईं; धौंकनियां दिन-रात साँसें भरती रहीं; और धुएँ के सलेटी खंभे उठकर पूरी दुनिया पर झुक आए, यहाँ तक कि दिन धुंधले पड़ गए, रातों में तारे न रहे, और हर हरी-भरी चीज़ खाँसने लगी।","lang":"hi","body":"But pride kept feeding the fires. One furnace became many; the bellows sighed day and night; and the smoke went up in grey pillars that leaned together over the world, until the days grew dim and the nights had no stars, and everything green began to cough.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-singbonga-furnaces.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.singbonga-furnaces|h2","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","East & the Islands"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.singbonga-furnaces-3":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.singbonga-furnaces:3","title":"Read it in Hindi · Sing Bonga and the Smoke That Hid the Sky","text":"इन सबसे ऊँचे आसमान में सिंग बोंगा थे — वे महान देवता जिन्हें मुंडा कहानियों में सूरज के रूप में पूजा जाता है, जो सब कुछ देखते हैं। उन्होंने धुएँ के पार अपनी धुंधली और मैली दुनिया को नीचे देखा, और तय किया कि कुछ भी करने से पहले, लोहा गलाने वालों से ठीक तरह से कहा जाए कि वे अपनी आग को धीमा कर लें। सो उन्होंने संदेशवाहक भेजे: परिंदों को।","lang":"hi","body":"High above it all was Sing Bonga — the great spirit whom the Munda tellings honour as the sun, the one who sees everything. He looked down through the smoke at his dimmed and dirty world, and decided that before anything else, the smelters should be asked, properly, to ease their fires. So he sent messengers: the birds.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-singbonga-furnaces.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.singbonga-furnaces|h3","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","East & the Islands"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.singbonga-furnaces-4":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.singbonga-furnaces:4","title":"Read it in Hindi · Sing Bonga and the Smoke That Hid the Sky","text":"एक-एक करके पंछी संदेश लेकर भट्टियों की ओर उड़े — और जब लौटे, तो बदले हुए थे। पुरानी कहानियाँ कहती हैं कि राजा कौआ कोयले जैसा काला झुलसकर लौटा, और बाकी पंछी धुएँ और अंगारों के निशान लेकर लौटे — और इसी वजह से आज तक वे पंछी वही रंग पहने हुए हैं।","lang":"hi","body":"One after another the birds flew down to the furnaces to carry the message — and came back changed. The tellings say the king crow came back scorched black as charcoal, and others came back marked by smoke and cinders — and that is why those birds wear those colours to this day.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-singbonga-furnaces.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.singbonga-furnaces|h4","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","East & the Islands"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.singbonga-furnaces-5":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.singbonga-furnaces:5","title":"Read it in Hindi · Sing Bonga and the Smoke That Hid the Sky","text":"इसलिए सूरज एक सीधे-सादे, धूल से सने बालक का रूप धरकर भट्टियों तक पहुँचे, वहाँ धौंकनी चलाई, और सबकी बातें सुनीं। उन्होंने लोहा गलाने वालों की होशियारी देखी और उसका सम्मान किया। उन्होंने उन लपटों को भी देखा जो कभी नहीं थमती थीं, और उस आसमान को भी जिसे वे निगलती जा रही थीं।","lang":"hi","body":"So the sun walked to the furnaces as a plain, dusty boy, and worked the bellows, and listened. He saw the cleverness of the smelters and honoured it. He also saw the fires that never once rested, and the sky they were eating.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-singbonga-furnaces.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.singbonga-furnaces|h5","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","East & the Islands"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.singbonga-furnaces-6":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.singbonga-furnaces:6","title":"Read it in Hindi · Sing Bonga and the Smoke That Hid the Sky","text":"फिर उन्होंने अपना असली रूप दिखाया — और इस सौम्य कहानी में, उनका वो तेज ही अपनी बात मनवाने के लिए काफ़ी था। \"तुम्हारा लोहा अच्छा है,\" उन्होंने कहा। \"पर तुम्हारा यूँ कभी न रुकना ठीक नहीं। मैं भी तो हर एक शाम ढलता हूँ। आग ज़रूर जले — पर उसे विश्राम भी मिलना चाहिए, वरना यह आसमान मेरी रोशनी की जगह तुम्हारे धुएँ का होकर रह जाएगा।\" और फिर भट्टियों ने रात को सोना सीख लिया, और आसमान में तारे लौट आए।","lang":"hi","body":"Then he revealed himself — and in this gentle telling, the blaze of him was argument enough. \"Your iron is good,\" he said. \"Your never-stopping is not. Even I set, every single evening. The fires may burn — but they must also rest, or the sky belongs to your smoke instead of my light.\" And the furnaces learned to sleep at night, and the stars came back.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-singbonga-furnaces.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.singbonga-furnaces|h6","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","East & the Islands"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.singbonga-furnaces-7":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.singbonga-furnaces:7","title":"Read it in Hindi · Sing Bonga and the Smoke That Hid the Sky","text":"इस कहानी के पुराने रूपों में लोहा गलाने वालों का अंजाम कहीं ज़्यादा कठोर होता है — नीचे दिया गया संदर्भ यह साफ़-साफ़ बताता है — पर हर कहानी का ढाँचा वही रहता है: वह धुआँ, वे झुलसे हुए पंछी जो आज भी अपने निशान लिए फिरते हैं, और खुद सूरज, जो कोई भी कदम उठाने से पहले खुद नीचे उतरकर आए।","lang":"hi","body":"The old tellings of this story end far more harshly for the smelters — the source below says so honestly — but every version keeps the same bones: the smoke, the singed birds who still wear their marks, and the sun who came down himself before he acted.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-singbonga-furnaces.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.singbonga-furnaces|h7","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","East & the Islands"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.sal-grove-promise-0":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.sal-grove-promise:0","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Grove the Axes Never Touch","text":"झारखंड से होकर गुज़रिए तो आपको यह बार-बार दिखाई देगा: खुले खेत, मकान, सड़कें — और फिर किसी गाँव के पास, लंबे और पुराने पेड़ों का एक अछूता सा टुकड़ा, गहरा हरा और शांत, मानो इस पुरानी दुनिया का ही कोई हिस्सा हो। यही है वह पवित्र उपवन — जिसे उरांव और मुंडा लोग सरना कहते हैं, और संथाल लोग जाहेर कहते हैं।","lang":"hi","body":"Drive through Jharkhand and you will see it again and again: open fields, houses, roads — and then, beside a village, a patch of tall old forest standing untouched, dark green and quiet, like a piece of the original world. That is the sacred grove — the sarna, as the Oraon and Munda say; the jaher, as the Santhals say.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-sal-grove-promise.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.sal-grove-promise|h0","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","East & the Islands"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.sal-grove-promise-1":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.sal-grove-promise:1","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Grove the Axes Never Touch","text":"ये कहानियाँ उस दौर की हैं जब पहले-पहल खेत बने थे। खेती करने के लिए ज़मीन साफ़ करनी ही होती है; तो शुरुआती परिवारों ने पेड़ काटे, जलाए और हल चलाए। एक-एक पेड़ करके जंगल पीछे हटता गया, और जहाँ कभी जंगल खड़ा था, वहाँ गाँव बसते चले गए।","lang":"hi","body":"The tellings go back to when the first fields were made. To farm, you must clear; the first families cut and burned and ploughed, and the forest gave ground, tree by tree, and the villages rose where it had stood.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-sal-grove-promise.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.sal-grove-promise|h1","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","East & the Islands"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.sal-grove-promise-2":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.sal-grove-promise:2","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Grove the Axes Never Touch","text":"लेकिन हर नए गाँव के किनारे, बड़ों ने कुल्हाड़ियों को रोक दिया। साल के बड़े-बड़े तनों पर हाथ रखते हुए उन्होंने कहा, \"पेड़ों के इस हिस्से को नहीं। इसे हम पूरा का पूरा बचाकर रखेंगे। जंगल ने हमें सब कुछ दिया है — हमारे खेत उसी का शरीर थे। जो इंसान सब कुछ ले लेता है और कुछ भी नहीं बचाता, वह भूल जाता है कि उसे पाला-पोसा किसने था।\"","lang":"hi","body":"But at the edge of each new village, the elders stopped the axes. \"Not this stand,\" they said, resting a hand on the great sal trunks. \"This one we keep whole. The forest has given us everything — our fields were its body. A person who takes everything and keeps nothing back has forgotten who fed them.\"","art":"art/story/sm/fk-sal-grove-promise.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.sal-grove-promise|h2","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","East & the Islands"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.sal-grove-promise-3":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.sal-grove-promise:3","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Grove the Axes Never Touch","text":"तो इस तरह ये कुंज आज भी खड़े हैं। साल के पेड़ों के नीचे गाँव अपने सबसे ख़ास दिन मनाता है — बसंत के सरहुल और बाहा त्योहार ढोल-नगाड़ों और फूलों के साथ सबसे पहले इसी कुंज में आते हैं, और गाँव के पुजारी, पाहन, वहाँ पूरे समाज की तरफ़ से प्रार्थना करते हैं। यह कुंज कोई सिर्फ़ देखने का नज़ारा नहीं है। यह एक ठिकाना है: जहाँ गाँव और यह जीती-जागती धरती आपस में बात करते हैं।","lang":"hi","body":"So the groves stand. Under the sal trees the village holds its most important days — the Sarhul and Baha festivals of spring come to the grove first, with drums and flowers, and the village priest, the pahan, speaks there for the whole community. The grove is not scenery. It is an address: it is where the village and the living land talk.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-sal-grove-promise.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.sal-grove-promise|h3","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","East & the Islands"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.sal-grove-promise-4":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.sal-grove-promise:4","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Grove the Axes Never Touch","text":"यही सरना परंपरा का दिल है — झारखंड के कई आदिवासी समुदायों की आस्था, जो एक महान शक्ति और कुंज, पहाड़ व नदी-नालों की शक्तियों का आदर करते हैं, और जो आपसे सीधे-सीधे कहेंगे: हमारे मंदिर की छत पत्तों की है। यह एक जीती-जागती आस्था है, जिसे आज लाखों लोग मानते हैं, और ये कुंज उनके पवित्र तीर्थ हैं।","lang":"hi","body":"This is the heart of the Sarna way — the faith of many Adivasi communities of Jharkhand, who honour a single great spirit and the spirits of grove, hill and stream, and who will tell you plainly: our temple has a roof of leaves. It is a living faith, held today by millions, and the groves are its holy places.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-sal-grove-promise.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.sal-grove-promise|h4","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","East & the Islands"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.sal-grove-promise-5":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.sal-grove-promise:5","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Grove the Axes Never Touch","text":"और वह वादा दोगुना समझदारी भरा साबित हुआ। इन पवित्र कुंजों का अध्ययन करने वाले वैज्ञानिक बार-बार यही पाते हैं: जब आसपास हर जगह से सब कुछ ख़त्म हो गया, तब भी पुराने पेड़, दवाइयों के पौधे, चिड़ियाँ, मधुमक्खियाँ और ठंडे झरने इन्हीं कुंजों में बचे रहे। निभाए गए वादे ने बीजों को बचाए रखा। वह धन्यवाद असल में बीजों का एक खज़ाना बन गया।","lang":"hi","body":"And the promise turned out to be wise twice over. Scientists who study the sacred groves keep finding the same thing: the old trees, the medicine plants, the birds and bees and cool springs survive in the groves when they have vanished everywhere around. The kept promise kept the seeds. The thank-you turned out to be a seed-bank.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-sal-grove-promise.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.sal-grove-promise|h5","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","East & the Islands"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.sal-grove-promise-6":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.sal-grove-promise:6","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Grove the Axes Never Touch","text":"बुज़ुर्ग कहते हैं कि साल का पेड़ साल भर देता है — पत्तलों के लिए पत्ते, दीयों और पूजा की धूनी के लिए राल, बसंत में फूल, और मई की तपती धूप में छाँव। वह बस वही माँगता है जो हर जीव माँगता है: मेरा आख़िरी हिस्सा भी मत छीन लेना।","lang":"hi","body":"A sal tree, the elders say, gives all year — leaves for plates, resin for lamps and blessing-smoke, flowers in spring, shade in the terrible May sun. All it asks is what everything asks: do not take the last of me.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-sal-grove-promise.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.sal-grove-promise|h6","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","East & the Islands"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.karam-brothers-0":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.karam-brothers:0","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Branch the Brothers Brought Home","text":"\"हर साल, जब बारिश धान की फसल को पका रही होती है, झारखंड के गांवों में करम का त्योहार मनाया जाता है। गीतों और ढोल-नगाड़ों के साथ करम के पेड़ की एक डाली घर लाई जाती है, उसे पूरे आदर के साथ आंगन में रोपा जाता है, और रात भर उसके चारों ओर नाच-गाना होता है। यह त्योहार वही कहानी कहता है — कर्मा और धर्मा नाम के दो भाइयों की कहानी।\"","lang":"hi","body":"Every year, when the rains are ripening the rice, the villages of Jharkhand keep the festival of Karam. A branch of the karam tree is carried home with songs and drums, planted with honour in the courtyard, and danced around all night. This is the story the festival tells — the story of Karma and Dharma, the two brothers.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-karam-brothers.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.karam-brothers|h0","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","East & the Islands"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.karam-brothers-1":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.karam-brothers:1","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Branch the Brothers Brought Home","text":"\"कर्मा और धर्मा किसान थे, और उनकी किस्मत के चर्चे दूर-दूर तक थे। उनके धान के पौधे सबसे लंबे होते, उनके मवेशी चमकते रहते, और उनके अनाज के भंडार के लिए एक बड़े दरवाजे की ज़रूरत पड़ गई थी। और हर साल, फसल पकने के समय, उनका परिवार अपनी माँ के सिखाए तरीके से रात भर गीतों के साथ करम की डाली का आदर करता था — यही उनकी किस्मत की जड़ थी, हालांकि दोनों भाई इसे लगभग भूल ही चुके थे।\"","lang":"hi","body":"Karma and Dharma were farmers, and their luck was famous. Their rice stood taller, their cattle shone, their granary needed a bigger door. And every year, at the ripening time, their household honoured the karam branch with songs, all night, the way their mother had taught them — that was the root of the luck, though the brothers had half forgotten it.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-karam-brothers.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.karam-brothers|h1","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","East & the Islands"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.karam-brothers-2":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.karam-brothers:2","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Branch the Brothers Brought Home","text":"\"फिर एक ऐसा साल आया जब बहुत काम था। व्यापार खूब चला, भाई अमीर हो गए और भाग-दौड़ में लगे रहे, और जब त्योहार का समय आया, तो उनके पास फुर्सत ही नहीं थी। दूसरे आंगनों में ढोल बजते रहे। उनके आंगन में सन्नाटा था — और कुछ कहानियों में तो यह भी कहा जाता है कि वे उस पवित्र डाली को सिर्फ भूले ही नहीं, बल्कि हड़बड़ी में उसे ठोकर मारकर एक तरफ कर दिया, जो कि और भी बुरा था।\"","lang":"hi","body":"Then came a busy year. Trade was good, the brothers were rich and rushing, and when the festival came round, they had no time. The drums played in other courtyards. In theirs, nothing — and in some tellings the sacred branch was not just forgotten but knocked aside in the hurry, which is worse.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-karam-brothers.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.karam-brothers|h2","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","East & the Islands"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.karam-brothers-3":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.karam-brothers:3","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Branch the Brothers Brought Home","text":"\"और किस्मत उनका साथ छोड़कर चली गई। चुपचाप, पूरी तरह से, ठीक वैसे ही जैसे कोई मेहमान उस घर से चला जाता है जहाँ कोई उसका स्वागत नहीं करता। धान में बीमारी लग गई, मवेशी भटक गए, अनाज का भंडार खाली हो गया, और साल भर के अंदर ही वे मशहूर भाई गरीब होकर एक खाली मेज़ के आमने-सामने बैठकर एक-दूसरे को ताकने लगे।\"","lang":"hi","body":"And the luck left. Quietly, completely, the way a guest leaves a house where no one greets her. The rice sickened, the cattle strayed, the granary emptied, and within the year the famous brothers were poor men staring at each other across a bare table.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-karam-brothers.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.karam-brothers|h3","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","East & the Islands"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.karam-brothers-4":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.karam-brothers:4","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Branch the Brothers Brought Home","text":"\"उन्होंने एक बुज़ुर्ग से पूछा कि उनसे क्या नियम टूटा है। \\\"आप जानते हैं कि आपने क्या तोड़ा है,\\\" उन्होंने कहा। \\\"सवाल यह है कि अब आप इसके बारे में क्या करेंगे?\\\"\"","lang":"hi","body":"They asked an elder what they had broken. \"You know what you have broken,\" she said. \"The question is what you will do about it.\"","art":"art/story/sm/fk-karam-brothers.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.karam-brothers|h4","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","East & the Islands"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.karam-brothers-5":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.karam-brothers:5","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Branch the Brothers Brought Home","text":"तो दोनों भाई चल पड़े। पुरानी कहानियाँ बताती हैं कि वे बहुत दूर तक गए — नदियाँ पार कीं, जंगलों से गुज़रे, और जो कोई भी मिला उससे पूछते रहे कि करम देवता कहाँ मिलेंगे। और इस तलाश ने ही उन्हें बदलना शुरू कर दिया: जिन दो लोगों के पास किसी चीज़ के लिए फ़ुर्सत नहीं थी, अब उनके पास हर बात के लिए समय था। रास्ते में जो भी मिला, उन्होंने उसकी मदद की, क्योंकि आख़िरकार वे समझ चुके थे कि मदद की ज़रूरत होना कैसा लगता है।","lang":"hi","body":"So the brothers walked. The tellings send them far — across rivers, through forests, asking everyone they met where the spirit of the karam might be found. And the search itself began to change them: two men who had had no time for anything now had time for everything, and helped whoever they met on the road, because they finally knew how it felt to need help.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-karam-brothers.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.karam-brothers|h5","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","East & the Islands"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.karam-brothers-6":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.karam-brothers:6","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Branch the Brothers Brought Home","text":"आख़िरकार, पानी के किनारे उन्हें करम का पेड़ मिल ही गया — और उन्होंने सच्चे मन से उससे माफ़ी माँगी, ठीक वैसे ही जैसे सचमुच पछतावा होने पर माँगी जाती है। फिर पूरे आदर के साथ उन्होंने एक डाली काटी और उसे ऊँचा उठाए घर की ओर चल पड़े। रास्ते भर वे वही गीत गाते रहे जो उनकी माँ ने उन्हें सिखाए थे, एक-एक बोल, पूरे रास्ते।","lang":"hi","body":"At last, by the water, they found the karam — and they asked its forgiveness, plainly, the way you ask when you mean it. And they cut one branch with honour, and carried it home high, singing the songs their mother had taught them, every verse, the whole way back.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-karam-brothers.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.karam-brothers|h6","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","East & the Islands"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.karam-brothers-7":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.karam-brothers:7","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Branch the Brothers Brought Home","text":"उन्होंने वह डाली अपने आँगन में रोप दी, और घर के सभी लोग रात भर उसके चारों ओर नाचे — और क़िस्मत भी उसी तरह घर लौट आई जैसे वह डाली आई थी: सिर-आँखों पर उठाकर, पूरे आदर के साथ, गीतों की धुन पर। खेत फिर से हरे-भरे हो गए। भाई फिर कभी यह बात नहीं भूले। जो भी एक डाली के लिए इतनी दूर चलकर गया हो, वह कभी भूलता नहीं।","lang":"hi","body":"They planted the branch in their courtyard, and the household danced around it all night — and the luck came home the way the branch had: carried, honoured, sung to. The fields recovered. The brothers did not forget again. Nobody who has walked that far for a branch forgets again.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-karam-brothers.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.karam-brothers|h7","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","East & the Islands"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.bamboo-bonga-0":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.bamboo-bonga:0","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Elephant and the Keeper of the Bamboo","text":"संथालों की भाषा में कहें, तो यह जीती-जागती दुनिया बोंगाओं से भरी है — यानी हर जगह की अपनी आत्मा: पहाड़ का बोंगा, झरने का बोंगा, चौराहे वाले पुराने पेड़ का बोंगा। जिस जगह पर बोंगा होता है, वह सिर्फ़ कोई बेजान चीज़ नहीं होती, बल्कि कोई जीता-जागता स्वरूप होती है। और यहीं से बात आती है उस हाथी की, और गाँव के ऊपर वाले बाँस के झुरमुट की।","lang":"hi","body":"In the Santhal way of speaking, the living world is full of bongas — the spirits of places: a spirit of the hill, of the stream, of the old tree at the crossing. A place with a bonga is a place that is somebody, not just something. Which brings us to the elephant, and the bamboo grove above the village.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-bamboo-bonga.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.bamboo-bonga|h0","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","East & the Islands"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.bamboo-bonga-1":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.bamboo-bonga:1","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Elephant and the Keeper of the Bamboo","text":"हर सर्दी में, जब जंगल में खाने की कमी हो जाती, तो वह हाथी पहाड़ी चढ़कर बाँस के बड़े झुरमुट के पास आता और भरपेट खाता। उस झुरमुट में हमेशा काफ़ी कुछ होता था: किनारों पर हरे-हरे बाँस और नरम ज़मीन में मीठी-मीठी कोपलें। वह खाता, हवा में ही कहीं हल्की घुरघुराहट के साथ धन्यवाद करता, और आराम से टहलता हुआ चला जाता। उसकी पूरी ज़िंदगी बस ऐसे ही चलती आई थी।","lang":"hi","body":"Every winter, when the forest grew lean, the elephant came up the hill to the great bamboo grove and ate. The grove always had enough: green canes at the edges, sweet shoots in the softer ground. He ate, rumbled his thanks in the general direction of nothing, and ambled off. It had worked this way his whole life.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-bamboo-bonga.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.bamboo-bonga|h1","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","East & the Islands"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.bamboo-bonga-2":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.bamboo-bonga:2","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Elephant and the Keeper of the Bamboo","text":"लेकिन यह सर्दी बाकी सर्दियों से ज़्यादा भूख भरी थी, और बाँस के उस झुरमुट के बीच खड़े हाथी के मन में एक बड़ा सा विचार आया: सिर्फ़ किनारों से थोड़ा-थोड़ा क्यों चबाना? वह तो एक ही दोपहर में पूरे जंगल को गिरा सकता था और हफ़्ते भर दावत उड़ा सकता था — बाँस के भीतरी नरम हिस्से, नई कोपलें, सब कुछ, एक साथ।","lang":"hi","body":"But this winter was hungrier than most, and standing in the middle of all that bamboo, the elephant had a big grey thought: why nibble at the edges? He could push the whole grove flat in an afternoon and feast for a week — the hearts of the clumps, the young shoots, everything, all at once.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-bamboo-bonga.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.bamboo-bonga|h2","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","East & the Islands"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.bamboo-bonga-3":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.bamboo-bonga:3","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Elephant and the Keeper of the Bamboo","text":"उसने पहले बड़े झुरमुट पर अपनी सूँड लपेटी ही थी कि जंगल बोल पड़ा। ज़ोर से नहीं। बोंगाओं को कभी-कभार ही ज़ोर से बोलने की ज़रूरत पड़ती है। वह बाँसों के बीच से बहती हवा जैसी आवाज़ थी, जो हर तरफ़ से आ रही थी और कहीं से भी नहीं: \"सर्दियों के मेहमान। खींचने से पहले — एक सवाल।\"","lang":"hi","body":"He had wrapped his trunk around the first great clump when the grove spoke. Not loudly. Bongas rarely need to be loud. It was a voice like wind through canes, coming from everywhere and nowhere: \"Winter guest. Before you pull — a question.\"","art":"art/story/sm/fk-bamboo-bonga.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.bamboo-bonga|h3","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","East & the Islands"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.bamboo-bonga-4":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.bamboo-bonga:4","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Elephant and the Keeper of the Bamboo","text":"\"तुमने अपनी ज़िंदगी की हर सर्दी यहीं खाया है,\" जंगल के रखवाले ने कहा। \"पिछली सर्दी तुम्हें किसने खिलाया?\" \"इसी जंगल ने,\" हाथी ने कहा। \"और उससे पिछली सर्दी?\" \"इसी जंगल ने।\" \"और अगली सर्दी तुम्हें कौन खिलाएगा?\" हाथी का मुँह खुला का खुला रह गया, और वह सूँड हवा में उठाए, वहीं खड़ा हिसाब लगाने लगा।","lang":"hi","body":"\"You have eaten here every winter of your life,\" said the keeper of the grove. \"Who fed you last winter?\" \"This grove,\" said the elephant. \"And the winter before?\" \"This grove.\" \"And who will feed you NEXT winter?\" The elephant opened his mouth, and stood there, trunk in the air, doing the arithmetic.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-bamboo-bonga.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.bamboo-bonga|h4","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","East & the Islands"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.bamboo-bonga-5":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.bamboo-bonga:5","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Elephant and the Keeper of the Bamboo","text":"\"...यही जंगल,\" उसने आख़िरकार बहुत धीमे से कहा। \"अगर यह बचा रहा तो।\" उसने बाँस के झुरमुट को छोड़ दिया। वह झूलकर वापस सीधा खड़ा हो गया, और पूरा जंगल सरसरा उठा — राहत से, या हँसी से; बाँसों में यह फ़र्क समझना मुश्किल होता है।","lang":"hi","body":"\"...This grove,\" he said at last, very quietly. \"If there is one.\" He let go of the clump. It swayed back upright, and the whole grove rustled — with relief, or laughter; with bamboo it is hard to tell the difference.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-bamboo-bonga.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.bamboo-bonga|h5","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","East & the Islands"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.bamboo-bonga-6":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.bamboo-bonga:6","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Elephant and the Keeper of the Bamboo","text":"\"तो फिर सुनो मेहमान, इस जंगल का नियम,\" बोंगा ने कहा। \"किनारों से खाओ, जहाँ मैं फिर से उगता हूँ। भीतरी हिस्से छोड़ दो, जहाँ मैं रहता हूँ। पेट भर खाओ और मुझे खड़ा रहने दो — और मैं तुम्हें, तुम्हारे बच्चों को, और उनके बच्चों को हर सर्दी खिलाऊँगा, जब तक कि हाथी यहाँ का रास्ता न भूल जाएँ। यह एक शोर भरी दोपहर से कहीं बेहतर सौदा है।\"","lang":"hi","body":"\"Then here is the grove's law, guest,\" said the bonga. \"Take from the edges, where I grow back. Leave the hearts, where I live. Eat your fill and leave me standing — and I will feed you, and your calves, and their calves, every winter until elephants forget the way here. That is a better bargain than one loud afternoon.\"","art":"art/story/sm/fk-bamboo-bonga.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.bamboo-bonga|h6","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","East & the Islands"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.bamboo-bonga-7":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.bamboo-bonga:7","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Elephant and the Keeper of the Bamboo","text":"हाथी ने किनारों से खाया — कहना पड़ेगा, बहुत सारा खाया; नियम ने पेट भर खाने को कहा था, और उसने छककर खाया। फिर उसने सबसे पुराने बाँस को अपनी सूँड से हौले से छुआ, जैसे बड़ों के पाँव छूते हैं, और पहाड़ी से नीचे लौट गया। और अगली सर्दी वह जंगल वहीं था। और उससे अगली सर्दी भी। और उससे अगली भी।","lang":"hi","body":"The elephant ate from the edges — a very large amount, it must be said; the law says fill, and he filled. Then he touched the oldest cane gently with his trunk, the way you touch an elder's feet, and went back down the hill. And the next winter the grove was there. And the next. And the next.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-bamboo-bonga.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.bamboo-bonga|h7","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","East & the Islands"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.sarhul-flowers-0":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.sarhul-flowers:0","title":"Read it in Hindi · When the Sal Trees Bloom","text":"\"हर बसंत, झारखण्ड के साल के जंगल चुपचाप एक अनोखा कमाल दिखाते हैं: उन विशाल पेड़ों पर फूल खिल उठते हैं — लाखों की तादाद में छोटे-छोटे, हल्के मलाई जैसे रंग के फूल, और शहद जैसी मीठी महक जो मीलों दूर तक फैल जाती है। और जब साल खिल उठता है, तब आदिवासियों का नया साल आ जाता है। इस त्योहार को सरहुल कहते हैं: साल के पेड़ों की पूजा।\"","lang":"hi","body":"Every spring, the sal forests of Jharkhand do something quietly spectacular: the great trees flower — small, cream-pale blossoms by the million, and a honeyed scent that drifts for miles. And when the sal blooms, the Adivasi new year has arrived. The festival is called Sarhul: the worship of the sal.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-sarhul-flowers.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.sarhul-flowers|h0","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","East & the Islands"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.sarhul-flowers-1":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.sarhul-flowers:1","title":"Read it in Hindi · When the Sal Trees Bloom","text":"\"इस पठार के कई समुदाय इसे अपने-अपने ढंग से मनाते हैं — उराँव, मुंडा, हो और दूसरे लोग सरहुल मनाते हैं, और संताल लोग फूलों के खिलने के इसी मौसम में अपना फूलों का त्योहार, बाहा, मनाते हैं। अलग-अलग गीत, अलग-अलग कदम, पर बात एक ही: नया साल तभी शुरू होता है जब पेड़ कहते हैं।\"","lang":"hi","body":"It is kept, in their own ways, by many peoples of the plateau — the Oraon, the Munda, the Ho and others keep Sarhul, and the Santhals keep their own flower festival, Baha, in the same blossoming season. Different songs, different steps, one shared idea: the year begins when the trees say so.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-sarhul-flowers.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.sarhul-flowers|h1","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","East & the Islands"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.sarhul-flowers-2":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.sarhul-flowers:2","title":"Read it in Hindi · When the Sal Trees Bloom","text":"त्योहार सबसे पहले पवित्र उपवन में जाता है। गाँव के पुजारी — पाहन — वहाँ सबकी तरफ से पूजा-अनुष्ठान करते हैं, अच्छी बारिश और अच्छे साल के लिए भेंट चढ़ाते हैं और प्रार्थना करते हैं; कई गाँवों में पाहन पानी के बर्तनों से संकेत पढ़ते हैं, और पूरा गाँव सुनता है कि पानी मानसून के बारे में क्या भरोसा दिला रहा है।","lang":"hi","body":"The festival goes to the sacred grove first. The village priest — the pahan — keeps the rites there on behalf of everyone, with offerings and prayers for good rains and a good year; in many villages the pahan reads the signs from vessels of water, and the village listens to what the water promises about the monsoon.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-sarhul-flowers.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.sarhul-flowers|h2","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","East & the Islands"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.sarhul-flowers-3":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.sarhul-flowers:3","title":"Read it in Hindi · When the Sal Trees Bloom","text":"फिर उपवन का आशीर्वाद घर आता है। उपवन से साल के फूल लाए जाते हैं और दरवाज़ों व घरों में आदर के साथ रखे जाते हैं — पुजारी और बुज़ुर्ग हर परिवार तक फूल पहुँचाते हैं, ताकि गाँव की हर छत जंगल के बसंत का एक हिस्सा पहन सके। नगाड़े बजने लगते हैं। नाचने वालों की कतारें बन जाती हैं। यह सब देर रात तक चलता रहता है, और किसी को भी इसे रोकने की कोई जल्दी नहीं होती।","lang":"hi","body":"Then the grove's blessing comes home. Sal blossoms are carried from the grove and set with honour on doorways and in houses — the priest and elders bringing flowers to every family, so that every roof in the village wears a piece of the forest's spring. Drums begin. Lines of dancers form. It goes on into the night, and nobody is in a hurry for it to stop.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-sarhul-flowers.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.sarhul-flowers|h3","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","East & the Islands"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.sarhul-flowers-4":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.sarhul-flowers:4","title":"Read it in Hindi · When the Sal Trees Bloom","text":"सरहुल में एक ऐसा रिवाज़ है जिस पर ठहरकर सोचने की ज़रूरत है। जब तक यह त्योहार मना नहीं लिया जाता — जब तक धन्यवाद नहीं कह दिया जाता — तब तक कई परिवार नए मौसम के जंगल के पहले फल और फूल नहीं खाते।","lang":"hi","body":"There is one custom inside Sarhul worth thinking about slowly. Until the festival is kept — until thanks are given — many families will not eat the new season's first fruits and flowers of the forest.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-sarhul-flowers.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.sarhul-flowers|h4","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","East & the Islands"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.sarhul-flowers-5":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.sarhul-flowers:5","title":"Read it in Hindi · When the Sal Trees Bloom","text":"राँची में, सरहुल शहर के सबसे शानदार नज़ारों में से एक बन चुका है: हर मोहल्ले से निकलती शोभायात्राएँ, लाल पाड़ वाली सफ़ेद साड़ियों में नर्तकों और ढोल बजाने वालों का सैलाब, हर तरफ साल के फूल, और गाती-गुनगुनाती चलती पूरी राजधानी। स्कूल बंद रहते हैं। यह पठार अपना ही उत्सव मनाता है।","lang":"hi","body":"In Ranchi, Sarhul has grown into one of the great sights of the city: processions from every neighbourhood, rivers of dancers and drummers in white saris bordered with red, sal blossoms everywhere, the whole capital walking and singing. Schools close. The plateau celebrates itself.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-sarhul-flowers.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.sarhul-flowers|h5","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","East & the Islands"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.sarhul-flowers-6":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.sarhul-flowers:6","title":"Read it in Hindi · When the Sal Trees Bloom","text":"और इन सबके बीच खड़े हैं वे पेड़ जिनसे यह सब शुरू हुआ — साल, इस पठार का पेड़, जो पत्तल, राल, छाँव, लकड़ी और इस एक हफ़्ते की महक देता है। अपने दिल में यह त्योहार पूरे समुदाय का जंगल की ओर मुड़कर, बाकायदा नगाड़ों के साथ यह कहने जैसा है: हमने आपकी देन को देखा। शुक्रिया। इस साल फिर से।","lang":"hi","body":"And through it all stand the trees that started it — the sal, the tree of the plateau, giver of leaf-plates and resin and shade and timber and this one week of perfume. The festival is, at its heart, a whole people turning to a forest and saying, formally and with drums: we noticed. Thank you. Again this year.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-sarhul-flowers.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.sarhul-flowers|h6","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","East & the Islands"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.boita-bandana-0":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.boita-bandana:0","title":"Read it in Hindi · Little Boats for the Big Sailors","text":"कार्तिक पूर्णिमा की सुबह अभी अंधेरा ही है — पवित्र कार्तिक महीने की पूर्णिमा — और पूरे ओडिशा में परिवार पानी की ओर जा रहे हैं। नदियाँ, कुंड, तालाब, और पुरी में खुद समंदर: जहाँ-जहाँ पानी है, वहाँ नींद से भरे बच्चे अपने सबसे अच्छे कपड़े पहने, बड़ी सावधानी से छोटी-छोटी नावें ले जा रहे हैं।","lang":"hi","body":"It is still dark on the morning of Kartika Purnima — the full moon of the holy month of Kartika — and all over Odisha, families are walking to water. Rivers, tanks, ponds, the sea itself at Puri: wherever there is water, there are sleepy children in their best clothes, carefully carrying little boats.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-boita-bandana.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.boita-bandana|h0","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","East & the Islands"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.boita-bandana-1":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.boita-bandana:1","title":"Read it in Hindi · Little Boats for the Big Sailors","text":"ये नावें केले के तने, छाल और रंग-बिरंगे कागज़ से बनी हैं, और हर नाव को किसी असली जहाज़ के छोटे रूप की तरह सजाया गया है: एक दीया, पान के पत्ते, फूल और एक सिक्का। भोर की पहली किरण फूटते ही, हर परिवार अपनी नन्हीं नाव को जलते हुए दीये के साथ पानी में उतारता है — और अचानक पूरी काली नदी बहते हुए तारों का बेड़ा बन जाती है।","lang":"hi","body":"The boats are made of banana stem and bark and coloured paper, and each one is loaded like a real ship in miniature: a lamp, betel leaves, flowers, a coin. At first light, each family sets its little boat on the water, lamp burning — and suddenly the whole dark river is a fleet of drifting stars.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-boita-bandana.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.boita-bandana|h1","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","East & the Islands"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.boita-bandana-2":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.boita-bandana:2","title":"Read it in Hindi · Little Boats for the Big Sailors","text":"जैसे ही नावें आगे बढ़ती हैं, सब मिलकर वही पुराना जयकारा लगाते हैं — \"आ का मा बोई!\" — यह इतनी पुरानी पुकार है कि इसमें समुद्री यात्रा के महीनों के ही नाम आते हैं; किसी ओड़िया परिवार से कहिए कि वे आपको इसे ठीक से बोलकर सुनाएँ। इस परंपरा को बोइता बंदाणा कहते हैं: नावों का वंदन। लेकिन कौन-सी नावें?","lang":"hi","body":"As the boats go out, everyone says the old cry together — \"Aa ka ma boi!\" — a counting-call so ancient that it names the sailing months themselves; ask an Odia family to say it for you properly. The custom is called Boita Bandana: the honouring of the boats. But which boats?","art":"art/story/sm/fk-boita-bandana.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.boita-bandana|h2","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","East & the Islands"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.boita-bandana-3":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.boita-bandana:3","title":"Read it in Hindi · Little Boats for the Big Sailors","text":"वे विशाल नावें। कई सदियों पहले, ओडिशा — जिसे उन दिनों कलिंग कहा जाता था — भारत के महान समुद्री क्षेत्रों में से एक था। वहाँ के व्यापारी, जिन्हें साधब कहा जाता था, 'बोइत' नाम के ऊँचे-ऊँचे जहाज़ बनाते थे, और जब बारिश के बाद हवाओं का रुख बदलता, तो पूरे के पूरे जहाज़ी बेड़े बंगाल की खाड़ी के पार निकल पड़ते थे — श्रीलंका, बर्मा, और सुदूर बाली, जावा और सुमात्रा के द्वीपों तक।","lang":"hi","body":"The huge ones. Many centuries ago, Odisha — Kalinga, in those days — was one of the great seafaring lands of India. Its merchants, the sadhabas, built tall ships called boitas, and when the winds turned after the rains, whole fleets set out across the Bay of Bengal — to Sri Lanka, to Burma, and all the way to the islands of Bali, Java and Sumatra.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-boita-bandana.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.boita-bandana|h3","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","East & the Islands"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.boita-bandana-4":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.boita-bandana:4","title":"Read it in Hindi · Little Boats for the Big Sailors","text":"ज़रा सोचिए, किनारे पर रह गए परिवारों के लिए उस यात्रा का क्या मतलब होता होगा। न कोई फ़ोन, न कोई भरोसेमंद नक्शा, महीनों तक कोई ख़बर नहीं — बस जाते समय मॉनसून की हवाएँ और, अगर सब ठीक रहा, तो लौटते समय भी मॉनसून की ही हवाएँ।","lang":"hi","body":"Think what a sailing like that meant for the families on the shore. No phones, no maps you could trust, no news for months — just the monsoon winds out and, if all went well, the monsoon winds home.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-boita-bandana.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.boita-bandana|h4","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","East & the Islands"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.boita-bandana-5":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.boita-bandana:5","title":"Read it in Hindi · Little Boats for the Big Sailors","text":"यह व्यापार दोनों तरफ़ से चला और उसने दोनों ओर अपनी छाप छोड़ी। आज भी, इंडोनेशिया में पाँच हज़ार किलोमीटर दूर बाली द्वीप पर कलिंग से अपने पुराने रिश्तों की याद में एक त्योहार मनाया जाता है, और ओड़िया व बाली के विद्वान दूर के रिश्तेदारों की तरह एक-दूसरे के उत्सवों में जाकर खानदानी ऐल्बम साझा करते हैं। समुद्र के इस रास्ते को दोनों किनारों पर याद रखा गया है।","lang":"hi","body":"The trade went both ways and left traces both ways. To this day, Bali — five thousand kilometres away in Indonesia — keeps its own festival remembering the old links with Kalinga, and Odia and Balinese scholars visit each other's festivals like distant cousins comparing family albums. The sea road is remembered at both ends.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-boita-bandana.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.boita-bandana|h5","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","East & the Islands"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.boita-bandana-6":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.boita-bandana:6","title":"Read it in Hindi · Little Boats for the Big Sailors","text":"और कटक में, महानदी के रेतीले तट पर, ये नन्हीं नावें एक बहुत बड़े मेले की शुरुआत करती हैं: बाली जात्रा — जिसका सीधा अर्थ है \"बाली की यात्रा\" — जो भारत के सबसे बड़े खुले मेलों में से एक है। कई दिनों तक वहाँ दुकानें, झूले, खिलौने और खाने-पीने के ढेरों पकवान होते हैं, नदी किनारे उत्सव का एक पूरा शहर ही बस जाता है, और इस सबका नाम एक समुद्री यात्रा पर रखा गया है।","lang":"hi","body":"And in Cuttack, on the sands of the Mahanadi river, the little boats launch a giant fair: Bali Jatra — literally \"the journey to Bali\" — one of the biggest open-air fairs in India. For days there are stalls and wheels and toys and mountains of food, a whole city of celebration on the riverbank, all of it named for a voyage.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-boita-bandana.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.boita-bandana|h6","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","East & the Islands"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.boita-bandana-7":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.boita-bandana:7","title":"Read it in Hindi · Little Boats for the Big Sailors","text":"सुबह-सुबह जो बच्चे नावें तैराते हैं, वे सचमुच का कोई जहाज़ कहीं नहीं ले जा सकते। पर बात यह है ही नहीं। बात तो यह है कि यह समुद्र तट याद रखता है कि कभी उसने क्या किया था — और पानी पर तैरता हर दीया कहता है: हम भूले नहीं हैं कि हमारे पुरखों ने कभी समंदर पार किया था।","lang":"hi","body":"The children who float boats at dawn mostly cannot sail a ship anywhere. That is not the point. The point is that a coastline remembers what it once did — and every lamp set on the water says: we have not forgotten that our great-great-grandparents crossed the sea.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-boita-bandana.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.boita-bandana|h7","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","East & the Islands"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-it.konark-chariot-0":{"src":"passage:hi:story:it.konark-chariot:0","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Chariot That Cannot Move and Never Stops","text":"ओडिशा के तट पर, समंदर के करीब, इंसानों द्वारा बनाई गई सबसे हैरान कर देने वाली इमारतों में से एक खड़ी है। यह इतिहास है — जो सबूत दिखाते हैं — और वह सबूत आज भी वहीं पत्थरों पर तराशा हुआ खड़ा है, जिसे कोई भी जाकर देख सकता है: कोणार्क का सूर्य मंदिर।","lang":"hi","body":"On the shore of Odisha, near the sea, stands one of the most astonishing buildings human beings have ever made. This is itihaas — what the evidence shows — and the evidence is still standing there, carved in stone, for anyone to go and see: the Sun Temple of Konark.","art":"art/story/sm/it-konark-chariot.jpg","route":"#/story/it.konark-chariot|h0","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","East & the Islands"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-it.konark-chariot-1":{"src":"passage:hi:story:it.konark-chariot:1","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Chariot That Cannot Move and Never Stops","text":"इसे तेरहवीं सदी में पूर्वी गंग वंश के राजा नरसिंहदेव प्रथम के आदेश पर बनाया गया था, जिनका इस तट पर राज था। उनके कारीगरों को एक बेहद सुंदर और अनूठी कल्पना दी गई थी: यह मंदिर सिर्फ़ सूर्य देवता का सम्मान ही नहीं करेगा। यह ख़ुद उनका रथ होगा — वही विशाल रथ जिसमें सवार होकर, जैसा कि कथा बताती है, सूर्य हर दिन आकाश की सैर करते हैं।","lang":"hi","body":"It was built in the thirteenth century, by order of King Narasimhadeva the First of the Eastern Ganga dynasty, who ruled this coast. His builders were given an idea of pure poetry: the temple would not merely honour Surya, the sun. It would BE his chariot — the great chariot in which, as the katha tells it, the sun rides across the sky each day.","art":"art/story/sm/it-konark-chariot.jpg","route":"#/story/it.konark-chariot|h1","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","East & the Islands"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-it.konark-chariot-2":{"src":"passage:hi:story:it.konark-chariot:2","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Chariot That Cannot Move and Never Stops","text":"तो उन्होंने पहाड़ी जितना बड़ा पत्थर का एक रथ बनाया। उसके किनारों पर उन्होंने बारह जोड़ी विशाल पहिए तराशे, जो किसी पूरे कद के इंसान से भी ऊँचे थे, और जिनकी हर तीली तथा धुरी पर गहनों जैसी बारीक नक्काशी की गई थी। और आगे, पत्थरों में पूरी ताक़त से ज़ोर लगाते हुए सात शक्तिशाली घोड़े, जो पूरे मंदिर को भोर की दिशा में खींच रहे हों।","lang":"hi","body":"So they built a chariot of stone the size of a hill. Along its sides they carved twelve pairs of gigantic wheels, taller than a grown man, every spoke and hub worked with carvings fine as jewellery. And at the front, straining forward in stone, seven mighty horses to draw the whole temple towards the dawn.","art":"art/story/sm/it-konark-chariot.jpg","route":"#/story/it.konark-chariot|h2","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","East & the Islands"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-it.konark-chariot-3":{"src":"passage:hi:story:it.konark-chariot:3","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Chariot That Cannot Move and Never Stops","text":"\"कोणार्क के गाइड आने वाले लोगों से गिनती वाला सवाल पूछना बहुत पसंद करते हैं, तो चलिए, वही सवाल आपके लिए भी है। पहियों के बारह जोड़े। सात घोड़े। मंदिर बनाने वालों ने ये संख्याएँ जान-बूझकर चुनी थीं।\"","lang":"hi","body":"Guides at Konark love to ask visitors the counting question, so here it is for you. Twelve pairs of wheels. Seven horses. The builders chose those numbers on purpose.","art":"art/story/sm/it-konark-chariot.jpg","route":"#/story/it.konark-chariot|h3","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","East & the Islands"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-it.konark-chariot-4":{"src":"passage:hi:story:it.konark-chariot:4","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Chariot That Cannot Move and Never Stops","text":"\"सदियों तक, बंगाल की खाड़ी के नाविक इस मंदिर को दिशा पहचानने के लिए इस्तेमाल करते थे और उन्होंने इसे एक नाम भी दिया था: 'ब्लैक पैगोडा' — इसके गहरे रंग के पत्थर की वजह से, और समुद्र तट पर आगे सफ़ेदी से पुते पुरी के मंदिर, यानी अपने 'व्हाइट पैगोडा' से अलग पहचानने के लिए। इतनी बड़ी इमारत कि पानी के जहाज़ इसे देखकर अपना रुख तय करते थे।\"","lang":"hi","body":"For centuries, sailors on the Bay of Bengal used the temple as a landmark and gave it a nickname: the Black Pagoda — for its dark stone, and to tell it apart from the white-washed temple of Puri up the coast, their White Pagoda. A building so large that ships steered by it.","art":"art/story/sm/it-konark-chariot.jpg","route":"#/story/it.konark-chariot|h4","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","East & the Islands"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-it.konark-chariot-5":{"src":"passage:hi:story:it.konark-chariot:5","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Chariot That Cannot Move and Never Stops","text":"\"सबूतों की सच्ची बात यह है: आज आप जो मंदिर देखते हैं, वह पूरा नहीं है। इसका मुख्य शिखर — जो पूरे भारत के सबसे ऊँचे शिखरों में से एक होता — सदियों पहले गिरकर खंडहर बन गया, और विद्वानों में आज भी इस बात पर बहस होती है कि यह ठीक कब और क्यों गिरा: ज़मीन की वजह से, समुद्री हवा से, नुकसान से, या अनदेखी से; पुराने दस्तावेज़ बहुत कम हैं और इतिहासकार अंदाज़ा लगाने के बजाय साफ़-साफ़ यही बताते हैं। जो आज बचा हुआ है, वह है इसका बड़ा मंडप और रथ का निचला हिस्सा — और सिर्फ़ इतना ही देख कर मन चकित रह जाता है।\"","lang":"hi","body":"Honesty about the evidence: the temple you see today is not complete. Its main tower — which would have been one of the tallest in India — fell in ruin centuries ago, and scholars still debate exactly when and why: the ground, the sea air, damage, neglect; the records are thin and historians say so rather than guessing. What survives is the great porch and the chariot base — and even that much is overwhelming.","art":"art/story/sm/it-konark-chariot.jpg","route":"#/story/it.konark-chariot|h5","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","East & the Islands"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-it.konark-chariot-6":{"src":"passage:hi:story:it.konark-chariot:6","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Chariot That Cannot Move and Never Stops","text":"\"नक्काशियों को ज़रा ध्यान से देखिए, तो मंदिर का रूप बिल्कुल गंभीर नहीं लगता: संगीतकार, नर्तक, हाथी, हंस, पहलवान, परिवार, और तेरहवीं सदी की ज़िंदगी का हर एक भरा-पूरा कोना। कारीगरों ने अपनी पूरी दुनिया को ही सूरज के रथ पर उकेर दिया था — तो एक तरह से, हर किसी को इस रथ पर सवारी करने का मौका मिल गया।\"","lang":"hi","body":"Look closely at the carvings and the temple stops being solemn: musicians, dancers, elephants, geese, wrestlers, families, whole crowded inches of thirteenth-century life. The builders carved their own world onto the sun's chariot — so in a way, everyone got to ride.","art":"art/story/sm/it-konark-chariot.jpg","route":"#/story/it.konark-chariot|h6","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","East & the Islands"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-it.konark-chariot-7":{"src":"passage:hi:story:it.konark-chariot:7","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Chariot That Cannot Move and Never Stops","text":"\"1984 में, कोणार्क को यूनेस्को विश्व धरोहर स्थल घोषित किया गया — दुनिया के उन अनमोल ख़ज़ानों में से एक जिन्हें सहेज कर रखने पर सब राज़ी हुए हैं — और भारतीय पुरातत्व सर्वेक्षण इसकी देखभाल करता है। इसे बचाने वाले विशेषज्ञ इस पर लगातार काम करते रहते हैं; पत्थर के रथ को सँभालना धीमा, सावधानी भरा और कभी न ख़त्म होने वाला काम है, बिल्कुल वैसे ही जैसे किसी भी सँभालने लायक चीज़ की हिफ़ाज़त की जाती है।\"","lang":"hi","body":"In 1984, Konark was inscribed as a UNESCO World Heritage Site — one of the treasures the whole world has agreed to keep — and the Archaeological Survey of India tends it. Conservators work on it constantly; keeping a stone chariot is slow, careful, unending work, like keeping anything worth keeping.","art":"art/story/sm/it-konark-chariot.jpg","route":"#/story/it.konark-chariot|h7","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","East & the Islands"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.manika-curd-0":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.manika-curd:0","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Milkmaid and the Two Riders","text":"यह ओडिशा की सबसे प्यारी कथाओं में से एक है — पुरी के मंदिर की एक कहानी, जो सदियों से सुनाई जा रही है। ओडिशा के एक राजा, पुरुषोत्तम देव, अपनी पूरी सेना के साथ दक्षिण की ओर, दूर कांची की लंबी यात्रा पर निकले थे। वे क्यों जा रहे थे, यह कहानी तब के लिए है जब आप थोड़े बड़े हो जाएँगे; यह कहानी तो सड़क किनारे की एक दुकान और उसे चलाने वाली महिला के बारे में है।","lang":"hi","body":"This is one of Odisha's best-loved kathas — a temple story of Puri, told for centuries. A king of Odisha, Purushottama Deva, was on a long march south with his whole army, towards far-off Kanchi. The why of the march is a story for when you are older; this story is about a stall by the road, and the woman who kept it.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-manika-curd.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.manika-curd|h0","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","East & the Islands"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.manika-curd-1":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.manika-curd:1","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Milkmaid and the Two Riders","text":"उनका नाम माणिका था, और वे दही बेचती थीं — अपनी ही गायों का बढ़िया गाढ़ा दही। उनके पास पीतल का एक बर्तन था, नारियल के खोल की कलछी थी, और झील के पास सड़क किनारे एक छायादार जगह थी। सेनाएँ हों, राजा हों, या तीर्थयात्री: सब उन्हीं रास्तों से गुज़रते हैं, और उन रास्तों पर प्यास सबको लगती है।","lang":"hi","body":"Her name was Manika, and she sold curd — good thick curd from her own cows, with a brass pot and a coconut-shell ladle and a shady spot where the road ran near the lake. Armies, kings, pilgrims: everyone travels the same roads, and everyone gets thirsty on them.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-manika-curd.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.manika-curd|h1","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","East & the Islands"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.manika-curd-2":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.manika-curd:2","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Milkmaid and the Two Riders","text":"उस तपती दोपहर, बाकी सबसे आगे सड़क पर दो घुड़सवार आए — देखने में दो भाई लगते थे, एक बारिश के बादल जैसा साँवला, काले... नहीं — कहानियों में यह बात बिल्कुल साफ़ बताई गई है: एक साँवला सवार, सफ़ेद घोड़े पर; एक गोरा सवार, काले घोड़े पर; दोनों ही बेहद सुंदर, दोनों ही धूल से सने हुए, और दोनों को ही सचमुच बहुत तेज़ प्यास लगी थी।","lang":"hi","body":"That hot afternoon, two riders came up the road ahead of all the rest — two brothers by the look of them, one dark as a rain cloud on a black... no — the tellings are exact about this: one rider dark, on a white horse; one fair, on a black horse; both of them beautiful, both of them dusty, both of them very thirsty indeed.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-manika-curd.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.manika-curd|h2","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","East & the Islands"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.manika-curd-3":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.manika-curd:3","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Milkmaid and the Two Riders","text":"\"माँ, दही पिलाइए,\" साँवले सवार ने कहा, और उन्होंने दोनों को दही परोसा — एक के बाद एक कई कटोरे भर-भर कर। वे ऐसे पी रहे थे जैसे सौ सालों से घोड़े दौड़ा रहे हों। जब आख़िरकार उनका पीना पूरा हुआ, तो साँवला सवार मुस्कुराया और — \"हमारे पास सिक्के नहीं हैं। आप यह रख लीजिए। हमारे पीछे इसी रास्ते से राजा आ रहे हैं; उन्हें यह दिखा दीजिएगा, और वे हमारा हिसाब चुका देंगे।\" और उसने उन्हें एक अँगूठी दे दी।","lang":"hi","body":"\"Curd, mother,\" said the dark one, and she served them — bowl after bowl after bowl. They drank like men who had been riding for a hundred years. When at last they were done, the dark rider smiled, and — \"We have no coins with us. Take this. The king is coming up this road behind us; show it to him, and he will settle our account.\" And he gave her a ring.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-manika-curd.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.manika-curd|h3","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","East & the Islands"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.manika-curd-4":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.manika-curd:4","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Milkmaid and the Two Riders","text":"माणिका ने अपनी हथेली में रखी अँगूठी को देखा। यह उनकी थामी हुई किसी भी अँगूठी से कहीं भारी थी, और उस पर ऐसी कारीगरी थी जिसका नाम भी वे नहीं जानती थीं। दो अजनबी, पास में कोई सिक्का नहीं, और राजा से जुड़ा एक वादा।","lang":"hi","body":"Manika looked at the ring in her palm. It was heavier than any ring she had held, and worked with a craft she had no name for. Two strangers, no coins, a promise about a king.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-manika-curd.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.manika-curd|h4","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","East & the Islands"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.manika-curd-5":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.manika-curd:5","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Milkmaid and the Two Riders","text":"सेना आ पहुँची — दूर क्षितिज तक उड़ती धूल, हाथी, झंडे, और ख़ुद राजा। माणिका शाही दल के आगे बढ़ीं, अँगूठी आगे बढ़ाई, और बस इतना कहा: \"महाराज, आपसे आगे निकले दो घुड़सवारों ने मेरी दुकान पर दही पिया था। उन्होंने कहा था कि पैसे आप देंगे।\"","lang":"hi","body":"The army arrived — dust to the horizon, elephants, banners, and the king himself. Manika stepped up to the royal party, held out the ring, and said, simply: \"Two riders ahead of you drank curd at my stall, Maharaj. They said you would pay.\"","art":"art/story/sm/fk-manika-curd.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.manika-curd|h5","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","East & the Islands"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.manika-curd-6":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.manika-curd:6","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Milkmaid and the Two Riders","text":"\"राजा ने अंगूठी पर बस एक नज़र डाली — और अपनी सवारी से नीचे उतर आए। क्योंकि वे उसे पहचानते थे। वह पुरी के मंदिर की थी; खुद प्रभु की अपनी थी। और वे वही बात समझ गए जो कहानियाँ समझती हैं: कि खुद जगन्नाथ और उनके भाई बलभद्र उनकी सेना के आगे-आगे चल रहे थे, दो भाई एक सफेद और एक काले घोड़े पर सवार — और वे भी किसी आम इंसान की तरह, एक अच्छी सी दुकान पर दही पीने रुके थे।\"","lang":"hi","body":"The king took one look at the ring — and got down from his mount. For he knew it. It was from the temple at Puri; it was the Lord's own. And he understood what the tellings understand: that Jagannath and his brother Balabhadra themselves were riding ahead of his army, two brothers on a white horse and a black — and that they had stopped, like anyone, for curd at a good stall.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-manika-curd.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.manika-curd|h6","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","East & the Islands"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.manika-curd-7":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.manika-curd:7","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Milkmaid and the Two Riders","text":"\"राजा ने तुरंत मणिका का पूरा हिसाब चुका दिया — और हिसाब से कहीं ज़्यादा दिया। कहानियाँ कहती हैं कि उन्होंने उसका गाँव उसी के और उसके परिवार के नाम कर दिया; और आज भी चिल्का झील के पास मणिकापटना नाम की एक जगह है — यानी मणिका का कस्बा — जिसे ओड़िआ परिवार सड़क से जाते हुए आपको दिखा देंगे।\"","lang":"hi","body":"The king paid Manika's account on the spot — and far more than the account. The tellings say he granted her village to her and her family; and to this day, near the Chilika lake, there is a place called Manikapatna — Manika's town — which Odia families will point out to you from the road.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-manika-curd.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.manika-curd|h7","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","East & the Islands"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.rasagola-door-0":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.rasagola-door:0","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Sweet That Opened the Door","text":"\"हर गर्मी में पुरी में रथ यात्रा आती है — रथों का त्योहार, जब सारे जग के स्वामी जगन्नाथ, अपने भाई बलभद्र और बहन सुभद्रा के साथ, हज़ारों हाथों से खींचे जाने वाले लकड़ी के विशाल रथों में सवार होकर बड़े मंदिर से बाहर निकलते हैं, और आगे सड़क पर बने एक दूसरे मंदिर में रहने जाते हैं। पूरे नौ दिनों के लिए।\"","lang":"hi","body":"Every summer at Puri comes the Rath Yatra — the festival of chariots, when Jagannath, Lord of the Universe, with his brother Balabhadra and sister Subhadra, rides out of the great temple in enormous wooden chariots pulled by thousands of hands, and goes to stay at another temple up the road. For nine whole days.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-rasagola-door.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.rasagola-door|h0","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","East & the Islands"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.rasagola-door-1":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.rasagola-door:1","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Sweet That Opened the Door","text":"\"नौ दिन का सफ़र काफ़ी लंबा होता है। और यहीं आकर पुरी की कहानियाँ बड़ी आत्मीय और घरेलू हो जाती हैं, क्योंकि कोई था जो इस सफ़र पर नहीं गया: जगन्नाथ की पत्नी लक्ष्मी, सौभाग्य और सुखी गृहस्थी की देवी। वे घर पर ही रहीं। पूरे नौ दिनों तक। जबकि उनके पति आगे सड़क पर अपने भाई और बहन के साथ छुट्टियाँ मना रहे थे।\"","lang":"hi","body":"Nine days is a long trip. And here the tellings of Puri turn warm and domestic, because somebody did not go on the trip: Lakshmi, Jagannath's wife, goddess of fortune and of well-run households. She stayed home. For nine days. While her husband holidayed up the road with his brother and sister.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-rasagola-door.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.rasagola-door|h1","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","East & the Islands"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.rasagola-door-2":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.rasagola-door:2","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Sweet That Opened the Door","text":"\"कहानियाँ उनके मन के भावों को बिल्कुल सच-सच बताती हैं, और इसीलिए यह कहानी सबको इतनी प्यारी लगती है। लक्ष्मी इंतज़ार करती रहीं। वे दिन गिनती रहीं। उन नौ दिनों के लगभग बीच में, वे आगे सड़क की ओर गईं — कुछ कहानियों के अनुसार चुपके से, रात के वक़्त — दूर से उस छुट्टी की चहल-पहल देखने के लिए। और फिर वे घर लौटीं, उन्होंने सोचा, और एक फ़ैसला किया।\"","lang":"hi","body":"The tellings are honest about her feelings, which is why everyone loves this story. Lakshmi waited. She counted the days. Somewhere around the middle of the nine, she went — in some tellings secretly, at night — up the road to look at the holiday from a distance. And then she came home, and thought, and made a decision.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-rasagola-door.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.rasagola-door|h2","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","East & the Islands"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.rasagola-door-3":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.rasagola-door:3","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Sweet That Opened the Door","text":"तो वह बड़ा सा जुलूस घर लौट आया — रथ, ढोल-नगाड़े, शंख, और रस्सियां खींचता आधा ओडिशा — और मंदिर के सामने आकर रुका, पर दरवाज़ा बंद था। सारे ब्रह्मांड के स्वामी अपनी ही चौखट पर खड़े थे। ढोल की आवाज़ धीरे-धीरे थम गई। अंदर कहीं, बिल्कुल शांत, खुद भाग्य की देवी इंतज़ार कर रही थीं यह सुनने के लिए कि वे अपने बचाव में क्या कहते हैं।","lang":"hi","body":"So the great procession came home — chariots, drums, conches, half of Odisha pulling the ropes — and rolled up to the temple, and the door was shut. The Lord of the Universe stood on his own doorstep. The drums trailed off. Somewhere inside, perfectly calm, fortune herself was waiting to hear what he had to say for himself.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-rasagola-door.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.rasagola-door|h3","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","East & the Islands"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.rasagola-door-4":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.rasagola-door:4","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Sweet That Opened the Door","text":"कहानियों में कहा जाता है कि उनके पास मिठाइयाँ थीं। रसगुल्ले — चाशनी में डूबे वो नरम, सफेद गोले, जिन्हें यह तट सदियों से मंदिर के लिए बनाता आया है। कटोरी भर-भरकर रसगुल्ले, दरवाज़े की झिरी से पेश किए गए, और शायद चेहरे पर उनका सबसे प्यारा सा भाव था। एक पति, जो दुनिया की सबसे जानी-पहचानी भाषा में माफ़ी मांग रहा था।","lang":"hi","body":"What he had, the tellings say, was sweets. Rasagolas — the soft white rounds soaked in syrup that this coast has made for the temple since long ago. Bowl upon bowl of them, offered at the crack of the door, with, one imagines, his most winning expression. A husband apologising in the universal language.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-rasagola-door.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.rasagola-door|h4","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","East & the Islands"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.rasagola-door-5":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.rasagola-door:5","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Sweet That Opened the Door","text":"लक्ष्मी ने उन्हें बस उतनी ही देर इंतज़ार कराया, जितनी सबक सिखाने के लिए ज़रूरी थी। फिर उन्होंने रसगुल्ले स्वीकार कर लिए — सच कहें तो वे थे भी बहुत लाजवाब — और अपनी शर्तें रख दीं: घर संभालने वाले की परवाह किए बिना अब नौ दिन की कोई यात्रा नहीं होगी। शर्तें मान ली गईं। दरवाज़ा खुला। सारे ब्रह्मांड के स्वामी घर आ गए।","lang":"hi","body":"Lakshmi let him wait exactly as long as was instructive. Then she accepted the rasagolas — they were, to be fair, excellent — and named her terms: no more nine-day trips without proper regard for the one who keeps the house. Terms agreed. The door opened. The Lord of the Universe came home.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-rasagola-door.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.rasagola-door|h5","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","East & the Islands"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.rasagola-door-6":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.rasagola-door:6","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Sweet That Opened the Door","text":"और यह सिर्फ एक कहानी नहीं है — यह मंदिर के पंचांग में दर्ज है। जिस दिन जगन्नाथ लौटते हैं और दरवाज़े पर सुलह करते हैं, उस दिन को नीलाद्रि बिजे कहा जाता है, और हर साल उस दिन रसगुल्ले का भोग लगाया जाता है। दरवाज़ा खुलवाने वाली इस मिठाई के सम्मान में, ओडिशा इस दिन को 'रसगोला दिबस' — यानी रसगुल्ला दिवस — के रूप में भी मनाता है।","lang":"hi","body":"And this is not just a story — it is on the temple calendar. The day Jagannath returns and makes peace at the door is called Niladri Bije, and rasagolas are offered that day, every single year. Odisha even keeps the date as Rasagola Dibasa — Rasagola Day — in honour of the sweet that opened the door.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-rasagola-door.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.rasagola-door|h6","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","East & the Islands"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.ridley-night-0":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.ridley-night:0","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Night the Sea Comes Ashore","text":"साल के ज़्यादातर समय, गहिरमाथा और रुशिकुल्या नदी के मुहाने पर ओडिशा के लंबे समुद्र तट सिर्फ रेत, हवा और मछुआरों की नावों से भरे होते हैं। लेकिन समुद्र इन तटों से मिलने का एक वादा निभाता है — और कुछ अंधेरी रातों में, आमतौर पर सर्दियों के ढलते दिनों में, वह आ पहुँचता है।","lang":"hi","body":"For most of the year, the long beaches of the Odisha coast at Gahirmatha and by the Rushikulya river mouth are just sand, wind and fishing boats. But the sea is keeping an appointment with these beaches — and on a few dark nights, usually late in winter, it arrives.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-ridley-night.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.ridley-night|h0","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","East & the Islands"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.ridley-night-1":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.ridley-night:1","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Night the Sea Comes Ashore","text":"इसकी शुरुआत लहरों के फेन में दिखते कुछ उभारों से होती है। फिर कुछ और। फिर और भी बहुत से। ऑलिव रिडले समुद्री कछुए — छोटे, गोल खोल वाले, भीगे हुए जैतून के रंग जैसे — लहरों से बाहर निकलकर चलने लगते हैं। सैकड़ों। फिर हज़ारों। फिर एक ही रात में दसियों हज़ार, यहाँ तक कि जहाँ तक टॉर्च की रोशनी जा सके, पूरा समुद्र तट कछुओं से पट जाता है—अगर कोई इतना नासमझ हो कि वहाँ टॉर्च जलाए।","lang":"hi","body":"It begins as bumps in the surf line. Then more. Then more. Olive ridley sea turtles — small, round-shelled, the colour of wet olives — start walking out of the waves. Hundreds. Then thousands. Then tens of thousands, in a single night, until the beach is cobbled with turtles as far as a torch could shine, if anyone were unwise enough to shine one.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-ridley-night.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.ridley-night|h1","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","East & the Islands"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.ridley-night-2":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.ridley-night:2","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Night the Sea Comes Ashore","text":"वैज्ञानिक इसके लिए स्पैनिश शब्द अरीबादा — \"आगमन\" — का इस्तेमाल करते हैं, क्योंकि पूरी दुनिया में बस कुछ ही समुद्र तटों पर ऐसा नज़ारा दिखता है, और ओडिशा के तट उनमें सबसे ख़ास हैं। इनमें से हर एक कछुआ एक माँ है, और हर एक माँ दूर समंदर पार तैरकर इसी ख़ास रेत पर आई है।","lang":"hi","body":"Scientists use the Spanish word arribada — \"the arrival\" — for this, because only a few beaches in the whole world host it, and Odisha's are among the greatest. Every one of those turtles is a mother, and every one has swum from far across the ocean to this particular sand.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-ridley-night.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.ridley-night|h2","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","East & the Islands"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.ridley-night-3":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.ridley-night:3","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Night the Sea Comes Ashore","text":"हर माँ खुद को खींचकर लहरों की पहुँच से ऊपर ले जाती है, अपने पिछले चप्पूदार पैरों से सुराही जैसा साफ़-सुथरा घोंसला खोदती है — बिना देखे, बस अपनी सहज समझ से, जैसे कोई पीठ पीछे बुनाई कर रहा हो — लगभग सौ नरम सफ़ेद अंडे देती है, उन्हें ढकती है, रेत को थपथपाकर बराबर करती है, और वापस समंदर में चली जाती है। वह अब लौटकर नहीं आएगी। बाकी काम रेत और सूरज कर देते हैं।","lang":"hi","body":"Each mother hauls herself above the tide line, digs a neat flask-shaped nest with her back flippers — working blind, by instinct, like someone knitting behind their back — lays a hundred-odd soft white eggs, covers them, pats the sand down, and walks back into the sea. She will not return. The sand and the sun do the rest.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-ridley-night.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.ridley-night|h3","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","East & the Islands"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.ridley-night-4":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.ridley-night:4","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Night the Sea Comes Ashore","text":"लगभग छह या सात हफ़्तों बाद, पूरे तट पर अंडों से बच्चे निकलने लगते हैं। हथेली में समा जाने जितने नन्हे-नन्हे कछुए हज़ारों की तादाद में रेत से उबलते हुए बाहर आते हैं — लगभग हमेशा रात के समय — और फ़ौरन दौड़ना शुरू कर देते हैं। उन्हें जल्दी से समंदर तक पहुँचना होता है। और यहाँ इंसानों की भूमिका बहुत ज़रूरी हो जाती है: इन तटों की रखवाली करने वाले वनकर्मी और गाँव वाले अंडों से बच्चे निकलने के मौसम में तट पर अँधेरा रखते हैं।","lang":"hi","body":"Some six or seven weeks later, the beach hatches. Tiny turtles, small enough to sit in your palm, boil up out of the sand by the thousand — almost always at night — and immediately begin to run. They must reach the sea, fast. And here people matter: the wardens and villagers who watch over these beaches keep the shore dark during hatching season.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-ridley-night.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.ridley-night|h4","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","East & the Islands"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.ridley-night-5":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.ridley-night:5","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Night the Sea Comes Ashore","text":"इसलिए अंडों से बच्चे निकलने वाली रातों में तट पर अँधेरे में लोग धीरे-धीरे आते-जाते दिखते हैं: वन विभाग के कर्मचारी, लाल रोशनी वाली टॉर्च लिए वैज्ञानिक, और गाँव वाले — जिनमें मछुआरों के परिवार भी शामिल हैं जो अंडे देने के मौसम में अपने जाल अलग तरह से लगाते हैं ताकि कछुआ माताएँ आसानी से निकल सकें। ओडिशा को इन कछुओं पर ठीक वैसे ही नाज़ है जैसे दूसरी जगहों को अपनी ऐतिहासिक इमारतों पर होता है।","lang":"hi","body":"So on hatching nights there are people on the beach in the dark, moving quietly: forest department staff, scientists with red-shaded torches, and villagers — including fishing families who set their nets differently in the nesting season so the mothers can pass. Odisha is proud of these turtles the way other places are proud of monuments.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-ridley-night.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.ridley-night|h5","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","East & the Islands"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.ridley-night-6":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.ridley-night:6","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Night the Sea Comes Ashore","text":"और जो नन्हे कछुए लहरों तक पहुँच जाते हैं, वे इस विशाल महासागर में तैरते हुए दूर चले जाते हैं, और सालों के लिए ग़ायब हो जाते हैं। फिर, बड़ी होने पर मादा कछुए एक हैरान कर देने वाला काम करती हैं: वे बिना किसी रास्ते वाले हज़ारों किलोमीटर लंबे समंदर को पार करके — ठीक उसी तट पर अंडे देने वापस आती हैं जहाँ वे खुद अंडों से निकली थीं। वे इतनी सटीकता से अपना रास्ता कैसे ढूँढ़ लेती हैं, इस पर अभी भी अध्ययन चल रहा है; इसका जवाब कहीं न कहीं खारे पानी, चुंबकत्व और यादों में छिपा है।","lang":"hi","body":"And the little ones that reach the waves swim out into the enormous ocean, and vanish for years. Then, grown, the females do the astonishing thing: they come back — across thousands of kilometres of trackless sea — to nest on the very coast where they hatched. How they navigate so exactly is still being studied; the answer is written somewhere in salt and magnetism and memory.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-ridley-night.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.ridley-night|h6","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","East & the Islands"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.tapoi-0":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.tapoi:0","title":"Read it in Hindi · Tapoi and the Seven Ships","text":"\"ओडिशा के समुद्री यात्राओं के सुनहरे दौर में एक सौदागर रहता था, जिसके सात बेटे थे और सबसे छोटी व सबसे लाडली एक बेटी: तपोई। वह पूरे घर का मोती थी — और जब हवाओं का रुख बदला, तो उसके सातों भाइयों ने दूर द्वीपों के लंबे सफ़र के लिए अपने सात जहाज़ लादे और तपोई को अपनी सात बहुओं की देखरेख में छोड़कर रवाना हो गए।\"","lang":"hi","body":"In the great sailing days of Odisha there lived a merchant with seven sons and, last and most loved, one daughter: Tapoi. She was the pearl of the household — and when the winds turned, her seven brothers loaded their seven ships for the long voyage to the far islands, and sailed, leaving Tapoi in the care of their seven wives.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-tapoi.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.tapoi|h0","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","East & the Islands"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.tapoi-1":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.tapoi:1","title":"Read it in Hindi · Tapoi and the Seven Ships","text":"\"कुछ समय तक तो सब रेशम और मिठाइयों जैसा सुखद रहा। लेकिन महीने खिंचते चले गए, कोई पाल लौटकर नहीं आया, और घर का धन कम होने लगा — और सात में से छह बहुओं का रंग छोटी बहन के लिए बदल गया। लाड-दुलार बंद हो गया। फिर दया भी ख़त्म हो गई। उन्होंने उसे चिथड़े पहनाए, जूठन खिलाई, और रोज़ बकरियाँ चराने झाड़ियों वाले मैदानों में भेजने लगीं। केवल सातवीं बहू, जो सबसे छोटी थी, दयालु बनी रही — वह चुपके से उसे खाना दे देती, उसके कपड़े सिल देती, और हौसला देती: धीरज रखो, छोटी; जहाज़ ज़रूर लौटेंगे।\"","lang":"hi","body":"For a while, all was silk and sweets. But the months stretched, and no sail came back, and the household's money thinned — and six of the seven wives changed towards the little sister. The petting stopped. Then the kindness stopped. They dressed her in rags, fed her scraps, and sent her out to the scrubland every day to herd the goats. Only the seventh wife, the youngest, stayed kind — slipping her food, mending her clothes, whispering: bear it, little one; the ships will come.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-tapoi.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.tapoi|h1","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","East & the Islands"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.tapoi-2":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.tapoi:2","title":"Read it in Hindi · Tapoi and the Seven Ships","text":"\"इस तरह तपोई बकरियों और मैनाओं के साथ हवादार बंजर ज़मीन पर रहने लगी, सौदागर का मोती अब चरवाही बन चुकी थी। और वहीं, भाद्रपद के महीने में, उसने रविवार के दिन गाँव की लड़कियों को ख़ुदा — यानी टूटे हुए चावल, जो सबसे मामूली अनाज है — का भोग लेकर इंतज़ार करने वालों की रखवाली करने वाली मंगला देवी की पूजा के लिए इकट्ठा होते देखा।\"","lang":"hi","body":"So Tapoi lived on the windy commons with the goats and the mynah birds, the merchant's pearl turned goatherd. And there, in the month of Bhadraba, she saw village girls gathering on Sundays with offerings of khuda — broken rice, the humblest grain there is — to worship the goddess Mangala, keeper of those who wait.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-tapoi.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.tapoi|h2","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","East & the Islands"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.tapoi-3":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.tapoi:3","title":"Read it in Hindi · Tapoi and the Seven Ships","text":"\"तपोई के पास कुछ भी नहीं था: न रेशम, न मिठाइयाँ, न अपने नाम का एक साबुत चावल का दाना। बस टूटा हुआ चावल था, जिसे उसने बकरियों के आगे फेंके गए दानों में से बटोरा था।\"","lang":"hi","body":"Tapoi had nothing: no silk, no sweets, not a whole grain of rice to her name. Only broken rice, gathered from what was thrown to the goats.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-tapoi.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.tapoi|h3","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","East & the Islands"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.tapoi-4":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.tapoi:4","title":"Read it in Hindi · Tapoi and the Seven Ships","text":"\"इसलिए तपोई हर रविवार अपने टूटे हुए चावल से, खुले मैदान में बकरियों की संगत के बीच पूजा करती रही — और बस एक ही चीज़ माँगती रही: मेरे भाइयों के जहाज़ों को घर लौटा लाओ।\"","lang":"hi","body":"So Tapoi worshipped with her broken rice, Sunday after Sunday, out on the commons with the goats for a congregation — and asked for one thing only: bring my brothers' ships home.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-tapoi.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.tapoi|h4","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","East & the Islands"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.tapoi-5":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.tapoi:5","title":"Read it in Hindi · Tapoi and the Seven Ships","text":"और एक सुबह क्षितिज पर पाल लहराते दिखे। पूरे सात। सातों जहाज़ पानी की सतह तक लदे हुए नदी में आगे बढ़े — सफ़र लंबा रहा था क्योंकि वह बड़ा कामयाब रहा था — और सातों भाई किनारे पर उतरते ही, सबसे पहले अपनी छोटी बहन के बारे में पूछने लगे।","lang":"hi","body":"And one morning the horizon grew sails. Seven of them. The seven ships came up the river laden to the waterline — the voyage had been long because it had been lucky — and the seven brothers stepped ashore asking, first thing, for their little sister.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-tapoi.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.tapoi|h5","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","East & the Islands"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.tapoi-6":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.tapoi:6","title":"Read it in Hindi · Tapoi and the Seven Ships","text":"छहों बहुएँ तपोई को रेशमी कपड़े पहनाने और छह महीने के ज़ुल्म को छह मिनट में मिटाने के लिए दौड़ पड़ीं। लेकिन सच रेशम से भी तेज़ चलता है। पूरी बात सामने आ ही गई — वे चीथड़े, बचा-खुचा खाना, बकरियाँ — और इन सब के बीच सबसे छोटी बहू की दया किसी दिए की तरह जगमगा रही थी।","lang":"hi","body":"The six wives flew to dress Tapoi in silk and undo six months of cruelty in six minutes. But truth walks faster than silk. The whole story came out — the rags, the scraps, the goats — the youngest wife's kindness shining out of it like a lamp.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-tapoi.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.tapoi|h6","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","East & the Islands"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.tapoi-7":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.tapoi:7","title":"Read it in Hindi · Tapoi and the Seven Ships","text":"पुरानी कहानियों में छहों बहुओं के साथ बड़ी सख़्ती बरती गई है, और नीचे दिया गया स्रोत भी यह बात साफ़-साफ़ कहता है। अगर इसे नरमी से कहें: तो उन्हें पूरे परिवार के सामने खड़ा करके सच सुनाया गया, और उनसे तपोई की वैसे ही सेवा करवाई गई जैसे तपोई से करवाई गई थी — तब तक, जब तक वे इसे दिल से समझ न गईं। जो शर्म सीख दे, वह बिना सीख की सज़ा से कहीं बेहतर होती है। सातवीं बहू का सबसे ज़्यादा आदर-सत्कार हुआ।","lang":"hi","body":"The oldest tellings deal harshly with the six wives, and the source below says so honestly. Told gently: they were made to stand before the whole household and hear the truth said out loud, and to serve Tapoi as she had been made to serve — until they understood it from the inside. Shame that teaches is worth more than punishment that doesn't. The seventh wife was honoured above them all.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-tapoi.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.tapoi|h7","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","East & the Islands"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.lalkamal-nilkamal-0":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.lalkamal-nilkamal:0","title":"Read it in Hindi · Lalkamal and Nilkamal","text":"यह कहानी 'ठाकुरमार झूली' से है — दादी माँ की कहानियों की पोटली, जो बंगाल की सबसे प्यारी कहानियों की किताब है। एक राजा की दो रानियाँ थीं। एक तो आम इंसानी रानी थी; दूसरी, हालाँकि दरबार में किसी को पता नहीं था, रक्खोश कुल की थी — यानी बंगाली कहानियों के वे बड़े, बेतुके राक्षस, जिनमें बस नुकीले दाँत और बेहिसाब भूख होती थी, पर अक़्ल बिल्कुल नहीं।","lang":"hi","body":"Out of Thakurmar Jhuli — the Grandmother's Bag of Tales, Bengal's most beloved storybook — comes this one. A king had two queens. One was an ordinary human queen; the other, though nobody at court knew it, came of rakkhosh folk — the big, ridiculous ogres of Bengali tales, all fangs and appetite and very little sense.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-lalkamal-nilkamal.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.lalkamal-nilkamal|h0","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","East & the Islands"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.lalkamal-nilkamal-1":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.lalkamal-nilkamal:1","title":"Read it in Hindi · Lalkamal and Nilkamal","text":"दोनों रानियों का एक-एक बेटा हुआ। राक्षसी रानी का बेटा था लालकमल, यानी लाल कमल; इंसानी रानी का बेटा था नीलकमल, यानी नीला कमल। और सबसे प्यारी बात यह थी: दोनों सौतेले भाई एक-दूसरे से बेहद प्यार करते थे। वही खेल, वही पढ़ाई, वही शैतानियाँ; ऐसा कभी नहीं होता था कि एक दिखे और दूसरा उसके ठीक पीछे न हो।","lang":"hi","body":"Each queen had a son. The rakkhosh-queen's boy was Lalkamal, the red lotus; the human queen's boy was Nilkamal, the blue lotus. And here is the lovely part: the two half-brothers loved each other completely. Same games, same lessons, same mischief; you never saw one without the other close behind.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-lalkamal-nilkamal.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.lalkamal-nilkamal|h1","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","East & the Islands"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.lalkamal-nilkamal-2":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.lalkamal-nilkamal:2","title":"Read it in Hindi · Lalkamal and Nilkamal","text":"लेकिन रात में, रक्खोश रिश्तेदार महल के आस-पास सूँघते-सूँघते आ धमके — और रक्खोश के आने की ख़बर तो एक मील दूर से ही लग जाती है, क्योंकि वह अपने ख़ानदान का नारा दहाड़े बिना रह ही नहीं सकता: \"हाऊ माऊ खाऊ! मानुषेर गन्धो पाऊ!\" — जिसका बंगाली में कुछ-कुछ यह मतलब होता है, \"हाऊ! माऊ! खाऊँगा! मुझे इंसान की गंध आ रही है!\" रक्खोश एक साथ बेहद ख़तरनाक भी होते हैं और छिपकर दबे पाँव आने में एकदम फिसड्डी भी।","lang":"hi","body":"But at night, rakkhosh relatives came sniffing round the palace — and a rakkhosh announces itself from a mile off, because it cannot help bellowing the family motto: \"Haau maau khaau! Manusher gawndho paau!\" — which is Bengali for roughly \"Fee! Fo! Yum! I smell a hu-man!\" Rakkhosh are extremely dangerous and extremely bad at being sneaky, both at once.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-lalkamal-nilkamal.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.lalkamal-nilkamal|h2","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","East & the Islands"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.lalkamal-nilkamal-3":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.lalkamal-nilkamal:3","title":"Read it in Hindi · Lalkamal and Nilkamal","text":"भाइयों को पता चला कि ख़तरा पास आ रहा है, और उन्होंने वही किया जो 'ठाकुरमार झूली' के वीर करते हैं: उन्होंने दो घोड़ों पर जीन कसी और इस ख़तरे का अंत करने निकल पड़े — सीधे रक्खोशों के अपने राज तक। वहाँ उन्होंने दानव-राजा के ही मेहमानख़ाने में एक कमरा लिया और बारी-बारी से पहरा देने की ठानी: एक सोएगा, एक जागकर पहरा देगा, और पहरा देने वाले को बिल्कुल भी सोना नहीं है।","lang":"hi","body":"The brothers learned the danger was creeping close, and did what heroes in Thakurmar Jhuli do: they saddled two horses and rode out to end it — all the way to the rakkhosh kingdom itself. There they took a room in the ogre-king's own guest house, and agreed to keep watch in turns: one sleeps, one guards, and the guard must NOT fall asleep.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-lalkamal-nilkamal.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.lalkamal-nilkamal|h3","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","East & the Islands"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.lalkamal-nilkamal-4":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.lalkamal-nilkamal:4","title":"Read it in Hindi · Lalkamal and Nilkamal","text":"और क्योंकि वह जाग रहा था, उसने सुन लिया — दो रक्खोश पहरेदार अंधेरे में गपशप लड़ा रहे थे, और रक्खोशों की आदत के मुताबिक बहुत ही ज़ोर-ज़ोर से उस इकलौते राज़ की बात कर रहे थे, जिसे उन्हें कभी मुँह से बाहर निकालना ही नहीं चाहिए था: दानव-राजा की जान उसके शरीर में थी ही नहीं। वह तो एक गहरे, अंधेरे तालाब की तलहटी में, एक बंद डिब्बे के अंदर दो मधुमक्खियों में बसी थी।","lang":"hi","body":"And because he was awake, he heard it — two rakkhosh sentries gossiping in the dark, as rakkhosh always do, far too loudly, about the one secret they should never have said aloud: the ogre-king's life was not kept in his body at all. It was kept in a pair of bees, sealed in a box, at the bottom of a deep, dark tank.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-lalkamal-nilkamal.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.lalkamal-nilkamal|h4","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","East & the Islands"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.lalkamal-nilkamal-5":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.lalkamal-nilkamal:5","title":"Read it in Hindi · Lalkamal and Nilkamal","text":"सुबह होते ही दोनों भाइयों ने वह तालाब ढूँढ निकाला। नीलकमल ने डुबकी लगाई — ठंडे, हरे पानी में गहरे और गहरे — और हाथों में डिब्बा थामे हाँफता हुआ बाहर निकला। अंदर दो सुनहरी मधुमक्खियाँ ग़ुस्से से भिनभिना रही थीं, और राज्य का हर एक रक्खोश एकदम चौंककर सीधा बैठ गया, क्योंकि उन्हें लगा कि दुनिया में कुछ तो गड़बड़ होने लगी है।","lang":"hi","body":"At dawn the brothers found the tank. Nilkamal dived — down and down through the cold green water — and came up gasping with the box in his hands. Inside, two golden bees buzzed furiously, and every rakkhosh in the kingdom sat bolt upright at once, feeling something go wobbly in the world.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-lalkamal-nilkamal.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.lalkamal-nilkamal|h5","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","East & the Islands"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.lalkamal-nilkamal-6":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.lalkamal-nilkamal:6","title":"Read it in Hindi · Lalkamal and Nilkamal","text":"हर दिशा से रक्खोश गरजते हुए, अपना हाऊ-माऊ-खाऊ चिल्लाते चले आए — तभी लालकमल ने वह डिब्बा हवा में उठा दिया, और पूरी फ़ौज फिसलती हुई ऐसे ठिठक कर रुक गई, जैसे किसी शादी में आई चाचियाँ-मौसियाँ अचानक बड़ी भली बन जाती हैं। \"ज़रा संभलकर,\" दानव-राजा ने दबी हुई आवाज़ में कहा। और जैसे ही मधुमक्खियों को छोड़ा गया और जादू टूटा, उस पूरे भयानक राज को बाँधे रखने वाला तिलिस्म बिखर गया — और दहाड़ें, नुकीले दाँत, ख़ानदानी नारा और बाकी सब कुछ, सलेटी धुएँ का गुबार बनकर ताड़ के पेड़ों के ऊपर हवा में उड़ गया।","lang":"hi","body":"Rakkhosh came thundering from every direction, roaring their haau-maau-khaau — and Lalkamal held up the box, and the whole army skidded to a halt, suddenly as polite as aunties at a wedding. \"Careful with that,\" said the ogre-king, in a small voice. And the moment the bees were let go and the spell was broken, the magic that held that whole grim kingdom together came undone — and it all went up in a puff of grey smoke and blew away over the palm trees, roars, fangs, motto and all.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-lalkamal-nilkamal.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.lalkamal-nilkamal|h6","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","East & the Islands"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.lalkamal-nilkamal-7":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.lalkamal-nilkamal:7","title":"Read it in Hindi · Lalkamal and Nilkamal","text":"दोनों भाई अपनी दोनों माताओं के पास घर लौट आए, और आखिरकार महल रात में चैन की नींद सोया। और बाद में हर किसी को जो बात याद रही, वह मधुमक्खियाँ या पानी में लगाई डुबकी नहीं थी, बल्कि सबसे सीधी-सादी बात थी: किसी भी पल, किसी भी ख़तरे में, दोनों में से किसी भाई ने एक बार भी दूसरे के बिना जाने की बात सोची तक नहीं थी।","lang":"hi","body":"The brothers rode home to both their mothers, and the palace slept soundly at night, at last. And what everyone remembered afterwards was not the bees or the diving, but the simplest thing: neither brother, at any point, in any danger, had even once considered leaving without the other.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-lalkamal-nilkamal.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.lalkamal-nilkamal|h7","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","East & the Islands"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.gopal-pot-of-wit-0":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.gopal-pot-of-wit:0","title":"Read it in Hindi · A Pot Full of Cleverness","text":"\"बंगाल के कृष्णनगर में राजा कृष्णचंद्र के दरबार में, सबसे तेज़ ज़ुबान और सबसे गोल-मटोल पेट, दोनों ही गोपाल भाँड़ के थे — जो शाही नाई और विदूषक थे — बीरबल को बंगाल का जवाब, और बंगाल में तो स्वाभाविक रूप से, दोनों में से उन्हीं को असली माना जाता था।\"","lang":"hi","body":"At the court of Raja Krishnachandra of Krishnanagar in Bengal, the sharpest tongue and the roundest belly both belonged to Gopal Bhar, the royal barber and jester — Bengal's answer to Birbal, and in Bengal, naturally, considered the original of the two.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-gopal-pot-of-wit.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.gopal-pot-of-wit|h0","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","East & the Islands"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.gopal-pot-of-wit-1":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.gopal-pot-of-wit:1","title":"Read it in Hindi · A Pot Full of Cleverness","text":"एक दिन बाहर से आए एक पंडित जी ने नाक सिकोड़ते हुए ताना मारा कि राजा का दरबार सोने से तो भरा है मगर यहाँ अक्ल की भारी कंगाली है। यह बात राजा को चुभ गई और उन्होंने एक ही झटके में सबको अपनी चतुराई दिखाने की ठान ली। \"गोपाल!\" भरे दरबार में उन्होंने ऐलान किया। \"कहते हैं कि तुम पूरे बंगाल के सबसे हाज़िरजवाब इंसान हो। इसे साबित करके दिखाओ। अगली पूर्णिमा तक मेरे लिए एक मटका भरकर बुद्धि—यानी एक मटका भरकर अक्ल लेकर आओ। अगर नहीं ला पाए, तो हम समझ जाएँगे कि तुम्हारी होशियारी सिर्फ बातों ही बातों की थी।\"","lang":"hi","body":"One day a visiting pandit sniffed that the Raja's court was rich in gold but poor in brains, and the Raja, stung, decided to out-clever everyone at once. \"Gopal!\" he announced before the full court. \"You are said to be the wittiest man in Bengal. Prove it. Bring me a pot full of buddhi — a pot full of wit — by the next full moon. Fail, and we shall know your cleverness was only talk.\"","art":"art/story/sm/fk-gopal-pot-of-wit.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.gopal-pot-of-wit|h1","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","East & the Islands"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.gopal-pot-of-wit-2":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.gopal-pot-of-wit:2","title":"Read it in Hindi · A Pot Full of Cleverness","text":"दरबार में दबी-दबी हँसी गूँज उठी। सुराही से कोई अक्लमंदी तो उँडेल नहीं सकता; सब समझ चुके थे कि आखिरकार गोपाल हार ही गया। लेकिन गोपाल ने झुककर आदाब किया, घर गया... और बाहर अपनी सब्ज़ियों की क्यारी में, एक संकरे मुँह वाले मिट्टी के घड़े के पास लौकी का एक बीज बो दिया।","lang":"hi","body":"The court tittered. You cannot pour cleverness out of a jug; everyone knew Gopal was beaten at last. Gopal, however, bowed deeply, went home... and out in his vegetable patch, planted one gourd seed beside a narrow-necked clay pot.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-gopal-pot-of-wit.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.gopal-pot-of-wit|h2","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","East & the Islands"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.gopal-pot-of-wit-3":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.gopal-pot-of-wit:3","title":"Read it in Hindi · A Pot Full of Cleverness","text":"\"बेल ऊपर चढ़ती गई, और गोपाल ने एक नन्हीं-सी लौकी को — तुम्हारे अँगूठे जितनी छोटी — मटके की सँकरी गर्दन से अंदर डाल दिया। और वहाँ, मटके के अँधेरे में, गर्दन के रास्ते बेल से खुराक पाती हुई, वह लौकी बढ़ती गई। और बढ़ती गई। यहाँ तक कि उसने अंदर की हर गोलाई को भर दिया, ठीक वैसे जैसे दस्ताने में मुट्ठी पूरी तरह समा जाती है।\"","lang":"hi","body":"The vine climbed, and Gopal trained one baby gourd — small as your thumb — in through the pot's narrow neck. And there, in the dark of the pot, fed by its vine through the neck, the gourd grew. And grew. Until it filled every curve of the inside, snug as a fist in a glove.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-gopal-pot-of-wit.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.gopal-pot-of-wit|h3","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","East & the Islands"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.gopal-pot-of-wit-4":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.gopal-pot-of-wit:4","title":"Read it in Hindi · A Pot Full of Cleverness","text":"पूर्णिमा के दिन, गोपाल ने सिंहासन के सामने घड़ा रख दिया, बेल अब भी लटक रही थी। \"महाराज, आपके हुक्म के मुताबिक, बुद्धि से भरा घड़ा।\" राजा ने अंदर झाँका, कद्दू देखा और हँस पड़े। \"अरे बदमाश, यह तो सब्ज़ी है!\" \"चखकर देख लीजिए, महाराज। लेकिन पहले आपको इसे बाहर निकालना होगा।\"","lang":"hi","body":"On the full moon, Gopal set the pot before the throne, vine still trailing. \"A pot full of buddhi, Maharaj, as ordered.\" The Raja peered in, saw the gourd, and laughed. \"This is a vegetable, you rogue!\" \"Taste it and see, Maharaj. But you will have to take it out first.\"","art":"art/story/sm/fk-gopal-pot-of-wit.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.gopal-pot-of-wit|h4","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","East & the Islands"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.gopal-pot-of-wit-5":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.gopal-pot-of-wit:5","title":"Read it in Hindi · A Pot Full of Cleverness","text":"राजा ने अंदर हाथ डाला। लौकी बाहर नहीं निकल रही थी — मटके का मुँह बहुत ही संकरा था। उन्होंने मटके को उल्टा किया। उसे हिलाया। उनका चेहरा शर्म से हल्का गुलाबी पड़ गया। \"यह बाहर नहीं निकल रही, गोपाल।\" \"जी नहीं, महाराज,\" गोपाल मुस्कुराते हुए बोला। \"बुद्धि की भी यही तो बात है। छोटे दिमाग में डालना आसान है, पर बड़े सिर से बाहर नहीं उड़ेल सकते।\"","lang":"hi","body":"The Raja reached in. The gourd would not come — the neck was far too narrow. He turned the pot over. He shook it. He went a delicate shade of pink. \"It does not come OUT, Gopal.\" \"No, Maharaj,\" said Gopal, beaming. \"That is the thing about buddhi. Easy to put into a young head. From a grown one, it does not pour.\"","art":"art/story/sm/fk-gopal-pot-of-wit.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.gopal-pot-of-wit|h5","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","East & the Islands"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.gopal-pot-of-wit-6":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.gopal-pot-of-wit:6","title":"Read it in Hindi · A Pot Full of Cleverness","text":"\"और इसीलिए, महाराज,\" गोपाल अपनी रौ में आते हुए आगे बोला, \"इसे उगाना पड़ता है — धीरे-धीरे, अँधेरे में, बिना दिखे, एक नन्हे-से बीज से। जो कोई भी आपसे बनी-बनाई अक्ल का मटका देने का वादा करता है,\" और यहाँ वह बाहर से आए पंडित जी की ओर हल्का-सा झुका, \"वह आपको एक खाली मटका ही बेच रहा है।\"","lang":"hi","body":"\"And that, Maharaj,\" Gopal went on, warming up nicely, \"is why it must be grown — slowly, in the dark, unseen, from one small seed. Anyone who promises you a pot of ready-made wit,\" and here he bowed very slightly towards the visiting pandit, \"is selling you an empty pot.\"","art":"art/story/sm/fk-gopal-pot-of-wit.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.gopal-pot-of-wit|h6","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","East & the Islands"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.gopal-pot-of-wit-7":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.gopal-pot-of-wit:7","title":"Read it in Hindi · A Pot Full of Cleverness","text":"राजा इतना हँसे कि उनका मुकुट खिसक गया, उन्होंने गोपाल को उसके वज़न के बराबर — खैर, बात बंगाल की है तो मिठाइयों के वज़न के बराबर — मिठाइयाँ दीं, और उस मटके को दरबार में सजाकर रखवा दिया। उसके बाद जब भी कोई अपनी अक्ल की डींग हाँकता, राजा कृष्णचंद्र बस चुपचाप उस मटके की तरफ इशारा कर देते।","lang":"hi","body":"The Raja laughed until his crown slipped, paid Gopal his weight in — well, in sweets, this being Bengal — and kept the pot on display in the court. Whenever anyone boasted of their brains thereafter, Krishnachandra would silently point at it.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-gopal-pot-of-wit.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.gopal-pot-of-wit|h7","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","East & the Islands"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.bonbibi-dukhey-0":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.bonbibi-dukhey:0","title":"Read it in Hindi · Bonbibi, Lady of the Forest","text":"बंगाल के दक्षिणी छोर पर, जहाँ गंगा की सैकड़ों धाराएँ समुद्र में मिलती हैं, सुंदरबन बसा है — धरती का सबसे बड़ा मैंग्रोव जंगल। यह ज्वार-भाटे वाली नदियों, साँस लेती मिट्टी और खारे पानी में खड़े पेड़ों की भूलभुलैया है, और रॉयल बंगाल टाइगर का बसेरा भी। लोग इसके किनारों पर रहते हैं और शहद, मछली तथा लकड़ी के लिए जंगल में जाते हैं। और कोई भी वहाँ अकेला कदम नहीं रखता।","lang":"hi","body":"At the bottom of Bengal, where the Ganga's hundred mouths meet the sea, lies the Sundarbans — the largest mangrove forest on Earth, a maze of tidal rivers and breathing mud and trees that stand in salt water, and the realm of the royal Bengal tiger. People live at its edge and enter it for honey, fish and wood. And no one enters alone.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-bonbibi-dukhey.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.bonbibi-dukhey|h0","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","East & the Islands"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.bonbibi-dukhey-1":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.bonbibi-dukhey:1","title":"Read it in Hindi · Bonbibi, Lady of the Forest","text":"जंगल की नदियों में नावें उतरने से पहले, शहद इकट्ठा करने वाले — जिन्हें मौले कहा जाता है — एक नाम पुकारते हैं: बोनबीबी। यानी जंगल की देवी। और उनकी अनोखी बात यह है: हिंदू परिवार भी उनका नाम लेते हैं और मुस्लिम परिवार भी, एक साथ, एक ही नाव में बैठकर। उनकी कहानी 'बोनबीबी जोहुरनामा' नाम की किताब से पढ़ी जाती है — जो इस्लाम के पवित्र ग्रंथों की तरह दाईं ओर से पढ़ने के लिए छपी है — और जंगल के किनारे उनके थान सबके लिए खुले हैं। साफ़ दिल से आने वाले हर इंसान की वह रक्षक हैं, और उन्होंने कभी किसी से उसका धर्म नहीं पूछा।","lang":"hi","body":"Before the boats slip into the forest rivers, the honey-gatherers — the moule, as they are called — say a name: Bonbibi. The lady of the forest. And here is the wonder of her: the Hindu families say it and the Muslim families say it, together, in the same boats. Her tale is read from a book called the Bonbibi Johuranama — printed, like the holy books of Islam, to be read from the right-hand side — and her shrines stand open to everyone at the forest's edge. She is the guardian of all who enter with a clean heart, and she has never once asked anyone their faith.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-bonbibi-dukhey.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.bonbibi-dukhey|h1","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","East & the Islands"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.bonbibi-dukhey-2":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.bonbibi-dukhey:2","title":"Read it in Hindi · Bonbibi, Lady of the Forest","text":"\"जंगल में एक और भी पुरानी शक्ति बसती है: दक्खिन राय, दक्षिण के स्वामी, जो एक विशाल बाघ का रूप धरकर चलते हैं। वे कोई राक्षस नहीं हैं — यह बात साफ़ समझ लो। वे जंगल की अपनी ही भयंकर शान हैं, जिनकी जंगल के थानों में पूरी श्रद्धा से पूजा होती है; लेकिन इंसानी लालच पर उनका गुस्सा भड़क उठता है, और जब लोग उनके जंगल से बहुत ज़्यादा छीन लेते हैं, तो उनका न्याय बड़ा भयानक होता है। यह पुरानी कहानी उसी दिन की है जब उन दोनों ने आपस में नियम तय किए थे।\"","lang":"hi","body":"The forest also has an older power: Dokkhin Rai, lord of the south, who rides in the shape of the great tiger. He is not a monster — say that clearly. He is the forest's own fierce majesty, honoured in his own right at forest shrines; but his anger burns against human greed, and when people take too much from his forest, his justice is terrible. The old tale is about the day the two of them settled the rules.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-bonbibi-dukhey.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.bonbibi-dukhey|h2","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","East & the Islands"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.bonbibi-dukhey-3":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.bonbibi-dukhey:3","title":"Read it in Hindi · Bonbibi, Lady of the Forest","text":"\"धोना नाम के एक लालची व्यापारी ने शहद के लिए सात नावें तैयार कीं, और — क्योंकि कहानी में कोई शर्मनाक बात भी होनी ही चाहिए — वह एक गरीब विधवा के छोटे बेटे दुखे को अपने साथ ले गया, जिसके नाम का मतलब ही 'दुख' होता है। जंगल के गहरे सन्नाटे में, धोना के लालच और दक्खिन राय के गुस्से का आमना-सामना हुआ, और एक भयानक सौदा तय हुआ: नावें शहद और मोम से लदकर लौटेंगी, और उस लड़के को कीचड़ भरे किनारे पर अकेला, बाघ-राज के हवाले छोड़ दिया जाएगा।\"","lang":"hi","body":"A greedy trader named Dhona fitted out seven boats for honey, and — because the tale must have its shame — brought along a poor widow's young son, Dukhey, whose name means sorrow. Deep in the forest, Dhona's greed and Dokkhin Rai's anger found each other, and a terrible bargain was struck: the boats would return heaped with honey and wax, and the boy would be left behind, alone on the mud flats, for the tiger-lord.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-bonbibi-dukhey.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.bonbibi-dukhey|h3","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","East & the Islands"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.bonbibi-dukhey-4":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.bonbibi-dukhey:4","title":"Read it in Hindi · Bonbibi, Lady of the Forest","text":"\"दुखे किनारे पर अकेला खड़ा रहा; नावें दूर जाकर छोटी होती गईं, जंगल बड़ा होता गया, और मैंग्रोव के जंगलों में कहीं सुनहरी धारियों वाली कोई चीज़ हिलने लगी। तब उस बालक ने वही एक काम किया जो नाव पर चढ़ने से पहले उसकी माँ ने उसे सिखाया था: \"अगर तुम कभी जंगल में भटक जाओ और कोई उम्मीद न बचे, तो माँ बोनबीबी को पुकारना। वे दौड़ी चली आती हैं।\"\"","lang":"hi","body":"Dukhey stood alone on the bank as the boats grew small, and the forest grew large, and somewhere in the mangroves something golden and striped began to move. And the boy did the one thing his mother had taught him before he sailed: \"If you are ever lost past hope in the forest, call Ma Bonbibi. She comes.\"","art":"art/story/sm/fk-bonbibi-dukhey.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.bonbibi-dukhey|h4","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","East & the Islands"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.bonbibi-dukhey-5":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.bonbibi-dukhey:5","title":"Read it in Hindi · Bonbibi, Lady of the Forest","text":"\"वे तुरंत आ पहुँचीं, साथ में उनके भाई शाह जोंगोली भी थे, और वे उस बालक तथा बाघ-राज के बीच खड़ी हो गईं। वहाँ कोई ऐसा युद्ध नहीं हुआ जिसे लड़ाई कहा जा सके — यही तो इस कहानी की कोमल सच्चाई है: दक्खिन राय का विनाश नहीं किया गया, क्योंकि जंगल के लोगों के लिए जो पूज्य है, उसका नाश नहीं हो सकता; उन्हें सुधारा गया। बोनबीबी बोलीं, दक्षिण के स्वामी ने सिर झुकाया, और दोनों के बीच सुलह हो गई — शर्तों वाली सुलह।\"","lang":"hi","body":"She came at once, with her brother Shah Jongoli at her side, and stood between the boy and the tiger-lord. There was no battle worth the name — this is the gentle truth of the tale: Dokkhin Rai was not destroyed, for nothing sacred to the forest people could be; he was corrected. Bonbibi spoke, and the lord of the south bowed, and peace was made between them — a peace with terms.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-bonbibi-dukhey.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.bonbibi-dukhey|h5","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","East & the Islands"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.bonbibi-dukhey-6":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.bonbibi-dukhey:6","title":"Read it in Hindi · Bonbibi, Lady of the Forest","text":"\"और वे शर्तें ही तो इस कहानी का असली खज़ाना हैं। जंगल का बँटवारा हो गया: गहरे बीहड़ इलाके हमेशा के लिए दक्खिन राय और उनके जीवों के नाम रहे; और किनारे के इलाके इंसानों के लिए — और इंसान वहाँ केवल अपनी ज़रूरत पर ही जा सकते हैं, महज़ अपनी चाहत पूरी करने कभी नहीं। सच्चे दिल और खाली हाथों से आओ, बस उतना ही लो जितनी तुम्हारे परिवार को ज़रूरत है, कुछ भी बर्बाद मत करो, और बोनबीबी तुम्हारे साथ चलेंगी। लालच लेकर आओगे, तो अकेले ही भटकोगे।\"","lang":"hi","body":"And the terms are the whole treasure of the story. The forest was shared out: the deep wild places for Dokkhin Rai and his creatures, forever; the edges for the people — and the people may enter ONLY needing, never merely wanting. Come with a clean heart and empty hands, take just what your family needs, waste nothing, and Bonbibi walks with you. Come greedy, and you walk alone.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-bonbibi-dukhey.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.bonbibi-dukhey|h6","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","East & the Islands"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.bonbibi-dukhey-7":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.bonbibi-dukhey:7","title":"Read it in Hindi · Bonbibi, Lady of the Forest","text":"\"दुखे को घर पहुँचाया गया — कहानियाँ कहती हैं कि एक बड़े मगरमच्छ की पीठ पर बैठाकर, जो पूरे बंगाली साहित्य में घर लौटने की सबसे अनोखी सवारी है — और साथ में इतना धन दिया गया कि उसकी माँ का जीवन हमेशा के लिए संवर जाए। बाज़ार-बाज़ार में धोना की शर्मनाक हरकत के चर्चे फैल गए। और आज के दिन तक मौले इन शर्तों को निभाते हैं: वे चुपचाप जाते हैं, ज़रूरत भर लेते हैं, और कभी घमंड नहीं करते, क्योंकि शहद जंगल का वरदान है, उनकी कोई जीत नहीं।\"","lang":"hi","body":"Dukhey was carried home — the tellings say on the back of a great crocodile, which is the best school-run in all of Bengali literature — with wealth enough to keep his mother forever. Dhona's shame was told in every market. And to this day the moule keep the terms: they enter quietly, take modestly, and never boast, for the honey is the forest's gift, not their conquest.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-bonbibi-dukhey.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.bonbibi-dukhey|h7","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","East & the Islands"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.bonbibi-dukhey-8":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.bonbibi-dukhey:8","title":"Read it in Hindi · Bonbibi, Lady of the Forest","text":"और बाघ बाघ ही रहता है — कहानी में न उसका कभी शिकार किया जाता है, न कोई उससे नफ़रत करता है। जंगल के लोग उसे बस आदर से याद करते हैं: उसी की वजह से घना जंगल घना बना रहता है, उसी की वजह से कोई अपनी ज़रूरत से ज़्यादा नहीं लेता, और उसी की वजह से सुंदरबन आज भी बचा हुआ है, जबकि इतने सारे जंगल ख़त्म हो गए। जिस जंगल की रखवाली हो, उसके पहरेदार का सचमुच रौबदार होना ज़रूरी भी है।","lang":"hi","body":"And the tiger stays the tiger — never hunted in the tale, never hated. The forest people's word for him is respect: he is why the deep forest stays deep, why no one takes too much, why the Sundarbans is still standing when so many forests are gone. A guarded forest needs its guard to be genuinely formidable.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-bonbibi-dukhey.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.bonbibi-dukhey|h8","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","East & the Islands"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.ilish-rain-0":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.ilish-rain:0","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Fish That Comes With the Rain","text":"बंगाल में मॉनसून कभी अकेला नहीं आता। जब आसमान भीगी स्लेट के रंग का हो जाता है और धूल पर पहली मोटी बूँदें गिरती हैं — 'ब्रिश्टी', बारिश के लिए बांग्ला शब्द, जिसे बंगाली ऐसे कहते हैं जैसे दूसरे लोग किसी मिठाई का नाम लेते हैं — तब कोलकाता से लेकर नदी किनारे बसे सबसे छोटे गाँव तक, हर किसी के मन में बस एक ही लज़ीज़ ख़याल आने लगता है: इलिश आ रही है।","lang":"hi","body":"In Bengal, the monsoon does not arrive alone. When the sky goes the colour of wet slate and the first fat drops hit the dust — brishti, the Bengali word for rain, a word Bengalis say the way other people say dessert — everyone from Kolkata to the smallest river village starts thinking the same delicious thought: the ilish are coming.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-ilish-rain.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.ilish-rain|h0","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","East & the Islands"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.ilish-rain-1":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.ilish-rain:1","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Fish That Comes With the Rain","text":"इलिश — जिसे अंग्रेज़ी में हिल्सा कहते हैं — समुद्र में रहने वाली एक रुपहली मछली है। लेकिन जब बारिश से नदियाँ उफान पर आती हैं, तो इलिश एक अनोखा काम करती है: वे हज़ारों की तादाद में चमकती हुई समंदर छोड़ देती हैं और नदियों के बहाव के ख़िलाफ़ ऊपर की ओर तैरने लगती हैं — हुगली में ऊपर, डेल्टा के चौड़े मुहानों से होते हुए — सीधे बंगाल के दिल तक, ठीक वैसे ही जैसे उनकी नस्ल तब से करती आ रही है जब बंगाल नाम की कोई जगह भी नहीं बनी थी।","lang":"hi","body":"The ilish — hilsa, in English — is a silver fish that lives in the sea. But when the rains swell the rivers, the ilish do an extraordinary thing: they leave the sea in their gleaming thousands and swim UP the rivers — up the Hooghly, up the wide mouths of the delta — against the current, into the very heart of Bengal, as their kind has done since before there was a Bengal to swim into.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-ilish-rain.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.ilish-rain|h1","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","East & the Islands"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.ilish-rain-2":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.ilish-rain:2","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Fish That Comes With the Rain","text":"मछुआरों के परिवार इन इशारों को किसी चिट्ठी की तरह पढ़ लेते हैं: बादलों का रंग, पानी से छूकर आती हवा की खुशबू, और वह दिन जब नदी का रुख़ ज़रा सा बदलता है। फिर सलेटी बारिश में नावें निकल पड़ती हैं — छोटी नावें, बड़े जाल, और पीढ़ियों की समझ — क्योंकि समंदर की इलिश अच्छी तो होती है, मगर मॉनसून की नदियों में खा-पीकर पुष्ट हुई नदी वाली इलिश ही वह है जिसके गीत कवियों ने गाए हैं।","lang":"hi","body":"The fishing families read the signs like a letter: the colour of the clouds, the smell of the wind off the water, the day the river turns just so. Then the boats go out in the grey rain — small boats, big nets, generations of knowing — because sea-ilish is good, but river-ilish, plumped on the monsoon rivers, is the one the poets meant.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-ilish-rain.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.ilish-rain|h2","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","East & the Islands"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.ilish-rain-3":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.ilish-rain:3","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Fish That Comes With the Rain","text":"और बाज़ारों में — अरे, इलिश के मौसम में बाज़ारों का क्या कहना! बर्फ़ पर सजी चाँदी जैसी कतारें। जौहरियों की तरह मछलियों पर झुककर उनके गलफड़ों की चमक परखते पारखी, और फ़ुटबॉल के विरोधी प्रशंसकों की तरह पद्मा बनाम हुगली पर बहस करते लोग। ऐसी दादियाँ-नानियाँ जो मछली चुनने के मामले में साठ साल से कम उम्र के किसी इंसान पर भरोसा नहीं करतीं। यह सिर्फ़ ख़रीदारी नहीं है; यह तो चमकदार छिलकों से सजा एक पूरा नाटक है।","lang":"hi","body":"And in the markets — oh, the markets in ilish season. The silver rows on the ice. The connoisseurs bending over them like jewellers, checking the gleam of a gill, arguing Padma-side versus Hooghly-side like rival football fans. Grandmothers who trust no one under sixty to choose a fish. It is not shopping; it is theatre with scales on.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-ilish-rain.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.ilish-rain|h3","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","East & the Islands"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.ilish-rain-4":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.ilish-rain:4","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Fish That Comes With the Rain","text":"मगर किसी चीज़ को हद से ज़्यादा चाहने का बंगाल को एक कड़वा सबक मिला है। सालों तक हर इलिश पकड़ते रहने की वजह से — जिसमें खोका इलिश, यानी नन्हे-मुन्ने बच्चे, और अंडे देने के लिए नदी के बहाव की ओर जाने वाली मां मछलियां भी शामिल थीं — नदियां खाली होने लगी थीं।","lang":"hi","body":"But Bengal has learned a hard lesson about loving something too hungrily. Years of catching every ilish — including the khoka ilish, the little young ones, and the mothers on their way upriver to lay eggs — began to empty the rivers.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-ilish-rain.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.ilish-rain|h4","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","East & the Islands"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.ilish-rain-5":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.ilish-rain:5","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Fish That Comes With the Rain","text":"इसलिए आज कुछ नियम बनाए गए हैं, जिनका अब और भी अच्छी तरह पालन होता है: सबसे नन्हीं इलिश को जाल में नहीं फंसाना, और उस समय मछली पकड़ने पर रोक लगाना जब मां मछलियां अंडे देने नदी में ऊपर की ओर जाती हैं। मछुआरों के परिवार थोड़ा बुदबुदाते हैं, पर बात मान लेते हैं और ज़्यादातर लोग इससे सहमत भी हैं — कोई भी ऐसी पीढ़ी नहीं बनना चाहता जिसने आखिरी मछली भी खाकर खत्म कर दी हो। सच तो यह है कि किसी मछली से सच्चा प्यार करने का मतलब यह भी होता है कि सही वक्त पर उसे अकेला छोड़ दिया जाए।","lang":"hi","body":"So today there are rules, kept better and better: no netting the tiniest ilish, rest periods when the mother fish run upriver to spawn. Fishing families grumble and comply and mostly agree — nobody wants to be the generation that ate the last one. Loving a fish properly, it turns out, includes leaving it alone at the right times.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-ilish-rain.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.ilish-rain|h5","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","East & the Islands"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.ilish-rain-6":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.ilish-rain:6","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Fish That Comes With the Rain","text":"और जब मौसम की पहली बढ़िया इलिश किसी घर की रसोई तक पहुंचती है — खिड़कियों पर बरसती मूसलाधार बारिश के बीच सरसों के साथ भाप में पकी हुई, या ढेर सारे भात के साथ कुरकुरी तली हुई — तो पूरे बंगाल को, कम से कम एक वक्त के खाने के लिए, पूरा सुकून मिल जाता है। सरहद पार बांग्लादेश में तो यह राष्ट्रीय मछली है, और किसकी नदियों की इलिश ज़्यादा बेहतर होती है, इस बात पर बहस छिड़ना अपने आप में एक पसंदीदा खेल जैसा है, जो हर शादी में खेला जाता है।","lang":"hi","body":"And when the season's first proper ilish reaches a family kitchen — steamed with mustard, or fried crisp with a mountain of rice while the rain hammers the windows — Bengal is, for one meal, entirely at peace. Across the border in Bangladesh it is the national fish, and the arguing over whose rivers make the better ilish is itself a beloved regional sport, played at every wedding.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-ilish-rain.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.ilish-rain|h6","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","East & the Islands"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-kh.dhyanchand-0":{"src":"passage:hi:story:kh.dhyanchand:0","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Wizard With the Stick","text":"\"यह एक सच्ची कहानी है — इतिहास, जो रिकॉर्ड की किताबें बताती हैं। क़रीब सौ साल पहले, ध्यानचंद नाम के एक नौजवान सिपाही भारतीय सेना के लिए हॉकी खेलते थे। वे सोलह साल की उम्र में झाँसी में फ़ौज में शामिल हुए थे, और अपनी ड्यूटी पूरी करने के बाद चाँदनी रात में अकेले अभ्यास किया करते थे, क्योंकि परेड ग्राउंड में कोई रोशनी नहीं थी और उनका मन रुकने को करता ही नहीं था।\"","lang":"hi","body":"This is a true story — itihaas, what the record books show. Around a hundred years ago, a young soldier named Dhyan Chand played hockey for the Indian army. He had joined at sixteen, in Jhansi, and after his duties were done he would practise alone, in the moonlight, because the parade ground had no lights and he could not bear to stop.","art":"art/story/sm/kh-dhyanchand.jpg","route":"#/story/kh.dhyanchand|h0","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Khel — India at Play"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-kh.dhyanchand-1":{"src":"passage:hi:story:kh.dhyanchand:1","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Wizard With the Stick","text":"\"जब भारत ओलंपिक खेलों में गया — 1928 में एम्सटर्डम, 1932 में लॉस एंजेलिस, 1936 में बर्लिन — तब दुनिया को पता चला कि उस सारी चाँदनी ने क्या कमाल रच दिया था। भारत ने हर एक बार स्वर्ण पदक जीता। तीन ओलंपिक, तीन स्वर्ण। 1932 के एक मैच में भारत ने मेज़बान देश अमेरिका को चौबीस के मुक़ाबले एक गोल से हराया। यह स्कोर पीढ़ियों तक रिकॉर्ड की किताबों में दर्ज रहा।\"","lang":"hi","body":"When India went to the Olympic Games — Amsterdam in 1928, Los Angeles in 1932, Berlin in 1936 — the world found out what all that moonlight had built. India won the gold medal every single time. Three Olympics, three golds. In one match in 1932, India beat the home team of the United States by twenty-four goals to one. That scoreline sat in the record books for generations.","art":"art/story/sm/kh-dhyanchand.jpg","route":"#/story/kh.dhyanchand|h1","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Khel — India at Play"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-kh.dhyanchand-2":{"src":"passage:hi:story:kh.dhyanchand:2","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Wizard With the Stick","text":"\"इस सब के केंद्र में ध्यानचंद थे, जो विपक्षी खिलाड़ियों के बीच से ऐसे फिसलते हुए निकल जाते थे मानो वे बस खड़े के खड़े रह गए हों, और गेंद उनकी स्टिक से चिपकी सी रहती थी। वे गोल ऐसे करते थे जैसे लोग बातों-बातों में नमस्ते कह देते हैं — अपने पूरे करियर में सैकड़ों गोल।\"","lang":"hi","body":"At the centre of it all was Dhyan Chand, gliding through defenders as if they were standing still, the ball stitched to his stick. He scored goals the way other people say hello — by the hundreds, across his career.","art":"art/story/sm/kh-dhyanchand.jpg","route":"#/story/kh.dhyanchand|h2","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Khel — India at Play"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-kh.dhyanchand-3":{"src":"passage:hi:story:kh.dhyanchand:3","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Wizard With the Stick","text":"\"और यहीं पर रिकॉर्ड ख़त्म होते हैं और कहानियाँ शुरू होती हैं — और इतिहास की एक कहानी ईमानदारी से बताती है कि सच क्या है और क़िस्सा क्या। लोग जो देख रहे थे उस पर उन्हें यक़ीन नहीं हो रहा था, इसलिए कहानियाँ बनने लगीं। कहा जाता है कि हॉलैंड में अधिकारियों ने उनकी स्टिक की जाँच की, यह देखने के लिए कि कहीं उसमें कोई चुंबक या गोंद तो नहीं छुपा है। कोई भी ऐसा दस्तावेज़ नहीं दिखा सकता जो यह साबित करे कि ऐसा हुआ था। लेकिन यह बात कि लोगों के लिए किसी जादुई स्टिक पर यक़ीन करना ज़्यादा आसान था बजाय इसके कि कोई इंसान इतना लाजवाब खेल सकता है — यह अपने आप में ही एक बड़ा सच बयाँ करती है।\"","lang":"hi","body":"And here is where the record ends and the stories begin — and an itihaas story tells you honestly which is which. People could not believe what they were seeing, so tales grew. In Holland, it is said, officials examined his stick to see if there was a magnet or glue hidden inside it. Nobody can show you a document proving that happened. But the fact that people found it easier to believe in a magic stick than in one man being that good — that tells you something true all by itself.","art":"art/story/sm/kh-dhyanchand.jpg","route":"#/story/kh.dhyanchand|h3","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Khel — India at Play"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-kh.dhyanchand-4":{"src":"passage:hi:story:kh.dhyanchand:4","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Wizard With the Stick","text":"\"1936 में बर्लिन में, जर्मनी के ख़िलाफ़ फ़ाइनल में, जहाँ पूरा स्टेडियम उनके ख़िलाफ़ खचाखच भरा था, भारत आठ के मुक़ाबले एक गोल से जीत गया। यह कोई मनगढ़ंत क़िस्सा नहीं है — यह किताबों में दर्ज है। यह तीसरा स्वर्ण पदक था, और इसने ध्यानचंद को कुछ ऐसा बना दिया जो विरले ही देखने को मिलता है: एक ऐसा खिलाड़ी जिसकी कहानियाँ दूसरे देश भी सुनाया करते थे।\"","lang":"hi","body":"In Berlin in 1936, in the final against Germany with the stands packed against them, India won eight goals to one. That one is no legend — it is in the books. It was the third gold, and it made Dhyan Chand something rare: an athlete other countries told stories about.","art":"art/story/sm/kh-dhyanchand.jpg","route":"#/story/kh.dhyanchand|h4","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Khel — India at Play"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-kh.kapil83-0":{"src":"passage:hi:story:kh.kapil83:0","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Cup Nobody Expected","text":"1983 की गर्मियों में, भारत क्रिकेट विश्व कप खेलने इंग्लैंड गया, और किसी ने भी इस बात पर खास ध्यान नहीं दिया। इससे पहले हुए दो विश्व कप में भारत ने सिर्फ एक ही मैच जीता था। सट्टा लगाने वाले भारत के ख़िलाफ़ छाछठ पर एक का दांव लगा रहे थे। ताकतवर वेस्ट इंडीज़ ने अब तक के दोनों विश्व कप जीते थे, और हर किसी को यकीन था कि इस बार भी वही जीतेंगे।","lang":"hi","body":"In the summer of 1983, India went to England for the cricket World Cup, and almost nobody noticed. India had won one single match in the two World Cups before. The bookmakers offered sixty-six to one against them. The mighty West Indies had won both cups ever played, and everyone knew they would win this one too.","art":"art/story/sm/kh-kapil83.jpg","route":"#/story/kh.kapil83|h0","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Khel — India at Play"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-kh.kapil83-1":{"src":"passage:hi:story:kh.kapil83:1","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Cup Nobody Expected","text":"भारत के कप्तान थे चौबीस साल के कपिल देव, एक ऐसे परिवार से जो कई मुश्किल भरे सफ़र तय करके उत्तर भारत में आ बसा था—एक ऐसे तेज़ गेंदबाज़ जो कड़कती बिजली की तरह गेंद को मारते थे और जिन्होंने हार के सारे अनुमानों को मानने से साफ़ इनकार कर दिया था। पूरी टीम उन्हें 'हरियाणा हरिकेन' कहती थी।","lang":"hi","body":"India’s captain was Kapil Dev, twenty-four years old, from a family that had settled in the north after hard journeys of its own — a fast bowler who hit the ball like a thunderclap and refused, completely, to believe the odds. The team called him the Haryana Hurricane.","art":"art/story/sm/kh-kapil83.jpg","route":"#/story/kh.kapil83|h1","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Khel — India at Play"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-kh.kapil83-2":{"src":"passage:hi:story:kh.kapil83:2","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Cup Nobody Expected","text":"ज़िम्बाब्वे के ख़िलाफ़ भारत की पारी लड़खड़ा गई और सत्रह रन पर पाँच विकेट गिर गए—एक बहुत बड़ा संकट! कपिल मैदान पर उतरे और उन्होंने इतिहास की सबसे महान पारियों में से एक खेली: नाबाद 175 रन, सोलह चौके और छह छक्के। और इस रिकॉर्ड की एक अजीब और अनोखी बात यह भी है: उस दिन टेलीविज़न के कैमरामैन हड़ताल पर थे। उस पारी की एक भी गेंद कैमरे में रिकॉर्ड नहीं हुई। विश्व कप को बचाने वाली वह पारी अब सिर्फ स्कोरबुक में और उस छोटे से मैदान पर मौजूद लोगों की यादों में ही ज़िंदा है।","lang":"hi","body":"Against Zimbabwe, India collapsed to seventeen runs for five wickets — a disaster. Kapil walked in and played one of the greatest innings ever: 175 not out, sixteen fours, six sixes. And here is the strange, wonderful footnote the record keeps: the television cameras were on strike that day. Not one ball of it was filmed. The innings that saved the World Cup exists only in the scorebook and in the memories of the people on that small ground.","art":"art/story/sm/kh-kapil83.jpg","route":"#/story/kh.kapil83|h2","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Khel — India at Play"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-kh.kapil83-3":{"src":"passage:hi:story:kh.kapil83:3","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Cup Nobody Expected","text":"पच्चीस जून, लॉर्ड्स का मैदान और फाइनल मैच। भारत ने पहले बल्लेबाज़ी की और पूरी टीम 183 रनों पर सिमट गई—सबका यही मानना था कि यह बहुत छोटा, बेहद छोटा स्कोर था। वेस्ट इंडीज़ ने लक्ष्य का पीछा करना शुरू किया, और दुनिया के सबसे ख़ौफ़नाक बल्लेबाज़, विव रिचर्ड्स, ऐसे चौके जड़ने लगे मानो यह खेल उन्हें उबाऊ लग रहा हो।","lang":"hi","body":"The final, at Lord’s, June the twenty-fifth. India batted first and were bowled out for 183 — a small total, far too small, everyone agreed. The West Indies began their chase, and the most feared batsman on Earth, Viv Richards, started hitting boundaries as if the game bored him.","art":"art/story/sm/kh-kapil83.jpg","route":"#/story/kh.kapil83|h3","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Khel — India at Play"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-kh.kapil83-4":{"src":"passage:hi:story:kh.kapil83:4","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Cup Nobody Expected","text":"उस कैच के बाद, अजेय मानी जाने वाली वेस्ट इंडीज़ की टीम ताश के पत्तों की तरह बिखर गई—पूरी टीम 140 रन पर आउट हो गई। भारत तैंतालीस रनों से विश्व कप जीत चुका था, और नीचे खड़ी हैरान तथा ख़ुशी से झूमती भारतीयों की भीड़ के नारों के बीच, कपिल ने लॉर्ड्स की बालकनी में सोने की ट्रॉफी हवा में उठा दी।","lang":"hi","body":"After that catch, the invincible West Indies crumbled — all out for 140. India had won the World Cup by forty-three runs, and Kapil lifted the golden trophy on the Lord’s balcony while a crowd of disbelieving, delighted Indians roared below.","art":"art/story/sm/kh-kapil83.jpg","route":"#/story/kh.kapil83|h4","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Khel — India at Play"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-kh.sachin-0":{"src":"passage:hi:story:kh.sachin:0","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Boy With the Ball in a Sock","text":"1980 के दशक में, बंबई के बांद्रा की एक कॉलोनी में, घुंघराले बालों वाला एक छोटा लड़का रस्सी से मोज़े में लटकी क्रिकेट की गेंद पर बैटिंग की प्रैक्टिस करता था — क्योंकि मोज़े वाली गेंद बार-बार झूलकर वापस आती है, और उसे किसी बॉलर की ज़रूरत नहीं पड़ती। उसका नाम सचिन तेंदुलकर था, और वह घंटों तक ऐसा करता रहता था। उसके घरवाले कभी-कभी सोचते थे कि क्या यह कभी रुकेगा भी।","lang":"hi","body":"In a colony in Bandra, Bombay, in the 1980s, a small boy with curly hair practised batting against a cricket ball hung inside a sock from a rope — because a ball in a sock swings back at you, again and again, and never needs a bowler. His name was Sachin Tendulkar, and he could do this for hours. His family sometimes wondered if he would ever stop.","art":"art/story/sm/kh-sachin.jpg","route":"#/story/kh.sachin|h0","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Khel — India at Play"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-kh.sachin-1":{"src":"passage:hi:story:kh.sachin:1","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Boy With the Ball in a Sock","text":"उनके कोच, रमाकांत आचरेकर का एक मशहूर तरीका था। प्रैक्टिस के आखिर में वे स्टंप्स के ऊपर एक रुपये का सिक्का टिका देते थे। जो भी बॉलर सचिन को आउट करता, सिक्का उसका हो जाता। और अगर कोई आउट न कर पाता, तो सिक्का सचिन का हो जाता। सचिन ने वे तेरह सिक्के ज़िंदगी भर संभाल कर रखे, और कहा कि वे उनके सबसे अनमोल इनामों में से थे।","lang":"hi","body":"His coach, Ramakant Achrekar, had a famous trick. At the end of practice he would balance a one-rupee coin on the stumps. Any bowler who got Sachin out won the coin. If nobody could, Sachin kept it. He kept thirteen of those coins all his life, and said they were among his most precious prizes.","art":"art/story/sm/kh-sachin.jpg","route":"#/story/kh.sachin|h1","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Khel — India at Play"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-kh.sachin-2":{"src":"passage:hi:story:kh.sachin:2","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Boy With the Ball in a Sock","text":"सोलह साल की उम्र में — सिर्फ़ सोलह! — वह पाकिस्तान के ख़तरनाक तेज़ गेंदबाज़ों के सामने भारत के लिए खेला, चोट खाई, ख़ून बहा, पर मैदान छोड़ने से साफ़ इनकार कर दिया। पूरे भारत ने देखा कि बड़ों के खेल में एक लड़का बच्चा बनकर पीछे हटने को तैयार नहीं था, और उस दिन एक ऐसा सिलसिला शुरू हुआ जो चौबीस साल तक नहीं थमा।","lang":"hi","body":"At sixteen — sixteen! — he played for India against the fierce fast bowlers of Pakistan, took a blow, bled, and refused to leave the field. India watched a boy in a man’s game refuse to be a boy about it, and something began that day that did not stop for twenty-four years.","art":"art/story/sm/kh-sachin.jpg","route":"#/story/kh.sachin|h2","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Khel — India at Play"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-kh.sachin-3":{"src":"passage:hi:story:kh.sachin:3","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Boy With the Ball in a Sock","text":"उन्होंने जो रिकॉर्ड बनाए, वे किसी छपाई की भूल जैसे लगते हैं। सौ अंतरराष्ट्रीय शतक — वहाँ तक कोई दूसरा कभी नहीं पहुँच पाया। चौंतीस हज़ार से भी ज़्यादा अंतरराष्ट्रीय रन। दो सौ टेस्ट मैच। 1990 के दशक में, जब भारतीय क्रिकेट के मुश्किल दिन चल रहे थे, तब पूरे देश का मिज़ाज इस बात से तय होता था कि क्या सचिन अभी क्रीज़ पर खेल रहे हैं।","lang":"hi","body":"The numbers he left behind read like misprints. One hundred international centuries — no one else has reached that. More than thirty-four thousand international runs. Two hundred Test matches. Through the 1990s, when Indian cricket had hard days, a whole country planned its mood around whether Sachin was still batting.","art":"art/story/sm/kh-sachin.jpg","route":"#/story/kh.sachin|h3","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Khel — India at Play"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-kh.sachin-4":{"src":"passage:hi:story:kh.sachin:4","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Boy With the Ball in a Sock","text":"बस एक ही इनाम था जो हाथ से छूटता जा रहा था — वर्ल्ड कप। आखिरकार 2011 में, अपनी छठी कोशिश में, भारत ने अपनी ही ज़मीन पर, यानी सचिन की अपनी बंबई में उसे जीत लिया। उनकी टीम के युवा खिलाड़ियों ने उन्हें अपने कंधों पर उठा लिया और पूरे मैदान में घुमाया। उनमें से एक, विराट कोहली ने उस रात कहा था कि सचिन ने इक्कीस साल तक पूरे देश का बोझ उठाया है, इसलिए अब उन्हें उठाने की बारी हमारी थी। भारत तब से उस बात को दोहराता आ रहा है।","lang":"hi","body":"The one prize that kept escaping was the World Cup — until 2011, his sixth try, when India finally won it at home, in his own Bombay. His young teammates lifted him onto their shoulders and carried him around the ground. One of them, Virat Kohli, said that night that Sachin had carried the burden of the nation for twenty-one years, so it was time to carry him. India has been repeating that sentence ever since.","art":"art/story/sm/kh-sachin.jpg","route":"#/story/kh.sachin|h4","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Khel — India at Play"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-kh.anand-0":{"src":"passage:hi:story:kh.anand:0","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Lightning Kid","text":"शतरंज का जन्म भारत में हुआ था — इसका पुराना रूप, चतुरंग, करीब चौदह सौ साल पहले यहीं खेला जाता था, इससे पहले कि वह पूरी दुनिया का चक्कर लगाकर एक बदले हुए रूप में घर लौटे। लेकिन 1980 के दशक तक, शतरंज के बड़े-बड़े महारथी बहुत दूर थे, और भारत के पास एक भी ग्रैंडमास्टर नहीं था। मद्रास में — जिसे आज चेन्नई कहा जाता है — छह साल का एक लड़का, विश्वनाथन आनंद, अपनी माँ से शतरंज की चालें सीख रहा था।","lang":"hi","body":"Chess was born in India — its ancestor, chaturanga, was played here some fourteen centuries ago before travelling the whole world and coming home changed. But by the 1980s, the world’s great chess powers were far away, and India did not have one single grandmaster. In Madras — the city now called Chennai — a boy named Viswanathan Anand was learning the moves from his mother, at six.","art":"art/story/sm/kh-anand.jpg","route":"#/story/kh.anand|h0","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Khel — India at Play"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-kh.anand-1":{"src":"passage:hi:story:kh.anand:1","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Lightning Kid","text":"शतरंज क्लब में सबने उसे एक नाम दिया: लाइटनिंग किड। वह इतनी तेज़ी से खेलता था कि बड़े-बड़े उस्ताद भी चकरा जाते थे — एक नज़र डाली, मोहरा चला, और खेल ख़त्म — लापरवाही से नहीं, बल्कि इसलिए क्योंकि उसे चालें दूसरों से पहले ही दिख जाती थीं। 1987 में वह वर्ल्ड जूनियर चैंपियन बना, और 1988 में, अठारह साल की उम्र में, वह भारत के इतिहास का पहला ग्रैंडमास्टर बन गया।","lang":"hi","body":"At the chess club they gave him a nickname: the Lightning Kid. He played at a speed that unsettled grown masters — glance, move, done — not out of carelessness but because he simply saw it faster. In 1987 he became world junior champion, and in 1988, at eighteen, he became the first grandmaster in the history of India.","art":"art/story/sm/kh-anand.jpg","route":"#/story/kh.anand|h1","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Khel — India at Play"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-kh.anand-2":{"src":"passage:hi:story:kh.anand:2","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Lightning Kid","text":"पहला होना एक अजीब काम होता है। उससे पहले कोई भी भारतीय इस रास्ते पर नहीं चला था, न कोई नक्शा था, और सबसे तगड़े खिलाड़ी और स्कूल सात समंदर पार थे। हर टूर्नामेंट का मतलब था अकेले दुनिया के दूसरे कोने तक जाना, और उन लोगों से मुक़ाबला करना जो शतरंज के बड़े-बड़े गढ़ों में पले-बढ़े थे। फिर भी वह आगे बढ़ता रहा, साल-दर-साल, एक के बाद एक मैच।","lang":"hi","body":"Being first is a strange job. There was no Indian who had walked this road ahead of him, no map, and the strongest players and schools were continents away. Every tournament meant travelling alone to the other side of the world to play people raised in the game’s great capitals. He kept going anyway, year after year, match after match.","art":"art/story/sm/kh-anand.jpg","route":"#/story/kh.anand|h2","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Khel — India at Play"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-kh.anand-3":{"src":"passage:hi:story:kh.anand:3","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Lightning Kid","text":"और वह चढ़ते-चढ़ते शिखर तक पहुँच गया। साल 2000 में वर्ल्ड चैंपियन बना। फिर, इस खेल के सबसे कठिन रूप में, 2007 में वह दोबारा चैंपियन बना — और 2008, 2010 और 2012 के मुक़ाबलों में उसने दुनिया के सबसे बेहतरीन खिलाड़ियों के ख़िलाफ़ अपना ख़िताब बचाए रखा। हर मैच हफ़्तों लंबा, हर एक किसी घेराबंदी जैसा। पाँच विश्व ख़िताब, जो एक दशक से भी ज़्यादा समय तक उसके नाम रहे।","lang":"hi","body":"And he climbed all the way. World champion in 2000. Then, in the toughest form of the game, champion again in 2007 — and he defended the title in matches in 2008, 2010 and 2012, against the best players alive, each match weeks long, each one a siege. Five world titles, held across more than a decade.","art":"art/story/sm/kh-anand.jpg","route":"#/story/kh.anand|h3","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Khel — India at Play"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-kh.anand-4":{"src":"passage:hi:story:kh.anand:4","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Lightning Kid","text":"मगर इस कहानी का असली अंत कोई ट्रॉफी नहीं है। जब आनंद भारत के पहले ग्रैंडमास्टर बने, तब वे अकेले थे। आज भारत में अस्सी से भी ज़्यादा ग्रैंडमास्टर हैं, जिनमें से कई चेन्नई से हैं, और कई ऐसे बच्चे हैं जिन्होंने खेलना इसलिए शुरू किया क्योंकि उनके अपने शहर के एक शांत, फुर्तीले और मुस्कुराते हुए इंसान ने यह कर दिखाया था। उन्हीं में से एक, सालों बाद, अठारह की उम्र में ख़ुद वर्ल्ड चैंपियन बनेगा — लेकिन वह इस ताक पर रखी सबसे आख़िरी कहानी है।","lang":"hi","body":"But the real ending of this story is not a trophy. When Anand became India’s first grandmaster, he was the only one. Today India has more than eighty, many of them from Chennai, many of them children who started because a calm, fast, smiling man from their own city had shown it could be done. One of them, years later, would take the world title himself at eighteen — but that is the last story on this shelf.","art":"art/story/sm/kh-anand.jpg","route":"#/story/kh.anand|h4","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Khel — India at Play"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-kh.marykom-0":{"src":"passage:hi:story:kh.marykom:0","title":"Read it in Hindi · Six Crowns from Kangathei","text":"\"कांगथई भारत के उत्तर-पूर्व के ख़ूबसूरत पहाड़ी इलाके मणिपुर का एक छोटा सा गाँव है, और मैरी कॉम वहीं धान के खेतों में अपने माता-पिता का हाथ बँटाते हुए बड़ी हुईं। 1998 में मणिपुर के एक मुक्केबाज़ डिंगको सिंह ने एशियाई खेलों में स्वर्ण पदक जीता, और पूरा राज्य ख़ुशी से झूम उठा। यह देखकर खेतों में काम करने वाली एक किशोरी ने मन ही मन तय कर लिया कि बॉक्सिंग ही उसकी मंज़िल है।\"","lang":"hi","body":"Kangathei is a small village in Manipur, in the beautiful hill country of India’s northeast, and Mary Kom grew up there helping her parents in the rice fields. In 1998, a boxer from Manipur named Dingko Singh won gold at the Asian Games, and the whole state lit up. Watching that, a teenage girl from the fields decided, privately, that boxing was hers.","art":"art/story/sm/kh-marykom.jpg","route":"#/story/kh.marykom|h0","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Khel — India at Play"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-kh.marykom-1":{"src":"passage:hi:story:kh.marykom:1","title":"Read it in Hindi · Six Crowns from Kangathei","text":"\"मन ही मन इसलिए, क्योंकि उनके गाँव की लड़कियों से मुक्केबाज़ी की उम्मीद नहीं की जाती थी, और उनके पिता को डर लगता था—चोटों का, पड़ोसियों का, हर बात का। इसलिए वे उन्हें बताए बिना अभ्यास करती रहीं, पैदल चलकर जिम जातीं, पैंतरे सीखतीं, मुक्के बरसाना सीखतीं। फिर उन्होंने राज्य स्तरीय चैंपियनशिप जीती, और अख़बार में उनकी तस्वीर छपी, और तब जाकर उनके पिता को पता चला कि उनकी बेटी एक मुक्केबाज़ है।\"","lang":"hi","body":"Privately, because girls from her village were not supposed to box, and her father feared it — the injuries, the neighbours, all of it. So she trained without telling him, walking to the gym, learning to move, learning to hit. Then she won a state championship, and her photograph appeared in the newspaper, and that is how her father found out his daughter was a boxer.","art":"art/story/sm/kh-marykom.jpg","route":"#/story/kh.marykom|h1","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Khel — India at Play"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-kh.marykom-2":{"src":"passage:hi:story:kh.marykom:2","title":"Read it in Hindi · Six Crowns from Kangathei","text":"\"फिर जो जीत का सिलसिला शुरू हुआ, वह रुका ही नहीं। 2002 में विश्व चैंपियनशिप का स्वर्ण पदक। फिर 2005 में। फिर 2006 में। हर महाद्वीप से मुक्केबाज़ आए, और बार-बार कांगथई की वही दुबली-पतली, फुर्तीली महिला अपने मुक्कों की बिजली से जीतती रही।\"","lang":"hi","body":"Then the winning started and would not stop. World championship gold in 2002. Again in 2005. Again in 2006. Boxers from every continent, and again and again the small, fast woman from Kangathei with the thunder in her hands.","art":"art/story/sm/kh-marykom.jpg","route":"#/story/kh.marykom|h2","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Khel — India at Play"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-kh.marykom-3":{"src":"passage:hi:story:kh.marykom:3","title":"Read it in Hindi · Six Crowns from Kangathei","text":"\"2007 में वे माँ बनीं—दो जुड़वाँ बेटों की—और दुनिया भर के लोगों ने मान लिया कि अब उनकी बॉक्सिंग ख़त्म हो गई, क्योंकि उन दिनों दुनिया यही सोचती थी। एक साल बाद उन्होंने वापसी की और फिर से विश्व चैंपियनशिप जीत ली। लोग उन्हें 'शानदार मैरी' यानी 'मैग्निफ़िसेंट मैरी' पुकारने लगे। 2010 में वे फिर जीतीं। और 2018 में, अपने पहले ख़िताब के सोलह साल बाद, उन्होंने अपना छठा ख़िताब जीता—इस खेल के इतिहास में किसी भी महिला से ज़्यादा विश्व ख़िताब।\"","lang":"hi","body":"In 2007 she became a mother — of twin boys — and much of the world assumed her boxing was finished, because that is what the world assumed in those days. One year later she came back and won the world championship again. They started calling her Magnificent Mary. She won again in 2010. And in 2018, sixteen years after her first crown, she won her sixth — more world titles than any woman in the history of the sport.","art":"art/story/sm/kh-marykom.jpg","route":"#/story/kh.marykom|h3","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Khel — India at Play"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-kh.marykom-4":{"src":"passage:hi:story:kh.marykom:4","title":"Read it in Hindi · Six Crowns from Kangathei","text":"\"2012 में, जब आख़िरकार महिला बॉक्सिंग को ओलंपिक में जगह मिली, तो वे लंदन में मौजूद थीं, उस मुक़ाबले में भारत की इकलौती महिला मुक्केबाज़, और उन्होंने लड़कर भारत के लिए कांस्य पदक जीता। जो लड़की कभी छुप-छुपकर अभ्यास करती थी, अब पूरा देश उसके लिए तालियाँ पीट रहा था और नारे लगा रहा था।\"","lang":"hi","body":"In 2012, when women’s boxing entered the Olympics at last, she was there in London, the only Indian woman in the draw, and fought her way to a bronze medal for India. A girl who had trained in secret now had a whole country making noise for her.","art":"art/story/sm/kh-marykom.jpg","route":"#/story/kh.marykom|h4","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Khel — India at Play"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-kh.sindhu-0":{"src":"passage:hi:story:kh.sindhu:0","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Girl Who Woke Before the Birds","text":"पी. वी. सिंधु का जन्म हैदराबाद में खेल-कूद से भरे एक घर में हुआ था — उनके माता-पिता दोनों भारत के लिए वॉलीबॉल खेलते थे। लेकिन 2001 में, जब वह छह साल की थीं, पुलेला गोपीचंद नाम के एक भारतीय ने ऑल इंग्लैंड बैडमिंटन ख़िताब जीता, जो इस खेल के सबसे बड़े सम्मानों में से एक है, और उस नन्हीं बच्ची ने वॉलीबॉल की जगह रैकेट को चुन लिया।","lang":"hi","body":"P. V. Sindhu was born in Hyderabad into a house full of sport — both her parents played volleyball for India. But in 2001, when she was six, an Indian named Pullela Gopichand won the All England badminton title, one of the sport’s great crowns, and the little girl chose the racquet over the volleyball.","art":"art/story/sm/kh-sindhu.jpg","route":"#/story/kh.sindhu|h0","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Khel — India at Play"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-kh.sindhu-1":{"src":"passage:hi:story:kh.sindhu:1","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Girl Who Woke Before the Birds","text":"गोपीचंद ने आगे चलकर एक ट्रेनिंग अकादमी खोली — शहर के दूसरे कोने पर। आठ साल की उम्र से ही सिंधु सूरज निकलने से पहले उठ जाती थीं, आने-जाने में दर्जनों किलोमीटर का सफ़र करती थीं, स्कूल से पहले सुबह का अभ्यास और स्कूल के बाद शाम का अभ्यास। कभी हिसाब लगाकर देखिए: सालों-साल की ऐसी सुबहें, जिनमें से हर एक सुबह को उन्होंने तब चुना जब बाकी पूरा शहर सो रहा था।","lang":"hi","body":"Gopichand went on to open a training academy — on the far side of the city. From the age of eight, Sindhu was up before dawn, travelling tens of kilometres there and back, morning practice before school, evening practice after. Do the sums sometime: years of mornings, every one of them chosen while the rest of the city slept.","art":"art/story/sm/kh-sindhu.jpg","route":"#/story/kh.sindhu|h1","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Khel — India at Play"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-kh.sindhu-2":{"src":"passage:hi:story:kh.sindhu:2","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Girl Who Woke Before the Birds","text":"2016 के रियो ओलंपिक में, इक्कीस साल की उम्र में, वह संघर्ष करते हुए फ़ाइनल तक पहुँचीं — ओलंपिक रजत पदक जीतने वाली पहली भारतीय महिला। पूरा देश उन्हें देखने के लिए रात भर जागा रहा। लेकिन रजत भी एक अजीब पदक है: यह चमकता तो है, पर उस एक मैच की फुसफुसाहट भी सुनाता रहता है जिसे आप जीत नहीं पाए।","lang":"hi","body":"At the Rio Olympics in 2016, at twenty-one, she fought her way to the final — the first Indian woman ever to win an Olympic silver. The whole country stayed up to watch. But silver is a strange medal: it glitters, and it whispers about the one match you did not win.","art":"art/story/sm/kh-sindhu.jpg","route":"#/story/kh.sindhu|h2","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Khel — India at Play"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-kh.sindhu-3":{"src":"passage:hi:story:kh.sindhu:3","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Girl Who Woke Before the Birds","text":"उन्होंने 2019 में बासेल में इसका जवाब दिया। विश्व चैंपियनशिप के फ़ाइनल में उन्होंने अपनी ज़िंदगी का सबसे यादगार मैच खेला, इतनी तेज़ और इतनी ज़ोरदार कि दुनिया की सबसे बेहतरीन खिलाड़ियों में से एक भी उनके सामने बमुश्किल अंक बना सकी। विश्व चैंपियन — बैडमिंटन में भारत की पहली, अब तक की सबसे पहली। और फिर टोक्यो में उन्होंने दोबारा ओलंपिक पदक जीता, और दो पदक जीतने वाली पहली भारतीय महिला बन गईं।","lang":"hi","body":"She answered in Basel, in 2019. In the final of the world championships she played the match of her life, so fast and so fierce that one of the best players on Earth could barely score against her. World champion — the first from India in badminton, ever. And in Tokyo she won an Olympic medal again, becoming the first Indian woman with two.","art":"art/story/sm/kh-sindhu.jpg","route":"#/story/kh.sindhu|h3","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Khel — India at Play"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-kh.sindhu-4":{"src":"passage:hi:story:kh.sindhu:4","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Girl Who Woke Before the Birds","text":"उन्हें खेलते देखिए और आपको दिखाई देगा: उनकी पहुँच, उनकी छलांग, और दरवाज़ा ज़ोर से बंद होने जैसी आवाज़ वाला स्मैश। लेकिन जो भी उनकी कहानी जानता है, उसे इसके पीछे कुछ और दिखता है — हैदराबाद के अंधेरे में कार में बैठी एक छोटी बच्ची, जो अभ्यास के रास्ते पर आधी दूर पहुँच चुकी है जबकि परिंदे अभी सो ही रहे हैं।","lang":"hi","body":"Watch her play and you see it: the reach, the leap, the smash that sounds like a door slamming. But everyone who knows her story sees something else behind it — a small girl in a car in the Hyderabad dark, halfway to practice while the birds are still asleep.","art":"art/story/sm/kh-sindhu.jpg","route":"#/story/kh.sindhu|h4","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Khel — India at Play"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-kh.neeraj-0":{"src":"passage:hi:story:kh.neeraj:0","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Spear From Khandra","text":"हरियाणा में पानीपत के पास खांद्रा नाम का एक किसान गाँव है—गेहूँ के खेत, भैंसें, और एक ही घर में रहता एक बड़ा संयुक्त परिवार। नीरज चोपड़ा उसी परिवार का एक हँसमुख और गोल-मटोल सा बच्चा था। जब वह लगभग तेरह साल का था, तो थोड़ी कसरत कराने के लिए उसके चाचाजी उसे शहर के स्टेडियम ले गए। बस, यही पूरी शुरुआत थी: न कोई भविष्यवाणी, न कोई प्रतिभा तलाशने वाला। एक चाचाजी, और एक लड़का जिसे दौड़-भाग की ज़रूरत थी।","lang":"hi","body":"Khandra is a farming village near Panipat, in Haryana — wheat fields, buffaloes, a big joint family in one house. Neeraj Chopra was the cheerful, roundish kid of that family, and when he was about thirteen his uncle marched him to the stadium in town to get some exercise. That is the whole beginning: no prophecy, no talent scout. An uncle, and a boy who needed a run.","art":"art/story/sm/kh-neeraj.jpg","route":"#/story/kh.neeraj|h0","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Khel — India at Play"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-kh.neeraj-1":{"src":"passage:hi:story:kh.neeraj:1","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Spear From Khandra","text":"स्टेडियम में उसने भाला फेंकने वालों को देखा—और बस, बात बन गई। एक ऐसा पल होता है जब भाला फेंकने वाले के हाथ से छूटकर हवा में ऐसे ठहर सा जाता है मानो कभी नीचे आएगा ही नहीं, और नीरज वह पल अपने लिए चाहता था। वह इसमें कमाल का निकला! साल 2016 की वर्ल्ड जूनियर चैंपियनशिप में उसने 86.48 मीटर भाला फेंका—अपनी उम्र के खिलाड़ियों के लिए एक नया विश्व रिकॉर्ड। खांद्रा के उस लड़के के नाम अब एक विश्व रिकॉर्ड था।","lang":"hi","body":"At the stadium he saw the javelin throwers — and that was that. There is a moment when a spear leaves a thrower’s hand and hangs in the air as if it may never come down, and Neeraj wanted that moment for himself. He turned out to be astonishing at it. At the world junior championships in 2016 he threw 86.48 metres — a world record for his age group. The boy from Khandra held a world record.","art":"art/story/sm/kh-neeraj.jpg","route":"#/story/kh.neeraj|h1","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Khel — India at Play"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-kh.neeraj-2":{"src":"passage:hi:story:kh.neeraj:2","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Spear From Khandra","text":"भाला फेंक के साथ एक ख़ास बात यह थी: एथलेटिक्स में भारत ने कभी कोई ओलंपिक स्वर्ण पदक नहीं जीता था। सौ से भी ज़्यादा सालों के खेलों के इतिहास में एक भी नहीं—दौड़ने, कूदने और फेंकने के जिन खेलों को दुनिया का हर बच्चा खेलता है, उनमें पदक तालिका पर भारत के नाम के आगे शून्य लिखा था। बेहतरीन भारतीय खिलाड़ियों की पूरी-की-पूरी पीढ़ियाँ चौथे नंबर पर रहीं, या पदक के बेहद क़रीब पहुँचकर घर लौट गईं।","lang":"hi","body":"Here is the thing about the javelin: India had never won an Olympic gold medal in athletics. Not one, in more than a century of Games — in the sports of running, jumping and throwing that every child on Earth plays, the medal table by India’s name said zero. Whole generations of brilliant Indian athletes had come fourth, or close, and gone home.","art":"art/story/sm/kh-neeraj.jpg","route":"#/story/kh.neeraj|h2","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Khel — India at Play"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-kh.neeraj-3":{"src":"passage:hi:story:kh.neeraj:3","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Spear From Khandra","text":"टोक्यो, 7 अगस्त 2021—टले हुए ओलंपिक, जो एक साल की देरी से हो रहे थे। तेईस साल का नीरज दुनिया के सबसे बेहतरीन खिलाड़ियों के ख़िलाफ़ फ़ाइनल में उतरा। उसका पहला थ्रो 87.03 मीटर गया और वह सबसे आगे निकल गया। उसका दूसरा थ्रो 87.58 मीटर पहुँचा। फिर बाक़ी पूरी शाम उसे बस खड़े होकर देखना था, जबकि दुनिया के ग्यारह सबसे ताक़तवर खिलाड़ी बारी-बारी से उससे आगे निकलने की कोशिश कर रहे थे।","lang":"hi","body":"Tokyo, the seventh of August, 2021 — the postponed Olympics, held a year late. Neeraj, twenty-three, walked into the final against the best throwers alive. His first throw went 87.03 metres and led the field. His second went 87.58. Then he had to stand and watch, for the rest of the evening, while eleven of the world’s strongest men took turns trying to pass it.","art":"art/story/sm/kh-neeraj.jpg","route":"#/story/kh.neeraj|h3","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Khel — India at Play"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-kh.neeraj-4":{"src":"passage:hi:story:kh.neeraj:4","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Spear From Khandra","text":"कोई भी उससे आगे नहीं निकल सका। खांद्रा का वह भाला पूरी दुनिया से आगे निकल चुका था। नीरज चोपड़ा पोडियम की सबसे ऊँची सीढ़ी पर खड़े हुए, राष्ट्रगान बजा, और एक सौ बीस साल का इंतज़ार ख़त्म हो गया। आने वाले सालों में वे विश्व चैंपियन भी बने—और एक और प्यारी बात हुई: उनका सबसे बड़ा प्रतिद्वंद्वी, पाकिस्तान का एक भाला फेंक खिलाड़ी, उनका बहुत अच्छा दोस्त बन गया; दोनों परिवार सरहद के दोनों तरफ़ से दोनों लड़कों का हौसला बढ़ाते। रिकॉर्ड की किताबों में पदक दर्ज हैं; तस्वीरों में दोस्ती सँभली हुई है।","lang":"hi","body":"Nobody could. The spear from Khandra had flown further than the whole world. Neeraj Chopra stood on the top step, the anthem played, and a hundred-and-twenty-year wait ended. In the years after, he became world champion too — and one more lovely thing: his warmest rival, a thrower from Pakistan, became one of his good friends, their two families cheering both boys across the border. The record books hold the medals; the photographs hold the friendship.","art":"art/story/sm/kh-neeraj.jpg","route":"#/story/kh.neeraj|h4","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Khel — India at Play"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-kh.avani-0":{"src":"passage:hi:story:kh.avani:0","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Stillest Person in the Room","text":"अवनी लेखरा राजस्थान के जयपुर में पली-बढ़ीं। जब वह ग्यारह साल की थीं, एक कार दुर्घटना में उनकी रीढ़ की हड्डी में चोट लग गई, और तब से वह व्हीलचेयर का इस्तेमाल करती हैं। यह उनकी ज़िंदगी की एक सच्चाई है, और यह कहानी इसे बिल्कुल वैसे ही बताती है जैसे वह इसे अपनाती हैं — साफ़-साफ़, और फिर सीधे उस दिलचस्प हिस्से पर आती है, कि इसके बाद उन्होंने क्या किया।","lang":"hi","body":"Avani Lekhara grew up in Jaipur, in Rajasthan. When she was eleven, a car accident injured her spine, and from then on she has used a wheelchair. That is a fact of her life, and this story tells it the way she carries it — plainly, and then straight on to the interesting part, which is what she did next.","art":"art/story/sm/kh-avani.jpg","route":"#/story/kh.avani|h0","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Khel — India at Play"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-kh.avani-1":{"src":"passage:hi:story:kh.avani:1","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Stillest Person in the Room","text":"उनके पिता ने उन्हें कोई खेल आज़माने के लिए बढ़ावा दिया। उन्होंने तीरंदाज़ी की कोशिश की। फिर उन्होंने निशानेबाज़ी — दस मीटर एयर राइफ़ल — आज़माई, और बात बन गई। उसी दौरान उन्होंने अभिनव बिंद्रा की आत्मकथा पढ़ी, वह निशानेबाज़ जिन्होंने 2008 में भारत का पहला व्यक्तिगत ओलंपिक स्वर्ण पदक जीता था, और अवनी ने तय कर लिया कि उनका असली निशाना क्या है।","lang":"hi","body":"Her father encouraged her to try sport. She tried archery. Then she tried shooting — the ten-metre air rifle — and something clicked. Around then she read the autobiography of Abhinav Bindra, the shooter who in 2008 had won India’s first-ever individual Olympic gold, and she decided precisely what she was aiming at.","art":"art/story/sm/kh-avani.jpg","route":"#/story/kh.avani|h1","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Khel — India at Play"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-kh.avani-2":{"src":"passage:hi:story:kh.avani:2","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Stillest Person in the Room","text":"टोक्यो, 2021, पैरालंपिक खेल। उन्नीस साल की उम्र, दस मीटर एयर राइफ़ल का फ़ाइनल, और सामने दुनिया के सबसे सधे हुए हाथ। एक के बाद एक शॉट, अवनी का निशाना बिल्कुल केंद्र से चूका ही नहीं। उन्होंने पैरालंपिक रिकॉर्ड स्कोर के साथ स्वर्ण पदक जीता — पैरालंपिक में स्वर्ण जीतने वाली पहली भारतीय महिला — और फिर, कुछ ही दिनों बाद, एक और मुक़ाबले में कांस्य पदक भी जीत लिया।","lang":"hi","body":"Tokyo, 2021, the Paralympic Games. Nineteen years old, in the final of the ten-metre air rifle, against the steadiest hands on the planet. Shot after shot, Avani simply did not miss the middle. She won gold with a Paralympic record score — the first Indian woman ever to win Paralympic gold — and then, days later, won a bronze in a second event for good measure.","art":"art/story/sm/kh-avani.jpg","route":"#/story/kh.avani|h2","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Khel — India at Play"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-kh.avani-3":{"src":"passage:hi:story:kh.avani:3","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Stillest Person in the Room","text":"चैंपियनों से सबसे ज़्यादा एक ही सवाल पूछा जाता है: क्या आप यह दोबारा कर सकते हैं? पेरिस में, 2024 में, जब बाकी सभी का निशाना उन्हीं पर था, वह लौटीं और फिर से स्वर्ण पदक जीता — अपने ही रिकॉर्ड स्कोर को तोड़ते हुए। इन दोनों खेलों के बीच, उन्होंने चुपचाप वकालत की पढ़ाई भी जारी रखी। लगता है, एकदम सटीक होना एक ऐसी आदत है जो हर जगह साथ चलती है।","lang":"hi","body":"Champions are asked one question above all: can you do it again? In Paris, in 2024, with the whole field aiming at her, she came back and won the gold again — beating her own record score. Between the two Games she also quietly got on with studying law. Precision, it seems, is a habit that travels.","art":"art/story/sm/kh-avani.jpg","route":"#/story/kh.avani|h3","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Khel — India at Play"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-kh.gukesh-0":{"src":"passage:hi:story:kh.gukesh:0","title":"Read it in Hindi · Eighteen, and King of the World","text":"याद है वह 'लाइटनिंग किड', जो शतरंज का ताज चेन्नई लेकर आए थे? यह कहानी उसी से आगे निकली है। गुकेश दोम्माराजू का जन्म 2006 में चेन्नई में हुआ था — एक ऐसे शहर में जो तब तक शतरंज का दीवाना हो चुका था, जहाँ ढेरों क्लब, कोच और स्कूल टूर्नामेंट थे, और इन सबका रास्ता आनंद तक जाता था। गुकेश ने सात साल की उम्र में शतरंज की चालें सीख ली थीं।","lang":"hi","body":"Remember the Lightning Kid, who brought the chess crown home to Chennai? This story is what grew from that one. Gukesh Dommaraju was born in Chennai in 2006 — into a city that was by then mad about chess, full of clubs and coaches and school tournaments, all of it tracing back to Anand. Gukesh learned the moves at seven.","art":"art/story/sm/kh-gukesh.jpg","route":"#/story/kh.gukesh|h0","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Khel — India at Play"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-kh.gukesh-1":{"src":"passage:hi:story:kh.gukesh:1","title":"Read it in Hindi · Eighteen, and King of the World","text":"वह बड़ी तेज़ी से आगे बढ़ा। उसके डॉक्टर पिता ने अपना काम-काज छोड़कर एक से दूसरे टूर्नामेंट में उसके साथ घूमना शुरू किया; पूरे परिवार ने एक लड़के के अनोखे शतरंज के लिए अपनी आम ज़िंदगी के कई साल दांव पर लगा दिए थे। बारह साल की उम्र में गुकेश ग्रैंडमास्टर बन गया — उस समय इस खेल के इतिहास में दूसरा सबसे कम उम्र का खिलाड़ी। जिस अकादमी ने उसे तराशने में मदद की, उसे खुद आनंद चलाते थे: पहला बादशाह, जो अगले बादशाह को सिखा रहा था।","lang":"hi","body":"He rose absurdly fast. His father, a doctor, set aside his own work to travel with him from tournament to tournament, the family betting years of ordinary life on a boy’s extraordinary chess. At twelve, Gukesh became a grandmaster — at the time, the second-youngest in the history of the game. The academy that helped train him was run by Anand himself: the first king, coaching the next one.","art":"art/story/sm/kh-gukesh.jpg","route":"#/story/kh.gukesh|h1","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Khel — India at Play"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-kh.gukesh-2":{"src":"passage:hi:story:kh.gukesh:2","title":"Read it in Hindi · Eighteen, and King of the World","text":"साल 2024 में उसने चैंपियनों का वह टूर्नामेंट जीत लिया जिससे तय होता है कि विश्व खिताब के लिए कौन चुनौती देगा — सत्रह साल की उम्र में यह कमाल करने वाला वह अब तक का सबसे कम उम्र का खिलाड़ी था। इस जीत से उसे चीन के मौजूदा विश्व चैंपियन डिंग लिरेन के खिलाफ मुकाबला खेलने का मौका मिला: सिंगापुर में चौदह बाजियों का मुकाबला, जो करीब एक महीने तक चला।","lang":"hi","body":"In 2024 he won the tournament of champions that decides who challenges for the world title — at seventeen, the youngest ever to do it. That earned him a match against the reigning world champion, Ding Liren of China: fourteen games, in Singapore, stretched across almost a month.","art":"art/story/sm/kh-gukesh.jpg","route":"#/story/kh.gukesh|h2","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Khel — India at Play"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-kh.gukesh-3":{"src":"passage:hi:story:kh.gukesh:3","title":"Read it in Hindi · Eighteen, and King of the World","text":"मुकाबला बेहद कड़ा और बराबरी का रहा, बिल्कुल आखिरी बाजी तक — जो घंटों-घंटों खिंचती हुई ड्रॉ की तरफ बढ़ रही थी। और फिर, ऐसी स्थिति में जहां लगभग हर कोई उम्मीद छोड़ चुका था, थके हुए चैंपियन ने अपने हाथी से एक नन्हीं सी चूक कर दी। गुकेश, जिसने पूरी दोपहर मौकों की तलाश बंद करने से इनकार कर दिया था, उसने इसे तुरंत देख लिया।","lang":"hi","body":"The match was brutal and level, all the way to the very last game — which drifted, hour after hour, towards a draw. And then, in a position almost everyone had given up on, the champion made one tired, tiny mistake with his rook. Gukesh, who had refused all afternoon to stop looking for chances, saw it instantly.","art":"art/story/sm/kh-gukesh.jpg","route":"#/story/kh.gukesh|h3","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Khel — India at Play"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-kh.gukesh-4":{"src":"passage:hi:story:kh.gukesh:4","title":"Read it in Hindi · Eighteen, and King of the World","text":"कुछ नपी-तुली चालों के बाद, विश्व चैंपियन ने हार मान ली — और चेन्नई के एक अठारह साल के लड़के ने विश्व शतरंज चैंपियनशिप जीत ली, क्लासिकल खेल के लंबे इतिहास का सबसे कम उम्र का चैंपियन, जिसने वह रिकॉर्ड तोड़ा जो उसके माता-पिता के मिलने से भी पहले से बना हुआ था। कैमरों ने उसे दोनों हाथों में सिर थामे रोते हुए कैद किया, एक लड़का और साथ ही साथ एक बादशाह।","lang":"hi","body":"A few precise moves later, the world champion resigned — and an eighteen-year-old from Chennai had won the world chess championship, the youngest champion in the long history of the classical game, breaking a record that had stood since before his parents met. The cameras caught him with his head in his hands, crying, a boy and a king at the same time.","art":"art/story/sm/kh-gukesh.jpg","route":"#/story/kh.gukesh|h4","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Khel — India at Play"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-kh.dhoni-0":{"src":"passage:hi:story:kh.dhoni:0","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Ticket Collector Who Finished It","text":"महेंद्र सिंह धोनी रांची में बड़े हुए — जंगलों और लोहे की धरती का एक शहर, जो अब झारखंड में है, क्रिकेट के मशहूर शहरों से उतना ही दूर जितना कोई हिंदुस्तानी लड़का हो सकता था। वह अपने स्कूल की फुटबॉल टीम के गोलकीपर थे, और एक खेल शिक्षक ने ही उस गोलकीपर से विकेटकीपिंग के दस्ताने आज़माने को कहा। बाद में पता चला कि ये हाथ दोनों ही जगह कमाल करते थे।","lang":"hi","body":"Mahendra Singh Dhoni grew up in Ranchi — a town of forests and iron country, in what is now Jharkhand, about as far from cricket’s famous cities as an Indian boy could be. He was his school’s football goalkeeper, and it was a games teacher who asked the goalkeeper to try the wicketkeeping gloves instead. The hands, it turned out, worked either way.","art":"art/story/sm/kh-dhoni.jpg","route":"#/story/kh.dhoni|h0","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Khel — India at Play"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-kh.dhoni-1":{"src":"passage:hi:story:kh.dhoni:1","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Ticket Collector Who Finished It","text":"बीस साल की उम्र में उन्हें वैसी नौकरी मिल गई जिसकी हर परिवार दुआ करता है: भारतीय रेल में एक पद, बंगाल के खड़गपुर स्टेशन पर टिकट चेक करने का काम। दो साल तक वे रेलवे क्वार्टर में रहे, प्लेटफ़ॉर्मों पर काम किया, और जब भी नौकरी से फुर्सत मिली, क्रिकेट खेला। सरकारी नौकरी एक गरम कोट जैसी होती है — उनका परिवार इसकी क़ीमत जानता था। और हर रोज़, दूसरे लोगों के सफ़र से भरी रेलगाड़ियाँ उनके सामने से गुज़रती रहीं।","lang":"hi","body":"At twenty he got the kind of job families pray for: a post with Indian Railways, checking tickets at Kharagpur station in Bengal. For two years he lived in the railway quarters, worked the platforms, and played cricket whenever the job allowed. A government job is a warm coat — his family knew what it was worth. And every day, trains full of other people’s journeys pulled out in front of him.","art":"art/story/sm/kh-dhoni.jpg","route":"#/story/kh.dhoni|h1","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Khel — India at Play"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-kh.dhoni-2":{"src":"passage:hi:story:kh.dhoni:2","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Ticket Collector Who Finished It","text":"दो ही साल के भीतर, राँची का यह लंबे बालों वाला विकेटकीपर भारत के लिए पाकिस्तान के ख़िलाफ़ 148 रन कूट रहा था। और 2007 में, जब पहले-पहल ट्वेंटी-20 वर्ल्ड कप के लिए एक युवा टीम की कप्तानी उन्हें सौंपी गई, तो उन्होंने कुछ ऐसा किया जो कोच आज भी सिखाते हैं: जब फ़ाइनल मैच आख़िरी ओवर पर टिका था, उन्होंने गेंद किसी बड़े स्टार को नहीं, बल्कि एक ऐसे गेंदबाज़ को थमाई जिसका नाम लगभग किसी ने नहीं सुना था — और शांत मन से चला गया यह दाँव भारत को कप जिता गया।","lang":"hi","body":"Within two years the long-haired wicketkeeper from Ranchi was smashing 148 against Pakistan for India. And in 2007, handed the captaincy of a young squad for the very first Twenty20 World Cup, he did something coaches still teach: with the final match hanging on its last over, he gave the ball not to a star but to a bowler almost nobody had heard of — and the gamble, calmly made, won India the cup.","art":"art/story/sm/kh-dhoni.jpg","route":"#/story/kh.dhoni|h2","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Khel — India at Play"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-kh.dhoni-3":{"src":"passage:hi:story:kh.dhoni:3","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Ticket Collector Who Finished It","text":"फिर आई मुंबई में 2 अप्रैल 2011 की रात — वर्ल्ड कप का फ़ाइनल, श्रीलंका के ख़िलाफ़ भारत 275 रनों का पीछा कर रहा था, और सौ करोड़ लोग साँस थामे बैठे थे। पूरे टूर्नामेंट में ख़राब फ़ॉर्म से जूझ रहे धोनी, बल्लेबाज़ी क्रम में ख़ुद ऊपर आ गए — कप्तान ने सबसे कठिन ज़िम्मेदारी अपने कंधों पर ले ली। वे 91 रन बनाकर नाबाद रहे, और लॉन्ग-ऑन के ऊपर से एक ऊँचा छक्का जड़कर मैच ख़त्म किया। वह शॉट भारतीय क्रिकेट के किसी भी शॉट से ज़्यादा बार देखा गया है। उसने अट्ठाईस साल का इंतज़ार ख़त्म कर दिया — वही कप जो 1983 में कपिल की टीम ने जीता था, आख़िरकार घर लौट आया, ख़ुद सचिन के अपने शहर में।","lang":"hi","body":"Then Mumbai, the night of 2 April 2011 — the World Cup final, India chasing 275 against Sri Lanka, a billion people holding their breath. Dhoni, out of form all tournament, promoted himself up the batting order — the captain taking the hardest job in the house for himself. He finished on 91 not out, and ended the match with a six lifted high over long-on. That shot has been replayed more than any stroke in Indian cricket. It ended a twenty-eight-year wait — the cup Kapil’s team had won in 1983, home at last, in Sachin’s own city.","art":"art/story/sm/kh-dhoni.jpg","route":"#/story/kh.dhoni|h3","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Khel — India at Play"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-kh.dhoni-4":{"src":"passage:hi:story:kh.dhoni:4","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Ticket Collector Who Finished It","text":"अख़बारों ने उन्हें 'कैप्टन कूल' कहा, और यह नाम इसलिए जम गया क्योंकि यह सच बयाँ करता था: क्रिकेट के सबसे हंगामेदार पलों में भी, वे ऐसे सोचते और चलते थे मानो कोई टाइम-टेबल पढ़ रहा हो। 2013 में उनकी टीम ने चैंपियंस ट्रॉफ़ी भी जीत ली — जिससे वे क्रिकेट के तीनों विश्व ख़िताब जीतने वाले इकलौते कप्तान बन गए। शांत रहना कोई ऐसी चीज़ नहीं जो आपके पास बस यूँ ही होती है। यह तो वह हुनर है जिसे आप रोज़-रोज़ साधते हैं।","lang":"hi","body":"The newspapers called him Captain Cool, and the name stuck because it named something real: in the loudest moments cricket can produce, he moved and thought like a man reading a timetable. In 2013 his team added the Champions Trophy — making him the only captain ever to win all three of cricket’s world titles. Calm, it turns out, is not something you have. It is something you practise.","art":"art/story/sm/kh-dhoni.jpg","route":"#/story/kh.dhoni|h4","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Khel — India at Play"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-kh.kohli-0":{"src":"passage:hi:story:kh.kohli:0","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Boy Who Batted That Morning","text":"1998 की गर्मियों में, पश्चिमी दिल्ली के एक नौ साल के लड़के ने अपने पड़ोस की एक नई-नवेली क्रिकेट अकादमी में दाख़िला लिया, और उसके पिता का एक ऐसा नियम शुरू हुआ जो सालों चला: दिल्ली के ट्रैफ़िक और दिल्ली के मौसम से जूझते हुए, दिन-ब-दिन अपने स्कूटर पर बच्चे को प्रैक्टिस के लिए ले जाना और वापस लाना। विराट कोहली का क्रिकेट, शुरू से ही, एक ऐसी चीज़ थी जिसे वे और उनके पिता मिलकर जीते थे।","lang":"hi","body":"In the summer of 1998, a nine-year-old from West Delhi joined a brand-new cricket academy in his neighbourhood, and his father began a routine that lasted years: driving the boy to practice and back on his scooter, day after day, through Delhi’s traffic and Delhi’s weather. Virat Kohli’s cricket was, from the very start, a thing he and his father did together.","art":"art/story/sm/kh-kohli.jpg","route":"#/story/kh.kohli|h0","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Khel — India at Play"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-kh.kohli-1":{"src":"passage:hi:story:kh.kohli:1","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Boy Who Batted That Morning","text":"दिसंबर 2006। अठारह साल के विराट दिल्ली के लिए एक बड़ा मैच खेल रहे थे, टीम मुश्किल में थी और वह क्रीज़ पर टिके हुए थे। उसी रात, तड़के घर पर उनके पिता का अचानक निधन हो गया। इसके बाद जो हुआ, उसकी चर्चा दिल्ली के ड्रेसिंग रूम में आज भी दबी ज़ुबान में की जाती है: सुबह होते ही उस लड़के ने अपने कोच को फ़ोन किया और कहा कि वह बल्लेबाज़ी करना चाहता है। वह मैदान पर आए, सुबह भर अपनी टीम के लिए बल्लेबाज़ी की, 90 रन बनाए — और मैदान से सीधे अपने पिता को अंतिम विदाई देने चले गए। वहाँ मौजूद किसी भी इंसान ने उस पारी को कभी सिर्फ़ रनों की पारी नहीं कहा।","lang":"hi","body":"December 2006. Virat, eighteen, was playing for Delhi in a big match, not out overnight with his team in trouble. In the small hours of that night, at home, his father died suddenly. What happened next is told quietly in Delhi dressing rooms to this day: at dawn the boy telephoned his coach and said he wanted to bat. He came to the ground, batted through the morning for his team, made 90 — and went from the field to say goodbye to his father. Nobody who was there has ever described that innings as just runs.","art":"art/story/sm/kh-kohli.jpg","route":"#/story/kh.kohli|h1","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Khel — India at Play"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-kh.kohli-2":{"src":"passage:hi:story:kh.kohli:2","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Boy Who Batted That Morning","text":"क्रिकेट उनके और उनके पिता के बीच की भाषा थी, और वह वही भाषा बोलते रहे। 2008 में उन्होंने भारत की अंडर-19 टीम की कप्तानी करके विश्व कप जिताया। 2011 में, बाईस साल की उम्र में, वह उस टीम में थे जिसने ख़ुद विश्व कप जीता — वह इसी शेल्फ़ पर रखी सचिन की कहानी वाले वही नौजवान हैं, उन साथियों में से एक जिन्होंने उस रात उस महान खिलाड़ी को अपने कंधों पर उठाकर पूरे मैदान का चक्कर लगाया था।","lang":"hi","body":"Cricket had been the language between him and his father, and he kept speaking it. In 2008 he captained India’s under-19s to a World Cup. In 2011, at twenty-two, he was in the team that won the World Cup itself — he is the young man in Sachin’s story on this shelf, one of the teammates who carried the great man around the ground on their shoulders that night.","art":"art/story/sm/kh-kohli.jpg","route":"#/story/kh.kohli|h2","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Khel — India at Play"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-kh.kohli-3":{"src":"passage:hi:story:kh.kohli:3","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Boy Who Batted That Morning","text":"फिर कहानी का वह हिस्सा आया जिसने भारतीय क्रिकेट की रोज़मर्रा की आदतों को ही बदल दिया। 2012 में, जैसा कि वह ख़ुद बताते हैं, उन्होंने ईमानदारी से अपने अंदर झाँका और तय किया कि उनके हुनर को एक बेहतर रखवाले की ज़रूरत है। उन्होंने सब कुछ नए सिरे से ढाला — क्या खाना है, कैसे कसरत करनी है, कैसे सोना है — जब तक कि वह दुनिया के सबसे फ़िट खिलाड़ियों में शामिल नहीं हो गए, और यह फ़िटनेस रनों में बदल गई: एक के बाद एक नामुमकिन लक्ष्य का पीछा किया गया, इतनी बार कि लोग उन्हें चेज़ मास्टर कहने लगे। और कप्तान ने जहाँ अपने पैमाने तय किए, पूरी टीम भी उसी राह पर चल पड़ी। आज भारतीय क्रिकेट का अभ्यास का तरीका अलग है, क्योंकि पहले एक खिलाड़ी ने ख़ुद के लिए स्तर ऊँचा उठाया था।","lang":"hi","body":"Then came the part of the story that changed Indian cricket’s daily habits. In 2012, by his own telling, he took an honest look at himself and decided his talent deserved a better keeper. He rebuilt everything — what he ate, how he trained, how he slept — until he was among the fittest athletes in world sport, and the fitness became runs: chase after impossible chase hunted down, so often that people simply started calling him the chase master. And where the captain’s standards went, a whole team’s followed. Indian cricket trains differently today because one player raised the bar on himself first.","art":"art/story/sm/kh-kohli.jpg","route":"#/story/kh.kohli|h3","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Khel — India at Play"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-kh.kohli-4":{"src":"passage:hi:story:kh.kohli:4","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Boy Who Batted That Morning","text":"शतक पर शतक बनते रहे। नवंबर 2023 में, मुंबई में, उन्होंने अपना पचासवाँ एकदिवसीय अंतर्राष्ट्रीय शतक बनाया — और सचिन तेंदुलकर का रिकॉर्ड तोड़ दिया, वही इंसान जिन्हें कभी उन्होंने कंधों पर उठाया था, और जो आज अपने ही घरेलू मैदान के स्टैंड में खड़े होकर तालियाँ बजा रहे थे। रिकॉर्ड की किताबों में तो बस आँकड़े दर्ज हैं। लेकिन तस्वीरों में एक हाथ से दूसरे हाथ में किसी विरासत को सौंपे जाने की झलक क़ैद है।","lang":"hi","body":"The hundreds kept coming. In November 2023, in Mumbai, he scored his fiftieth one-day international century — passing the record of Sachin Tendulkar, the man he had helped carry, who stood applauding in the stands of his own home ground. The record books hold the number. The photographs hold the passing of something from one pair of hands to another.","art":"art/story/sm/kh-kohli.jpg","route":"#/story/kh.kohli|h4","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Khel — India at Play"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-kh.mithali-0":{"src":"passage:hi:story:kh.mithali:0","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Dancer at the Crease","text":"मिताली राज हैदराबाद में एक वायु सेना परिवार में पली-बढ़ीं, और आठ सालों तक उनकी हर सुबह भरतनाट्यम के नाम रही — घुँघरू, थकने तक साधी जाने वाली मुद्राएँ, और शास्त्रीय नृत्य का कड़ा अनुशासन। क्रिकेट तो ज़िंदगी में यूँ ही अचानक आ गया: उन्हें उनके बड़े भाई के कोचिंग कैंप में साथ ले जाया गया, इंतज़ार करते-करते उन्होंने बल्ला उठा लिया, और कोच लड़कों को देखना भूलकर उन्हें ही देखने लगे।","lang":"hi","body":"Mithali Raj grew up in Hyderabad, in an Air Force family, and for eight years her mornings belonged to bharatanatyam — the anklets, the postures held until they burned, the discipline of classical dance. Cricket arrived sideways: she was taken along to her elder brother’s coaching camp, picked up a bat while she waited, and the coaches stopped watching the boys.","art":"art/story/sm/kh-mithali.jpg","route":"#/story/kh.mithali|h0","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Khel — India at Play"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-kh.mithali-1":{"src":"passage:hi:story:kh.mithali:1","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Dancer at the Crease","text":"जब वह बारह-तेरह साल की हुईं, तो डांस और क्रिकेट दोनों ही उनकी हर सुबह माँगने लगे, और उन्होंने इस चुनाव का किस्सा कई बार सुनाया है: दोनों एक साथ नहीं चल सकते थे।","lang":"hi","body":"By her early teens, both dance and cricket wanted every morning she had, and she has told the story of the choice many times: it could not be both.","art":"art/story/sm/kh-mithali.jpg","route":"#/story/kh.mithali|h1","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Khel — India at Play"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-kh.mithali-2":{"src":"passage:hi:story:kh.mithali:2","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Dancer at the Crease","text":"सोलह साल की उम्र में, 1999 में, उन्होंने भारत के लिए अपना पहला मैच खेला और शतक बनाया — 114 रन, नाबाद। उन्नीस साल की उम्र में उन्होंने इंग्लैंड के ख़िलाफ़ कई दिनों तक बल्लेबाज़ी की और 214 रन बनाए, जो उस समय महिला टेस्ट क्रिकेट के इतिहास का सबसे बड़ा स्कोर था। गेंदबाज़ बदले, दशक बदले; लेकिन पिच के दूसरे छोर पर बना वह शांत ठहराव कभी नहीं बदला।","lang":"hi","body":"At sixteen, in 1999, she played her first match for India and scored a century — 114 not out. At nineteen she batted for days against England and made 214, then the highest score in the history of women’s Test cricket. Bowlers changed, decades changed; the calm at the other end of the pitch did not.","art":"art/story/sm/kh-mithali.jpg","route":"#/story/kh.mithali|h2","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Khel — India at Play"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-kh.mithali-3":{"src":"passage:hi:story:kh.mithali:3","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Dancer at the Crease","text":"उन्होंने दो अलग-अलग दशकों में भारत की कप्तानी की — 2005 में टीम को वर्ल्ड कप फ़ाइनल तक पहुँचाया, और फिर 2017 में भी। उसी 2017 वर्ल्ड कप में, एक तस्वीर पूरी दुनिया में फैल गई: पैड पहने मिताली, वर्ल्ड कप मैच में बल्लेबाज़ी की अपनी बारी का इंतज़ार करते हुए — चुपचाप एक किताब पढ़ रही थीं। दुनिया को यह बात हैरान कर देने वाली लगी। पर जो उन्हें जानते थे, उनके लिए यह बिल्कुल सटीक था: एक ऐसा मन जिसे बचपन से ही पूरी तरह वहीं टिके रहने की आदत थी, जहाँ वह रहना चाहे।","lang":"hi","body":"She captained India across two different decades — leading the team to a World Cup final in 2005, and again in 2017. At that 2017 World Cup, a photograph went around the world: Mithali, padded up, waiting to bat in a World Cup match — quietly reading a book. The world found it astonishing. Anyone who knew her found it exact: a mind trained since childhood to be perfectly where it chooses to be.","art":"art/story/sm/kh-mithali.jpg","route":"#/story/kh.mithali|h3","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Khel — India at Play"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-kh.mithali-4":{"src":"passage:hi:story:kh.mithali:4","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Dancer at the Crease","text":"2017 के फ़ाइनल ने लॉर्ड्स के पूरे मैदान को भर दिया — क्रिकेट का मक्का, सारे टिकट बिक चुके थे, वह भी एक महिला मैच के लिए, और पूरे भारत में लाखों लोग इसे देख रहे थे। इंग्लैंड नौ रनों से जीता, पर इसके बाद जो हुआ, उसके आगे इस बात का कोई फ़र्क नहीं पड़ा: लड़कियों की अकादमियाँ भरने लगीं, खिलाड़ियों को कॉन्ट्रैक्ट मिले, और भारत में महिला क्रिकेट को अब किसी से तवज्जो माँगने की ज़रूरत नहीं रही, क्योंकि वह उसे मिल चुकी थी। जब मिताली 2022 में रिटायर हुईं, तो उनके 10,868 अंतरराष्ट्रीय रन महिला क्रिकेट में किसी भी देश के, किसी भी खिलाड़ी द्वारा बनाए गए सबसे ज़्यादा रन थे।","lang":"hi","body":"The 2017 final filled Lord’s — the home of cricket, sold out, for a women’s match, with millions more watching across India. England won by nine runs, and it barely mattered to what happened next: girls’ academies filled, the players won contracts, and women’s cricket in India stopped asking for attention because it finally had it. When Mithali retired in 2022, her 10,868 international runs were the most ever scored in women’s cricket, by anyone, from any country.","art":"art/story/sm/kh-mithali.jpg","route":"#/story/kh.mithali|h4","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Khel — India at Play"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-kh.saina-0":{"src":"passage:hi:story:kh.saina:0","title":"Read it in Hindi · The First Shuttle Through the Door","text":"साइना नेहवाल का जन्म 1990 में हरियाणा के हिसार में हुआ था — कुश्ती का इलाक़ा, गेहूँ का इलाक़ा, बैडमिंटन का इलाक़ा तो बिल्कुल नहीं। लेकिन उनकी माँ राज्य स्तर की बैडमिंटन खिलाड़ी रह चुकी थीं, जिनका अपना खेल जल्दी ही छूट गया था, जैसा उन दिनों ज़्यादातर महिलाओं के खेलों के साथ होता था। और उस घर ने उस अधूरे सपने को वैसे ही सँभाल कर रखा जैसे घर रखा करते हैं: चुपचाप, और पूरी तरह से।","lang":"hi","body":"Saina Nehwal was born in 1990 in Hisar, in Haryana — wrestling country, wheat country, not badminton country. But her mother had been a state-level badminton player whose own game had stopped early, the way women’s games mostly did in those days, and the house held that unfinished dream the way houses do: quietly, and completely.","art":"art/story/sm/kh-saina.jpg","route":"#/story/kh.saina|h0","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Khel — India at Play"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-kh.saina-1":{"src":"passage:hi:story:kh.saina:1","title":"Read it in Hindi · The First Shuttle Through the Door","text":"\"जब साइना आठ साल की थीं, तब उनके वैज्ञानिक पिता के काम की वजह से उनका परिवार हैदराबाद आ गया — और हैदराबाद में तो असली बैडमिंटन था। एकेडमी शहर के दूसरे छोर पर थी, इसलिए उनके पिताजी उन्हें भोर होने से पहले ही जगा देते और रोज़ सुबह अपने स्कूटर पर बैठाकर मीलों दूर ले जाते, फिर प्रैक्टिस ख़त्म होने तक इंतज़ार करके वापस ले आते। अगर भोर की ये सवारियाँ जानी-पहचानी लग रही हैं, तो लगनी भी चाहिए: सालों बाद हैदराबाद की ही एक और लड़की, पी. वी. सिंधु, बैडमिंटन की इसी दुनिया तक पहुँचने के लिए ऐसी ही सुबहें जीने वाली थीं — उनकी कहानी अलमारी में ठीक इसी कहानी के ऊपर रखी है।\"","lang":"hi","body":"When Saina was eight, her scientist father’s work moved the family to Hyderabad — and Hyderabad had real badminton. The academy was on the far side of the city, so her father woke her before daybreak and rode her there on his scooter, tens of kilometres, morning after morning, then waited through practice to ride her back. If those dawn rides sound familiar, they should: years later another Hyderabad girl, P. V. Sindhu, would live the same mornings on the way to the same badminton world — her story sits just above this one on the shelf.","art":"art/story/sm/kh-saina.jpg","route":"#/story/kh.saina|h1","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Khel — India at Play"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-kh.saina-2":{"src":"passage:hi:story:kh.saina:2","title":"Read it in Hindi · The First Shuttle Through the Door","text":"\"सुबह-सुबह की यह मेहनत रंग लाने लगी। 2008 में वह जूनियर वर्ल्ड चैंपियन बनीं — ऐसा करने वाली पहली भारतीय खिलाड़ी। 2009 में उन्होंने इंडोनेशिया ओपन जीता, जो इस खेल के सबसे बड़े ख़िताबों में से एक था, और वह भी दुनिया में बैडमिंटन की सबसे ज़ोरदार भीड़ के सामने — एक बार फिर, इतना बड़ा ख़िताब जीतने वाली पहली भारतीय महिला। हिसार की वह लड़की अब सिर्फ़ उभरती हुई खिलाड़ी नहीं थी। वह अपनी मंज़िल पर पहुँच चुकी थीं।\"","lang":"hi","body":"The mornings compounded. In 2008 she became junior world champion — the first Indian ever. In 2009 she won the Indonesia Open, one of the sport’s biggest crowns, in front of the loudest badminton crowd on Earth — again the first Indian woman to take a title that size. The girl from Hisar was no longer coming up. She had arrived.","art":"art/story/sm/kh-saina.jpg","route":"#/story/kh.saina|h2","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Khel — India at Play"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-kh.saina-3":{"src":"passage:hi:story:kh.saina:3","title":"Read it in Hindi · The First Shuttle Through the Door","text":"\"लंदन, 2012। ओलिंपिक खेलों के सौ से भी ज़्यादा सालों के इतिहास में भारत ने बैडमिंटन में कुछ नहीं जीता था। साइना लड़ते हुए कांस्य पदक तक पहुँचीं — भारतीय इतिहास में बैडमिंटन का पहला ओलिंपिक पदक। यह पहला पदक एक अजीब ही तरह का पदक होता है: इसका वज़न बाकी सभी कांस्य पदकों जितना ही होता है, पर इसके साथ वह सब कुछ भी जुड़ा होता है जिसे पहले नामुमकिन कहा जाता था।\"","lang":"hi","body":"London, 2012. In more than a century of Olympic Games, India had won badminton nothing. Saina fought her way to the bronze medal — the first Olympic badminton medal in Indian history. It is a strange kind of medal, a first: it weighs what every other bronze weighs, and also carries everything that was previously called impossible.","art":"art/story/sm/kh-saina.jpg","route":"#/story/kh.saina|h3","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Khel — India at Play"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-kh.saina-4":{"src":"passage:hi:story:kh.saina:4","title":"Read it in Hindi · The First Shuttle Through the Door","text":"\"अप्रैल 2015 में वह दुनिया की नंबर एक खिलाड़ी बनीं — बैडमिंटन की विश्व रैंकिंग में पहले पायदान पर पहुँचने वाली पहली भारतीय महिला। और अब ज़रा देखिए कि उनके पीछे-पीछे क्या कुछ हुआ: सिंधु का रजत पदक और वर्ल्ड टाइटल उसी दरवाज़े से होकर आए, जिसे देश ने साइना को धक्का देकर खोलते देखा था। चैंपियन नतीजे देते हैं; मगर पहले चैंपियन भरोसा देते हैं।\"","lang":"hi","body":"In April 2015 she reached the top of the world rankings — the first Indian woman ever ranked world number one in badminton. And look at what stands behind her now: Sindhu’s silver and world title came through a door the country had watched Saina hit open. Champions make results; first champions make belief.","art":"art/story/sm/kh-saina.jpg","route":"#/story/kh.saina|h4","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Khel — India at Play"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-kh.malleswari-0":{"src":"passage:hi:story:kh.malleswari:0","title":"Read it in Hindi · Iron in the Village","text":"\"वूसावानीपेटा, आंध्र के समुद्र तट पर श्रीकाकुलम ज़िले का एक गाँव है, और 1980 के दशक में वहाँ कुछ अनोखा था: मिट्टी के फ़र्श वाला एक छोटा-सा जिम जहाँ एक स्थानीय कोच लोहे का खेल सिखाते थे — यानी वेटलिफ़्टिंग। कर्णम मल्लेश्वरी अपनी बहनों के पीछे-पीछे बारह साल की उम्र में वहाँ आईं; उनका घर वज़न उठाने वाली लड़कियों का घर बन गया, एक ऐसे देश में जहाँ ऐसे किसी घर की कल्पना भी शायद ही किसी ने की थी।\"","lang":"hi","body":"Voosavanipeta is a village in Srikakulam district, on the Andhra coast, and in the 1980s it held something unusual: a little gymnasium with a mud floor where a local coach taught the iron game — weightlifting. Karnam Malleswari came to it at twelve, following her sisters; theirs became a household of girls who lifted, in a country that had barely imagined such a household.","art":"art/story/sm/kh-malleswari.jpg","route":"#/story/kh.malleswari|h0","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Khel — India at Play"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-kh.malleswari-1":{"src":"passage:hi:story:kh.malleswari:1","title":"Read it in Hindi · Iron in the Village","text":"\"लोग वेटलिफ़्टिंग को सिर्फ़ ताक़त का खेल समझते हैं। पर यह तो सौ किलो वज़न के साथ घड़ीसाज़ी करने जैसा बारीक काम है। दोनों लिफ़्ट — स्नैच, यानी ज़मीन से आसमान तक एक सधा हुआ झटका, और क्लीन एंड जर्क, ज़मीन से कंधों तक और फिर आसमान तक — बारीकी, सही समय और हिम्मत की परीक्षा हैं, जहाँ एक सेंटीमीटर की चूक भी पूरी दुनिया को आप पर गिरा सकती है। ताक़त आपको कमरे के अंदर लाती है। हुनर आपको जिताता है।\"","lang":"hi","body":"People picture weightlifting as brute force. It is closer to watchmaking done with a hundred kilograms. The two lifts — the snatch, one clean movement from floor to sky, and the clean and jerk, floor to shoulders to sky — are exercises in precision, timing and nerve, where a centimetre of error drops the world on you. Strength gets you into the room. Craft wins.","art":"art/story/sm/kh-malleswari.jpg","route":"#/story/kh.malleswari|h1","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Khel — India at Play"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-kh.malleswari-2":{"src":"passage:hi:story:kh.malleswari:2","title":"Read it in Hindi · Iron in the Village","text":"\"मल्लेश्वरी का हुनर उन्हें गाँव के जिम से निकालकर दुनिया के मंच पर ले गया — और 1994 में, इस्तांबुल में, वे विश्व चैंपियन बनीं। 1995 में उन्होंने यह कारनामा फिर कर दिखाया। श्रीकाकुलम ज़िले की एक महिला, लोहे के इस खेल में दो बार विश्व चैंपियन बनीं, वह भी तब जब भारत के ज़्यादातर लोगों ने कभी महिलाओं की वेटलिफ़्टिंग प्रतियोगिता देखी तक नहीं थी।\"","lang":"hi","body":"Malleswari’s craft took her out of the village gym and onto the world stage — and in 1994, in Istanbul, she became champion of the world. In 1995 she did it again. A woman from Srikakulam district, twice world champion in the iron game, years before most of India had ever watched a women’s weightlifting competition.","art":"art/story/sm/kh-malleswari.jpg","route":"#/story/kh.malleswari|h2","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Khel — India at Play"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-kh.malleswari-3":{"src":"passage:hi:story:kh.malleswari:3","title":"Read it in Hindi · Iron in the Village","text":"\"सिडनी, सितंबर 2000: वे पहले ओलंपिक खेल जिनमें महिलाओं की वेटलिफ़्टिंग को शामिल किया गया था। मल्लेश्वरी ने स्नैच में 110 किलोग्राम और क्लीन एंड जर्क में 130 किलोग्राम — कुल 240 किलोग्राम — वज़न उठाया और कांस्य पदक जीता। अगला वाक्य ज़रा ठहरकर पढ़िए, क्योंकि पूरी-पूरी पीढ़ियों ने इसका इंतज़ार किया था: आधुनिक ओलंपिक के सौ से भी ज़्यादा सालों में, किसी भी भारतीय महिला ने किसी भी खेल में, किसी भी रंग का पदक नहीं जीता था। वे पहली थीं।\"","lang":"hi","body":"Sydney, September 2000: the first Olympic Games ever to include women’s weightlifting. Malleswari lifted 110 kilograms in the snatch and 130 in the clean and jerk — 240 in all — and won bronze. Read the next sentence slowly, because whole generations waited for it: in more than a hundred years of the modern Olympics, no Indian woman had ever won a medal of any colour, in any sport. She was the first.","art":"art/story/sm/kh-malleswari.jpg","route":"#/story/kh.malleswari|h3","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Khel — India at Play"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-kh.malleswari-4":{"src":"passage:hi:story:kh.malleswari:4","title":"Read it in Hindi · Iron in the Village","text":"\"अब इस ताक़ पर नज़र डालकर देखिए कि उनके बाद कौन-कौन आया: मैरी कॉम का कांस्य, साइना का कांस्य, सिंधु का रजत, मीराबाई का रजत, अवनि के स्वर्ण पदक। इनमें से हर एक चैंपियन उस मंच पर पहुँची, जहाँ भारतीय महिलाओं के लिए सबसे पहले मल्लेश्वरी पहुँची थीं। पहला पदक सचमुच यही सौग़ात लाता है — रिकॉर्ड की किताबों में सिर्फ़ एक जगह नहीं, बल्कि पूरे देश की बेटियों के लिए मंज़ूरी की एक पर्ची।\"","lang":"hi","body":"Now look around this shelf at who came after: Mary Kom’s bronze, Saina’s bronze, Sindhu’s silver, Mirabai’s silver, Avani’s golds. Every one of those champions stepped onto a podium that, for Indian women, Malleswari reached first. That is what a first medal actually buys — not one place in the record books, but a permission slip for a whole country’s daughters.","art":"art/story/sm/kh-malleswari.jpg","route":"#/story/kh.malleswari|h4","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Khel — India at Play"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-kh.mirabai-0":{"src":"passage:hi:story:kh.mirabai:0","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Girl Who Carried the Firewood","text":"\"नोंगपोक काकचिंग मणिपुर की पहाड़ियों में बसा एक गाँव है, इंफ़ाल से उबड़-खाबड़ रास्तों का एक घंटे का सफ़र, और गाँव के ज़्यादातर बच्चों की तरह सैखोम मीराबाई चानू भी घर के काम करते हुए बड़ी हुईं — जिनमें से एक काम था, पहाड़ी ढलानों से जलाने की लकड़ियाँ लाना। उनके परिवार को यह बताना बहुत पसंद है कि जब वे क़रीब बारह साल की थीं तब क्या हुआ था: उनके बड़े भाई से लकड़ियों का भारी गट्ठर नहीं संभल रहा था, और मीराबाई ने उसे आसानी से उठा लिया और घर ले आईं, मानो पहाड़ से ही यह समझने में भूल हो गई हो कि ताक़तवर कौन था।\"","lang":"hi","body":"Nongpok Kakching is a village in the hills of Manipur, a bumpy hour from Imphal, and like most village children Saikhom Mirabai Chanu grew up doing chores — among them, fetching firewood from the hillsides. Her family loves telling what happened when she was about twelve: her elder brother could not manage a heavy bundle, and Mirabai picked it up and carried it home, easily, as if the hill had made a mistake about who was strong.","art":"art/story/sm/kh-mirabai.jpg","route":"#/story/kh.mirabai|h0","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Khel — India at Play"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-kh.mirabai-1":{"src":"passage:hi:story:kh.mirabai:1","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Girl Who Carried the Firewood","text":"\"वह तीरंदाज़ बनना चाहती थी। लेकिन मणिपुर एक ऐसा राज्य है जहाँ चैंपियन वैसे पैदा होते हैं जैसे दूसरी जगहों पर चावल — इस शेल्फ़ पर रखी मैरी कॉम की कहानी भी इन्हीं पहाड़ियों से शुरू होती है — और वहाँ की सबसे महान वेटलिफ़्टर, कुंजारानी देवी, हर मणिपुरी घर में एक मिसाल थीं। मीराबाई ने बारबेल को चुना, और जैसे भी मुमकिन हुआ इम्फाल ट्रेनिंग के लिए पहुँचती रहीं — अक्सर अपने गाँव के पास से गुज़रने वाले रेत के ट्रकों को हाथ देकर रुकवातीं, और ड्राइवरों के साथ केबिन में बैठकर प्रैक्टिस के लिए जातीं।\"","lang":"hi","body":"She had wanted to be an archer. But Manipur is a state that produces champions the way other places produce rice — Mary Kom’s story on this shelf begins in these same hills — and its greatest weightlifter, Kunjarani Devi, was a legend in every Manipuri household. Mirabai chose the barbell, and got herself to training in Imphal however she could — often by waving down the sand trucks that ran past her village, riding to practice in the cab with the drivers.","art":"art/story/sm/kh-mirabai.jpg","route":"#/story/kh.mirabai|h1","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Khel — India at Play"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-kh.mirabai-2":{"src":"passage:hi:story:kh.mirabai:2","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Girl Who Carried the Firewood","text":"\"रियो, 2016: उसका पहला ओलंपिक, इक्कीस साल की उम्र, पहली बार उसे देखता हुआ पूरा देश — और फिर भारी तबाही। क्लीन एंड जर्क में वह तीनों कोशिशों में नाकाम रही। कोई कुल स्कोर नहीं, कोई नतीजा नहीं; उसके नाम के आगे रिकॉर्ड में वही अक्षर लिखे थे जिनसे हर लिफ़्टर डरता है। वह कैमरों के सामने रो पड़ी, और कैमरों ने अपनी नज़र नहीं हटाई।\"","lang":"hi","body":"Rio, 2016: her first Olympics, twenty-one years old, a nation newly watching — and disaster. In the clean and jerk she failed all three attempts. No total, no result; beside her name the record shows the letters that lifters dread. She wept in front of the cameras, and the cameras did not look away.","art":"art/story/sm/kh-mirabai.jpg","route":"#/story/kh.mirabai|h2","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Khel — India at Play"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-kh.mirabai-3":{"src":"passage:hi:story:kh.mirabai:3","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Girl Who Carried the Firewood","text":"\"रियो के एक साल बाद, अमेरिका में 2017 की वर्ल्ड चैंपियनशिप में, मीराबाई चानू दुनिया की चैंपियन बनीं। और टोक्यो में, 24 जुलाई 2021 को — देर से हुए ओलंपिक की पहली ही सुबह — उन्होंने स्नैच में 87 किलोग्राम और क्लीन एंड जर्क में 115 किलोग्राम उठाया, कुल 202 किलोग्राम, और सिल्वर मेडल जीता: उन खेलों में भारत का पहला मेडल, पहले ही दिन, उस लड़की की तरफ़ से जिसके खेल पाँच साल पहले आँसुओं में खत्म हुए थे।\"","lang":"hi","body":"One year after Rio, at the 2017 world championships in America, Mirabai Chanu was champion of the world. And in Tokyo, on 24 July 2021 — the first morning of the delayed Olympics — she lifted 87 kilograms in the snatch and 115 in the clean and jerk, 202 in all, and won silver: India’s first medal of those Games, on their first day, from the girl whose Games five years earlier had ended in tears.","art":"art/story/sm/kh-mirabai.jpg","route":"#/story/kh.mirabai|h3","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Khel — India at Play"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-kh.mirabai-4":{"src":"passage:hi:story:kh.mirabai:4","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Girl Who Carried the Firewood","text":"\"मणिपुर वापस लौटकर उन्होंने कुछ ऐसा किया जिसकी परवाह आम तौर पर रिकॉर्ड की किताबें नहीं करतीं, लेकिन यह शेल्फ़ करता है: उन्होंने रेत के ट्रक चलाने वाले उन ड्राइवरों को ढूँढ निकाला जो इतने सालों तक गाँव की एक लड़की को प्रैक्टिस के लिए ले जाते रहे थे, और अपने गाँव में तोहफ़ों और दावत के साथ उनका शुक्रिया अदा किया। चैंपियन ट्रेनिंग से बनते हैं। वे उन सभी लोगों से भी बनते हैं जिन्होंने उन्हें आगे बढ़ने का सहारा दिया।\"","lang":"hi","body":"Back home in Manipur she did something the record books do not usually bother with, but this shelf does: she tracked down the sand-truck drivers who had carried a village girl to practice all those years, and thanked them with gifts and a feast in her village. Champions are made of training. They are also made of everyone who gave them a lift.","art":"art/story/sm/kh-mirabai.jpg","route":"#/story/kh.mirabai|h4","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Khel — India at Play"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-ny.kurien-0":{"src":"passage:hi:story:ny.kurien:0","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Milkman of India","text":"1949 की बात है, केरल के कोझिकोड के रहने वाले वर्गीज़ कुरियन नाम के एक युवा इंजीनियर को सरकार ने गुजरात के आणंद नाम के एक छोटे, धूल भरे शहर में एक डेयरी में काम करने का आदेश दिया। उन्होंने धातु विज्ञान की पढ़ाई की थी — यानी धातुओं की, दूध की नहीं। वे वहाँ जाना नहीं चाहते थे, वहाँ पहुँचे तो उन्हें बिल्कुल अच्छा नहीं लगा, और उन्होंने तय कर लिया था कि जैसे ही उनका बॉन्ड पूरा होगा, वे उसी पल वहाँ से निकल जाएँगे। यह बात याद रखिएगा, क्योंकि इसी वजह से आगे जो हुआ, वह और भी मज़ेदार लगता है।","lang":"hi","body":"In 1949 a young engineer named Verghese Kurien, from Kozhikode in Kerala, was ordered by the government to a small dusty town in Gujarat called Anand, to work at a creamery. He had studied metallurgy — metals, not milk. He did not want to go, he did not like it when he got there, and he planned to leave the moment his bond was done. Remember that, because it makes what happened next funnier.","art":"art/story/sm/ny-kurien.jpg","route":"#/story/ny.kurien|h0","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Naya India — The Builders"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-ny.kurien-1":{"src":"passage:hi:story:ny.kurien:1","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Milkman of India","text":"आणंद में उन्होंने देखा कि किसानों का भारी शोषण हो रहा था। किसान तड़के सूरज निकलने से पहले उठते, अपनी भैंसों का दूध दुहते, और बिचौलियों को औने-पौने दामों पर दूध बेचने के लिए मजबूर थे — अक्सर ना के बराबर पैसे मिलते, जबकि वही दूध बॉम्बे में कई गुना ज़्यादा दाम पर बेचा जाता था। त्रिभुवनदास पटेल नाम के एक शांत स्थानीय नेता की अगुआई में किसानों ने एक सहकारी संस्था (कोऑपरेटिव) शुरू की थी: एक ऐसी डेयरी, जिसके मालिक किसान ख़ुद थे।","lang":"hi","body":"In Anand he found farmers who were being squeezed. They rose before dawn, milked their buffaloes, and had no choice but to sell to middlemen for whatever was offered — often next to nothing, while the milk was sold on in Bombay for many times more. The farmers, led by a quiet local organiser named Tribhuvandas Patel, had started a cooperative: a dairy owned by the farmers themselves.","art":"art/story/sm/ny-kurien.jpg","route":"#/story/ny.kurien|h1","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Naya India — The Builders"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-ny.kurien-2":{"src":"passage:hi:story:ny.kurien:2","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Milkman of India","text":"जो इंजीनियर वहाँ से भागना चाहता था, उसने पाया कि वह किसानों की मदद किए बिना रह ही नहीं पा रहा है। मशीनों को मरम्मत की ज़रूरत थी; उन्होंने ठीक कर दीं। डेयरी बनानी थी; उन्होंने बना दी। उनका बॉन्ड ख़त्म हो गया, और — जैसा कि उन्होंने ख़ुद अपनी आत्मकथा में हँसते हुए माना था, उन्हें ख़ुद भी ताज्जुब हुआ — वे वहीं रुक गए। किसानों की इस डेयरी को एक नया नाम मिला: अमूल, एक ऐसे शब्द से निकला जिसका मतलब होता है अनमोल।","lang":"hi","body":"The engineer who wanted to leave found he could not stop helping. The machines needed fixing; he fixed them. The dairy needed building; he built it. His bond ended, and — to his own lasting surprise, as he cheerfully admitted in his memoir — he stayed. The farmers’ dairy took a brand name: Amul, from a word meaning priceless.","art":"art/story/sm/ny-kurien.jpg","route":"#/story/ny.kurien|h2","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Naya India — The Builders"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-ny.kurien-3":{"src":"passage:hi:story:ny.kurien:3","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Milkman of India","text":"फिर सामने आई एक ऐसी मुश्किल, जिसे जानकारों ने नामुमकिन कह दिया था। तब तक दूध का पाउडर सिर्फ़ गाय के दूध से ही बनता था, और आणंद में दूध भैंसों का होता था। दुनिया भर के डेयरी विशेषज्ञों का कहना था कि भैंस के दूध से पाउडर बन ही नहीं सकता। कुरियन और उनके साथी एच. एम. दलाया ने इसे फिर भी कर दिखाया — दुनिया में पहली बार भैंस के दूध का पाउडर बना — और देखते ही देखते दूध की वह बाढ़, जो कभी गर्मी में ख़राब हो जाती थी, अब सँभाली जा सकती थी, एक जगह से दूसरी जगह भेजी जा सकती थी और बेची जा सकती थी। जो नामुमकिन लग रहा था, वह बस पहले कभी किया नहीं गया था।","lang":"hi","body":"Then came a problem the experts called impossible. Milk powder had only ever been made from cow’s milk, and Anand’s milk came from buffaloes. The world’s dairy authorities said it could not be done. Kurien and his colleague H. M. Dalaya did it anyway — the first buffalo-milk powder anywhere — and suddenly the flood of milk that once spoiled in the heat could be stored, moved and sold. The impossible turned out to be merely undone.","art":"art/story/sm/ny-kurien.jpg","route":"#/story/ny.kurien|h3","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Naya India — The Builders"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-ny.kurien-4":{"src":"passage:hi:story:ny.kurien:4","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Milkman of India","text":"सरकार ने उनसे आणंद के इस विचार को पूरे देश में ले जाने को कहा, और यह कार्यक्रम — 'ऑपरेशन फ़्लड' — दुनिया का सबसे बड़ा डेयरी विकास अभियान बन गया। गाँव-गाँव, राज्य-राज्य, लाखों किसान परिवार अपनी ख़ुद की मिल्क कोऑपरेटिव से जुड़ते चले गए। और 1998 में आँकड़ों में एक लगभग अविश्वसनीय बात सामने आई: भारत, जो कभी बाहर से दूध मँगवाता था, अब धरती के किसी भी देश से ज़्यादा दूध पैदा कर रहा था।","lang":"hi","body":"The government asked him to take the Anand idea to the whole country, and the programme — Operation Flood — became the largest dairy development the world had ever seen. Village by village, state by state, millions of farming families joined cooperatives they owned themselves. And in 1998 the almost unbelievable line appeared in the statistics: India, which had once imported milk, now produced more of it than any country on Earth.","art":"art/story/sm/ny-kurien.jpg","route":"#/story/ny.kurien|h4","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Naya India — The Builders"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-ny.infosys-0":{"src":"passage:hi:story:ny.infosys:0","title":"Read it in Hindi · Ten Thousand Rupees and Seven Engineers","text":"1981 की बात है, एन. आर. नारायण मूर्ति नाम के एक शांत स्वभाव वाले इंजीनियर एक सॉफ़्टवेयर कंपनी शुरू करना चाहते थे — और वो भी उस भारत में, जहाँ इस बात का कोई मतलब ही नहीं बनता था। तब कंप्यूटर बहुत कम हुआ करते थे, बाहर से मँगवाने में सालों लग जाते थे, और सॉफ़्टवेयर तो बस दूर-दराज के देशों का काम माना जाता था। उनके साथ इस सफ़र में कूदने के लिए छह साथी तैयार थे, और पैसे लगभग न के बराबर थे। शुरुआत के दस हज़ार रुपये ज़्यादातर उनकी पत्नी सुधा मूर्ति की बचत से आए — जो ख़ुद भी एक इंजीनियर थीं, और जिन्होंने अपने पति के इस नामुमकिन से सपने पर अपनी गाढ़ी कमाई लगा दी।","lang":"hi","body":"In 1981, a soft-spoken engineer named N. R. Narayana Murthy wanted to start a software company — in an India where that sentence barely made sense. Computers were rare, imports took forever, and software was something faraway countries did. He had six colleagues willing to jump with him, and almost no money. The starting capital, ten thousand rupees, came mostly from the savings of his wife, Sudha Murty — an engineer herself, who bet her rainy-day fund on her husband’s improbable idea.","art":"art/story/sm/ny-infosys.jpg","route":"#/story/ny.infosys|h0","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Naya India — The Builders"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-ny.infosys-1":{"src":"passage:hi:story:ny.infosys:1","title":"Read it in Hindi · Ten Thousand Rupees and Seven Engineers","text":"कंपनी का नाम रखा गया इंफ़ोसिस। उसका पहला दफ़्तर था एक घर का सामने वाला कमरा। और सोचने वाली बात तो यह है: एक ऐसी सॉफ़्टवेयर कंपनी, जिसके पास काफ़ी समय तक अपना एक कंप्यूटर तक नहीं था — क्योंकि उन दिनों बाहर से कंप्यूटर मँगवाने के काग़ज़ी काम में ही बरसों बीत जाते थे। वे दूसरों के कंप्यूटरों पर ग्राहकों का काम करते, इंतज़ार करते, और आगे बढ़ते रहते। लगभग दो साल बाद जब उनका अपना पहला कंप्यूटर आया, तो उसका स्वागत ठीक वैसे ही किया गया जैसे घर में किसी नए बच्चे के आने पर होता है।","lang":"hi","body":"The company was called Infosys. Its first office was the front room of a house. And here is a detail to sit with: a software company that could not, for a long time, even get a computer — the paperwork to import one took years in those days. They wrote work for clients on other people’s machines, and waited, and kept going. The first computer of their own arrived about two years in, and was received roughly the way families receive a new baby.","art":"art/story/sm/ny-infosys.jpg","route":"#/story/ny.infosys|h1","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Naya India — The Builders"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-ny.infosys-2":{"src":"passage:hi:story:ny.infosys:2","title":"Read it in Hindi · Ten Thousand Rupees and Seven Engineers","text":"वे असल में मशीनें नहीं बेच रहे थे। वे बेच रहे थे एक वादा: कि भारत में बैठी एक टीम दुनिया की सबसे बड़ी कंपनियों के लिए सॉफ़्टवेयर बना सकती है, उसे सही समय पर पहुँचा सकती है, और उस पर आँख मूँदकर भरोसा किया जा सकता है। भरोसा बनने में वक्त लगता है और टूटने में एक पल, और उन्होंने एक-एक काम और सब्र भरे एक-एक साल के साथ उस भरोसे को बनाया।","lang":"hi","body":"What they were selling, in the end, was not machines. It was a promise: that a team in India could write software for the biggest companies in the world, deliver it on time, and be trusted absolutely. Trust is slow to build and quick to lose, and they built it order by order, year after patient year.","art":"art/story/sm/ny-infosys.jpg","route":"#/story/ny.infosys|h2","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Naya India — The Builders"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-ny.infosys-3":{"src":"passage:hi:story:ny.infosys:3","title":"Read it in Hindi · Ten Thousand Rupees and Seven Engineers","text":"यह काम किसी की भी उम्मीद से कहीं बेहतर साबित हुआ। सात इंजीनियरों से शुरू होकर इंफ़ोसिस दुनिया की सबसे बड़ी सॉफ़्टवेयर कंपनियों में से एक बन गई। बेंगलुरु में उसका हरा-भरा परिसर — घास के मैदान, शीशे की इमारतें, हज़ारों युवा इंजीनियर — एक ऐसी जगह बन गया जिसे बाहर के देशों से आने वाले नेता ख़ास तौर पर देखने की माँग करते थे, क्योंकि वह उस भविष्य जैसा दिखता था जो भारत ने अपने हाथों से बनाया था।","lang":"hi","body":"It worked beyond anybody’s sensible guess. Infosys grew from seven engineers into one of the great software companies of the world. Its green campus in Bengaluru — lawns, glass, thousands of young engineers — became a place visiting leaders from other countries actually asked to see, because it looked like a future India had built for itself.","art":"art/story/sm/ny-infosys.jpg","route":"#/story/ny.infosys|h3","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Naya India — The Builders"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-ny.infosys-4":{"src":"passage:hi:story:ny.infosys:4","title":"Read it in Hindi · Ten Thousand Rupees and Seven Engineers","text":"और एक बात और, जो अपने आप में एक शांत क्रांति थी: संस्थापकों ने कंपनी की हिस्सेदारी अपने कर्मचारियों के साथ बाँटी, यहाँ तक कि ड्राइवरों और दफ़्तर के कर्मचारियों के साथ भी, और वह भी तब जब ऐसा करने का कोई चलन नहीं था। जब इंफ़ोसिस को कामयाबी मिली, तो वह कामयाबी हज़ारों आम घरों तक पहुँची — और मूर्ति जी हमेशा यही मानते थे कि कुछ भी बड़ा बनाने का असली मक़सद यही होता है।","lang":"hi","body":"And one more thing, quietly revolutionary: the founders shared ownership of the company with its employees, down to drivers and office staff, long before that was fashionable. When Infosys succeeded, the success spread through thousands of ordinary households — which was, Murthy always argued, the whole point of building anything.","art":"art/story/sm/ny-infosys.jpg","route":"#/story/ny.infosys|h4","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Naya India — The Builders"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-ny.sudha-letter-0":{"src":"passage:hi:story:ny.sudha-letter:0","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Postcard to Mr Tata","text":"1974 में, सुधा कुलकर्णी — जो बाद में सुधा मूर्ति बनीं — बैंगलोर में इंजीनियरिंग की एक होनहार छात्रा थीं। वे अक्सर कक्षा में अकेली महिला होती थीं और हमेशा अपनी क्लास में सबसे आगे रहती थीं। एक दिन नोटिस बोर्ड पर उन्हें टेल्को का एक विज्ञापन दिखा, जो ट्रक बनाने वाली मशहूर टाटा कंपनी थी। बढ़िया नौकरी, अच्छी तनख्वाह और दिलचस्प काम। और सबसे नीचे एक लाइन लिखी थी: महिला उम्मीदवार आवेदन न करें।","lang":"hi","body":"In 1974, Sudha Kulkarni — later Sudha Murty — was a star engineering student in Bangalore, usually the only woman in the room and usually at the top of the class. One day on a notice board she saw an advertisement from TELCO, the great Tata company that built trucks. Good job, good pay, interesting work. And at the bottom, one line: lady candidates need not apply.","art":"art/story/sm/ny-sudha-letter.jpg","route":"#/story/ny.sudha-letter|h0","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Naya India — The Builders"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-ny.sudha-letter-1":{"src":"passage:hi:story:ny.sudha-letter:1","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Postcard to Mr Tata","text":"इसके बाद जो हुआ, वह उन्होंने कई बार बताया है, और अपनी उस उम्र के गुस्से पर वे हमेशा हँस पड़ती हैं। उनके पास महँगे कागज़-कलम के पैसे नहीं थे, इसलिए उन्होंने एक पोस्टकार्ड उठाया — एक सादा सरकारी पोस्टकार्ड — और सीधे पूरे टाटा समूह के मुखिया, जे. आर. डी. टाटा को लिख भेजा कि टाटा जैसे सम्मानित घराने का सिर्फ़ महिला होने की वजह से उम्मीदवारों के लिए दरवाज़ा बंद करना सरासर नाइंसाफ़ी है।","lang":"hi","body":"She has described what happened next many times, always with a laugh at her own young indignation. She did not have money for fancy stationery, so she took a postcard — a plain government postcard — and wrote to the head of the whole Tata group, J. R. D. Tata himself, saying that it was unfair for a house as respected as Tata to shut a door on candidates simply for being women.","art":"art/story/sm/ny-sudha-letter.jpg","route":"#/story/ny.sudha-letter|h1","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Naya India — The Builders"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-ny.sudha-letter-2":{"src":"passage:hi:story:ny.sudha-letter:2","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Postcard to Mr Tata","text":"पुणे में इंटरव्यू के दौरान उन्होंने पूछे गए हर सवाल का जवाब दिया, और अपनी बात पूरी ईमानदारी से रखी। उन्होंने उन्हें नौकरी पर रख लिया। सुधा मूर्ति टेल्को के कारख़ाने में काम करने वाली पहली महिला इंजीनियर बनीं — रोज़ हज़ारों पुरुषों और सौ साल पुरानी आदतों वाली फ़ैक्टरी में जाना, और बस तब तक बेहतरीन काम करते रहना, जब तक कि सबको इसकी आदत न हो गई।","lang":"hi","body":"At the interview in Pune she answered everything they asked, and told them honestly what she thought. They hired her. Sudha Murty became the first woman engineer on the shop floor at TELCO — walking each day into a factory of thousands of men and a hundred years of habit, and simply doing excellent work until the strangeness wore off.","art":"art/story/sm/ny-sudha-letter.jpg","route":"#/story/ny.sudha-letter|h2","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Naya India — The Builders"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-ny.sudha-letter-3":{"src":"passage:hi:story:ny.sudha-letter:3","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Postcard to Mr Tata","text":"जो दरवाज़ा उन्होंने खोला था, वह उनके पीछे बंद नहीं हुआ। जहाँ कभी एक महिला इंजीनियर की कल्पना भी नहीं की जा सकती थी, वहाँ जल्द ही और भी महिलाएँ आ गईं — उस फ़ैक्टरी में और धीरे-धीरे हर जगह। सालों बाद उन्होंने अपनी कमाई और अपने जीवन के कई साल हज़ारों पुस्तकालय और स्कूल बनाने में लगाए, और यह कहानी सुनने वाले हर नौजवान को सुनाई।","lang":"hi","body":"The door she pushed open did not close behind her. Where one woman engineer had been unthinkable, there were soon more — at that factory and, slowly, everywhere. Years later she would use her own money and years of her life to build libraries and schools by the thousand, and to tell this story to every young audience that would listen.","art":"art/story/sm/ny-sudha-letter.jpg","route":"#/story/ny.sudha-letter|h3","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Naya India — The Builders"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-ny.isro-0":{"src":"passage:hi:story:ny.isro:0","title":"Read it in Hindi · From a Church Yard to Mars","text":"1963 में, भारत का अंतरिक्ष कार्यक्रम मछुआरों के एक छोटे से गाँव में समाया हुआ था। केरल के तट पर थुम्बा नाम की जगह पर, स्थानीय चर्च समुदाय ने वैज्ञानिकों को काम करने के लिए अपने चर्च की इमारत और बिशप का घर दे दिया — वेदी वाला हिस्सा दफ़्तर बन गया, आँगन उपकरणों से भर गया, और ए. पी. जे. अब्दुल कलाम नाम के एक युवा इंजीनियर उस टीम में शामिल थे जो वहाँ भारत के पहले रॉकेट जोड़ रही थी।","lang":"hi","body":"In 1963, India’s space programme fitted inside a fishing village. At Thumba, on the Kerala coast, the local church community lent the scientists their church building and the bishop’s house to work in — the altar end became an office, the yard filled with equipment, and a young engineer named A. P. J. Abdul Kalam was among the team assembling India’s first rockets there.","art":"art/story/sm/ny-isro.jpg","route":"#/story/ny.isro|h0","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Naya India — The Builders"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-ny.isro-1":{"src":"passage:hi:story:ny.isro:1","title":"Read it in Hindi · From a Church Yard to Mars","text":"उस ज़माने की एक ऐसी तस्वीर है जिसे देखकर भारतीयों का दिल कभी नहीं भरता: साइकिल के पीछे रॉकेट का नोज़ कोन ले जाया जा रहा है। पुर्जे साइकिल और बैलगाड़ी से ढोए गए, क्योंकि उस वक़्त जो साधन था, वही था। और उसी माँगे हुए चर्च के अहाते से, नवंबर 1963 में, भारत का पहला रॉकेट समंदर के किनारे से उठकर आसमान में उड़ गया।","lang":"hi","body":"There is a photograph from those days that Indians never tire of: a rocket nose cone being carried on the back of a bicycle. Parts went by bicycle and bullock cart because that is what there was. And from that borrowed church yard, in November 1963, India’s first rocket rose off the beach and into the sky.","art":"art/story/sm/ny-isro.jpg","route":"#/story/ny.isro|h1","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Naya India — The Builders"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-ny.isro-2":{"src":"passage:hi:story:ny.isro:2","title":"Read it in Hindi · From a Church Yard to Mars","text":"उस समंदर किनारे से जो संस्था पनपी, उसका नाम है इसरो, और उसने साइकिल वाले दिनों की एक आदत हमेशा-हमेशा के लिए बनाए रखी: काम सादगी से करो, कम ख़र्च में करो, और ज़रा भी बर्बादी मत होने दो। दुनिया की दूसरी अंतरिक्ष एजेंसियों के पास पैसों के पहाड़ थे। इसरो के पास थी समझदारी, सब्र, और ऐसे इंजीनियर जो एक-एक रुपये का ख़याल किसी मुसाफ़िर की तरह रखते थे।","lang":"hi","body":"The organisation that grew from that beach is called ISRO, and it kept one habit from the bicycle days forever: do it simply, do it cheaply, waste nothing. Other space agencies had mountains of money. ISRO had cleverness, patience, and engineers who treated every rupee like a passenger.","art":"art/story/sm/ny-isro.jpg","route":"#/story/ny.isro|h2","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Naya India — The Builders"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-ny.isro-3":{"src":"passage:hi:story:ny.isro:3","title":"Read it in Hindi · From a Church Yard to Mars","text":"2013 में इसरो ने मंगल की ओर जाने वाला अंतरिक्ष यान 'मंगलयान' छोड़ा — और सितंबर 2014 में वह पहली ही कोशिश में उस लाल ग्रह की कक्षा में पहुँच गया, जो आज तक कोई भी देश पहली बार में नहीं कर पाया था। इस पूरे मिशन का कुल ख़र्च हॉलीवुड की अंतरिक्ष वाली किसी एक फ़िल्म के बजट से भी कम था। दुनियाभर के वैज्ञानिकों ने उस आँकड़े को दो-दो बार जाँचकर देखा।","lang":"hi","body":"In 2013 ISRO launched Mangalyaan, a spacecraft to Mars — and in September 2014 it slipped into orbit around the red planet on the very first attempt, something no nation had ever managed first time. The bill for the whole mission was famously smaller than the budget of a single Hollywood space film. Scientists around the world checked that number twice.","art":"art/story/sm/ny-isro.jpg","route":"#/story/ny.isro|h3","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Naya India — The Builders"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-ny.isro-4":{"src":"passage:hi:story:ny.isro:4","title":"Read it in Hindi · From a Church Yard to Mars","text":"फिर बारी आई चाँद की। इससे पहले वाला लैंडर पूरे देश की आँखों के सामने क्रैश हो गया था — अंतरिक्ष ग़लती माफ़ नहीं करता, और इसरो ने यह बात साफ़-साफ़ मानी, जो ख़राबी थी उसे सुधारा, और दोबारा पहुँचा। 23 अगस्त 2023 को, चंद्रयान-3 ने चाँद के दक्षिणी ध्रुव के पास अपना लैंडर हौले से उतार दिया — उस इलाक़े में उतरने वाला दुनिया का यह पहला अंतरिक्ष यान था — और एक नन्हा-सा रोवर बाहर निकलकर उस मिट्टी पर भारत के पहियों के निशान छोड़ आया, जहाँ पहले कभी कोई गाड़ी नहीं चली थी।","lang":"hi","body":"Then the Moon. An earlier lander had crashed, in full view of a watching country — space is unforgiving, and ISRO said so plainly, fixed what failed, and went back. On the twenty-third of August 2023, Chandrayaan-3 set its lander down gently near the Moon’s south pole — the first spacecraft from any nation to land in that region — and a little rover rolled out and left India’s wheel-marks in soil where nothing had ever driven.","art":"art/story/sm/ny-isro.jpg","route":"#/story/ny.isro|h4","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Naya India — The Builders"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-ny.upi-0":{"src":"passage:hi:story:ny.upi:0","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Square That Ate the Wallet","text":"आज भारत की किसी भी गली में चाय की दुकान को देखिए। कप में चाय डलती है, जेब से फ़ोन निकलता है, धागे से लटके एक छोटे-से छपे हुए चौकोर कोड की तरफ़ एक सेकंड के लिए टिकता है — और पैसे पहुँच जाते हैं। दस रुपये, एक इंसान के बैंक खाते से निकलकर दूसरे के खाते में चले गए, उतनी ही देर में जितनी देर में आपने यह वाक्य पढ़ा। न कोई सिक्के, न कार्ड वाली मशीन, न छुट्टे गिनने का झंझट।","lang":"hi","body":"Watch a chai stall in any Indian street today. A cup is poured, a phone comes out, it points for a second at a small printed square hanging on a string — and the payment is done. Ten rupees, gone from one person’s bank account into the other’s, in about the time it took you to read this sentence. No coins, no card machine, no counting change.","art":"art/story/sm/ny-upi.jpg","route":"#/story/ny.upi|h0","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Naya India — The Builders"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-ny.upi-1":{"src":"passage:hi:story:ny.upi:1","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Square That Ate the Wallet","text":"\"इस कहानी का कोई एक अकेला हीरो नहीं है, और यही इसकी असली बात है। इसके पीछे काम करने वाली मशीन को यूपीआई कहते हैं, और इसे एनपीसीआई ने बनाया था — एक ऐसी संस्था जिसे भारत के बैंकों ने मिलकर बनाया था, मुनाफ़ा कमाने के लिए नहीं, बल्कि पैसों के लेन-देन के लिए एक साझी पाइपलाइन बिछाने के लिए, ठीक वैसे ही जैसे कोई शहर ऐसी सड़कें बनाता है जिनका इस्तेमाल हर गाड़ी कर सके। यूपीआई की शुरुआत 2016 में हुई थी।\"","lang":"hi","body":"This story has no single hero, and that is the point of it. The machine underneath is called UPI, and it was built by NPCI — an organisation India’s banks set up together, not to make a profit but to build shared plumbing for money, the way a city builds roads that every car may use. UPI switched on in 2016.","art":"art/story/sm/ny-upi.jpg","route":"#/story/ny.upi|h1","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Naya India — The Builders"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-ny.upi-2":{"src":"passage:hi:story:ny.upi:2","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Square That Ate the Wallet","text":"\"इसकी सबसे समझदारी भरी बात यह है कि यूपीआई क्या नहीं है। यह किसी एक कंपनी का ऐप नहीं है। कोई भी बैंक इससे जुड़ सकता है, कोई भी ऐप इसमें शामिल हो सकता है, और एक ऐप वाला व्यक्ति किसी बिल्कुल अलग ऐप वाले व्यक्ति को पैसे भेज सकता है — ठीक वैसे ही जैसे किन्हीं भी दो फ़ोन के बीच फ़ोन कॉल काम करती है। और आम लोगों के लिए पैसे भेजने का कोई ख़र्च नहीं लगता।\"","lang":"hi","body":"The clever part is what UPI is not. It is not one company’s app. Any bank can join, any app can plug in, and a person on one app can pay a person on a completely different one — the way a phone call works between any two phones. And for ordinary people, sending money costs nothing.","art":"art/story/sm/ny-upi.jpg","route":"#/story/ny.upi|h2","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Naya India — The Builders"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-ny.upi-3":{"src":"passage:hi:story:ny.upi:3","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Square That Ate the Wallet","text":"\"और सबने यही किया। सब्ज़ी के ठेले, मंदिर की दान-पेटियाँ, ऑटो-रिक्शा, शादियों के तोहफ़ों वाले काउंटर — वह छोटा-सा चौकोर कोड हर जगह पहुँच गया, क्योंकि उसे छापने में लगभग कुछ भी ख़र्च नहीं होता। कई देशों को नक़दी से चेक और फिर कार्ड तक पहुँचने में सौ साल लग गए। पर ज़्यादातर भारत कुछ ही सालों में सीधे नक़द से फ़ोन पर आ गया, और आज यूपीआई हर महीने अरबों पेमेंट्स संभालता है — यह धरती के सबसे व्यस्त तुरंत-भुगतान सिस्टम्स में से एक है।\"","lang":"hi","body":"And everyone did. Vegetable carts, temple donation boxes, auto-rickshaws, wedding gift counters — the little square went everywhere, because printing one costs almost nothing. Many countries had leapt from cash to cheques to cards over a century. Much of India jumped straight from cash to the phone in a handful of years, and today UPI carries billions of payments every single month — among the busiest instant-payment systems on Earth.","art":"art/story/sm/ny-upi.jpg","route":"#/story/ny.upi|h3","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Naya India — The Builders"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-ny.upi-4":{"src":"passage:hi:story:ny.upi:4","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Square That Ate the Wallet","text":"\"इसकी सबसे शांत बात ही इसकी सबसे निष्पक्ष बात है। कार्ड की मशीन पर इतना ख़र्च आता था जो कोई छोटा दुकानदार कभी नहीं कर सकता था, इसलिए कार्ड बड़ी दुकानों की चीज़ थे। कागज़ के एक चौकोर टुकड़े को छापने में बस एक रुपया लगता है — इसलिए सबसे छोटी गली के सबसे छोटे चायवाले को भी वही पेमेंट सिस्टम मिल गया जो मॉल की सबसे बड़ी दुकान को मिला था। वही चौकोर डिब्बा, वही एक सेकंड, वही पटरी।\"","lang":"hi","body":"The quietest part is the fairest part. A card machine cost more than a small vendor could ever spend, so cards belonged to big shops. A paper square costs a rupee to print — so the smallest chaiwala in the smallest lane got the same payment system as the grandest store in the mall. The same square, the same second, the same rails.","art":"art/story/sm/ny-upi.jpg","route":"#/story/ny.upi|h4","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Naya India — The Builders"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-ny.flipkart-0":{"src":"passage:hi:story:ny.flipkart:0","title":"Read it in Hindi · Two Bansals and a Bookshop in the Air","text":"\"2007 में, बेंगलुरु के दो युवा इंजीनियरों ने — सचिन बंसल और बिन्नी बंसल, एक जैसा सरनेम, कोई रिश्तेदारी नहीं, एक ऐसा इत्तेफ़ाक जिसे वे ज़िंदगी भर समझाते रहे — अपनी आरामदेह नौकरियाँ छोड़ दीं ताकि कुछ ऐसा कर सकें जो उस समय भारत के ज़्यादातर लोगों को मज़ाकिया लगता था: बिना दुकान की एक दुकान। किताबें बेचने वाली एक वेबसाइट, जो कोरमंगला के एक फ़्लैट के दो कमरों से और अपनी बचत के कुछ लाख रुपयों के सहारे चलती थी।\"","lang":"hi","body":"In 2007, two young engineers in Bengaluru — Sachin Bansal and Binny Bansal, same surname, no relation, a coincidence they explained for the rest of their lives — quit comfortable jobs to try something most of India found funny at the time: a shop with no shop. A website that sold books, run from a couple of rooms in a Koramangala flat, on a few lakh rupees of their own savings.","art":"art/story/sm/ny-flipkart.jpg","route":"#/story/ny.flipkart|h0","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Naya India — The Builders"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-ny.flipkart-1":{"src":"passage:hi:story:ny.flipkart:1","title":"Read it in Hindi · Two Bansals and a Bookshop in the Air","text":"\"शक करने वालों की बात में दम तो था। 2007 के भारत में, शायद ही कोई चीज़ों के लिए ऑनलाइन पैसे चुकाता था। पार्सल तो रास्ते में ही ग़ायब हो जाते थे। भला कोई किसी वेबसाइट पर पैसे भेजकर यह भरोसा क्यों करता कि पार्सल घर आ ही जाएगा? ऐसा भरोसा तब था ही नहीं। उसे धीरे-धीरे बनाना पड़ा — एक बार में एक पार्सल पहुँचाकर।\"","lang":"hi","body":"The doubters had a real point. In the India of 2007, hardly anyone paid for things online. Deliveries went missing. Why would anyone send money into a website and trust that a parcel would come? That trust did not exist. It had to be manufactured — one parcel at a time.","art":"art/story/sm/ny-flipkart.jpg","route":"#/story/ny.flipkart|h1","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Naya India — The Builders"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-ny.flipkart-2":{"src":"passage:hi:story:ny.flipkart:2","title":"Read it in Hindi · Two Bansals and a Bookshop in the Air","text":"\"कंपनी का सबसे पहला ऑर्डर तो एक ऐसी दास्तान है जिसके पक्के सबूत आज भी मौजूद हैं: एक किताब, जिसे किसी बड़े शहर की किताबों की दुकान से बहुत दूर रहने वाले एक ग्राहक ने ऑर्डर किया था — एक ऐसी वेबसाइट पर दांव लगाकर, जिसका नाम तब किसी ने सुना भी नहीं था। यहाँ से पार्सल निकला, वहाँ किताब पहुँची, और उस ग्राहक ने यह बात औरों को बताई। निभाया गया वही एक अकेला वादा, जब करोड़ों बार दोहराया गया, तो बस वही भारतीय ऑनलाइन शॉपिंग की पूरी कहानी बन गया।\"","lang":"hi","body":"The very first order is company legend with the receipts to prove it: one book, ordered by a customer far from any big city bookshop, who took the gamble on a website nobody had heard of. The parcel went out, the book arrived, the customer told people. That single kept promise, multiplied by millions, is essentially the whole story of Indian online shopping.","art":"art/story/sm/ny-flipkart.jpg","route":"#/story/ny.flipkart|h2","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Naya India — The Builders"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-ny.flipkart-3":{"src":"passage:hi:story:ny.flipkart:3","title":"Read it in Hindi · Two Bansals and a Bookshop in the Air","text":"\"किताबों से शुरुआत होकर यह शेल्फ़ बढ़ता गया — और फ्लिपकार्ट भारतीय इंटरनेट की सबसे अहम कंपनियों में शुमार हो गई, वही कंपनी जिसने पूरे देश को 'खरीदें' वाले बटन पर भरोसा करना सिखाया। निवेशकों ने इतनी बड़ी बनने वाली नई कंपनियों को कहानियों की किताब वाले एक ख़ास शब्द से पुकारना शुरू किया: यूनिकॉर्न। जब भारत ने अपने यूनिकॉर्न गिनने शुरू किए, तो एक फ़्लैट से चलने वाली किताबों की यह दुकान उस झुंड की पहली सदस्य थी।\"","lang":"hi","body":"From books, the shelf grew — and Flipkart grew into one of the defining companies of the Indian internet, the one that taught a country it could trust the buy button. Investors came to describe young companies that grow that large with a storybook word: a unicorn. When India began counting its unicorns, this bookshop-from-a-flat was the herd’s first.","art":"art/story/sm/ny-flipkart.jpg","route":"#/story/ny.flipkart|h3","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Naya India — The Builders"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-ny.nykaa-0":{"src":"passage:hi:story:ny.nykaa:0","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Bell She Rang at Fifty","text":"\"फाल्गुनी नायर ने, अगर समझदारी से देखा जाए, तो ज़िंदगी की सबसे ऊँची चढ़ाई पूरी कर ली थी। वह मुंबई की सबसे वरिष्ठ बैंकरों में से एक थीं, हर जगह उनका बहुत सम्मान था, और उनके दोनों जुड़वाँ बच्चे भी बड़े हो चुके थे। और फिर 2012 में, लगभग पचास की उम्र में, वह यह सब कुछ छोड़कर बिल्कुल नए सिरे से एक कंपनी शुरू करने निकल पड़ीं — वह भी ब्यूटी प्रोडक्ट्स के क्षेत्र में, जिसमें उन्होंने पहले कभी काम नहीं किया था।\"","lang":"hi","body":"Falguni Nayar had, by any sensible measure, finished the climbing part of life. She was one of the most senior bankers in Mumbai, respected everywhere, her twin children grown. And in 2012, at nearly fifty, she walked away from all of it to start a brand-new company from scratch — in beauty products, an industry she had never worked in.","art":"art/story/sm/ny-nykaa.jpg","route":"#/story/ny.nykaa|h0","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Naya India — The Builders"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-ny.nykaa-1":{"src":"passage:hi:story:ny.nykaa:1","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Bell She Rang at Fifty","text":"\"उनका विचार बिल्कुल साफ़ और अडिग था: भारतीय महिलाओं के पास मेकअप और त्वचा की देखभाल का सामान खरीदने के लिए एक भरोसेमंद जगह होनी ही चाहिए, जहाँ ईमानदार सलाह, असली रिव्यू और असली सामान मिले — चाहे वे दक्षिण मुंबई में रहती हों या किसी ब्यूटी स्टोर से दिन भर के सफ़र जितनी दूर किसी छोटे से कस्बे में। उन्होंने इसका नाम रखा नायका, जो निकला था 'नायिका' से: यानी कहानी की हीरोइन। ज़रा ध्यान दीजिए, हीरोइन — हीरोइन की कोई सहेली या मददगार नहीं।\"","lang":"hi","body":"Her idea was plain and stubborn: Indian women deserved a trustworthy place to buy makeup and skincare, with honest advice, real reviews and genuine products — whether they lived in south Mumbai or in a small town a day’s journey from any beauty counter. She named it Nykaa, from nayika: the heroine of a story. The heroine, note — not the sidekick.","art":"art/story/sm/ny-nykaa.jpg","route":"#/story/ny.nykaa|h1","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Naya India — The Builders"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-ny.nykaa-2":{"src":"passage:hi:story:ny.nykaa:2","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Bell She Rang at Fifty","text":"शुरुआती साल उस बिना चमक-दमक वाली कठिन मेहनत के दिन थे, जो कभी मुख्य सुर्खियों में नहीं दिखती — गोदाम, डिलीवरी, किसी नए चेहरे पर भरोसा करने के लिए मशहूर ब्रांड्स को मनाना, और अपने चेहरों के लिए एक वेबसाइट पर यकीन करने के लिए ग्राहकों को राज़ी करना। स्टार्टअप की दुनिया के नौजवान लड़कों से वह उम्र में दशकों बड़ी थीं, और उन्होंने इस बात को तूल देने लायक समझा ही नहीं।","lang":"hi","body":"The early years were the unglamorous kind of hard that never makes the highlight reel — warehouses, deliveries, convincing famous brands to trust a newcomer, convincing customers to trust a website with their faces. She was decades older than the boys of the startup world, and she simply declined to find that interesting.","art":"art/story/sm/ny-nykaa.jpg","route":"#/story/ny.nykaa|h2","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Naya India — The Builders"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-ny.nykaa-3":{"src":"passage:hi:story:ny.nykaa:3","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Bell She Rang at Fifty","text":"नौ साल तक कंपनी को खड़ा करने के बाद, नवंबर 2021 में नायका को स्टॉक एक्सचेंज में लिस्ट किया गया — और अपने परिवार के साथ और अपनी टीम के बीच, फाल्गुनी नायर ने मुंबई के मंच पर खड़े होकर बाज़ार की शुरुआत की घंटी बजाई। पचास साल की उम्र में जो कंपनी उन्होंने शुरू की थी, वह अब भारत की सबसे चर्चित लिस्टिंग में से एक थी, और पहले ही दिन से एक महिला द्वारा बनाई और चलाई गई भारत की पहली बड़ी इंटरनेट कंपनियों में से एक थी।","lang":"hi","body":"Nine years of building later, in November 2021, Nykaa was listed on the stock exchange — and Falguni Nayar stood on the platform in Mumbai and rang the opening bell, with her family beside her and her team around her. The company she had started at fifty was now one of the most talked-about listings in India, and one of the first big Indian internet companies built and led by a woman from day one.","art":"art/story/sm/ny-nykaa.jpg","route":"#/story/ny.nykaa|h3","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Naya India — The Builders"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-ny.nykaa-4":{"src":"passage:hi:story:ny.nykaa:4","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Bell She Rang at Fifty","text":"उस घंटी की गूंज बहुत दूर तक सुनाई देती है। जब भी यह कहानी सुनाई जाती है, कहीं न कहीं कोई ऐसा इंसान, जिसने चुपचाप यह मान लिया था कि वह अपने आइडिया के लिए बहुत बूढ़ा हो चुका है, अपनी सोच का हिसाब फिर से लगाता है।","lang":"hi","body":"Rings of that bell are heard a long way. Somewhere, every time this story is told, someone who had quietly decided they were too old for their own idea does a small recalculation.","art":"art/story/sm/ny-nykaa.jpg","route":"#/story/ny.nykaa|h4","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Naya India — The Builders"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-ny.oyo-0":{"src":"passage:hi:story:ny.oyo:0","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Teenager Who Slept in a Hundred Guest Houses","text":"रितेश अग्रवाल ओडिशा के एक छोटे से कस्बे बिसम कटक में दुकानदारों के एक परिवार में पले-बढ़े। जब वे किशोर थे, उन्हें घूमने-फिरने का शौक लग गया — और जेब में बहुत कम पैसे होने की वजह से, वे वहीं ठहरते जहाँ बहुत कम पैसे वाले ठहरते हैं: सस्ते गेस्ट हाउस। टूटे हुए नल, न जाने कैसी चादरें, और इधर-उधर गायब रहने वाले रिसेप्शनिस्ट। ज़्यादातर यात्री बड़बड़ाते और भूल जाते। उन्होंने बड़बड़ाया भी और अपनी डायरी में नोट भी किया।","lang":"hi","body":"Ritesh Agarwal grew up in Bissam Cuttack, a small town in Odisha, in a family of shopkeepers. As a teenager he fell in love with travelling — and, having very little money, he stayed where very little money stays: cheap guest houses. Broken taps, mystery bedsheets, receptionists who had wandered off. Most travellers grumbled and forgot. He grumbled and took notes.","art":"art/story/sm/ny-oyo.jpg","route":"#/story/ny.oyo|h0","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Naya India — The Builders"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-ny.oyo-1":{"src":"passage:hi:story:ny.oyo:1","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Teenager Who Slept in a Hundred Guest Houses","text":"जब तक वे ऐसे लगभग सौ गेस्ट हाउसों में ठहरे, उनकी नोटबुक में एक बात साफ़ हो गई थी: परेशानी यह नहीं थी कि सस्ते कमरे मौजूद थे, बल्कि यह थी कि मुसाफिर को कभी पता ही नहीं होता था कि उसे क्या मिलने वाला है। एक गेस्ट हाउस बहुत बढ़िया निकलता, तो अगला एकदम बेकार, और बाहर से देखकर यह जानने का कोई तरीका नहीं था कि कौन-सा कैसा है।","lang":"hi","body":"By the time he had stayed in about a hundred of them, his notebook held a pattern: the problem was not that cheap rooms existed, but that a traveller could never know what they were getting. One guest house was a gem, the next a disaster, and nothing on the outside told you which.","art":"art/story/sm/ny-oyo.jpg","route":"#/story/ny.oyo|h1","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Naya India — The Builders"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-ny.oyo-2":{"src":"passage:hi:story:ny.oyo:2","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Teenager Who Slept in a Hundred Guest Houses","text":"अठारह साल की उम्र में वह दिल्ली आ गया और अपना काम शुरू किया — पहले ठहरने की जगहों की लिस्ट बनाने वाली एक वेबसाइट, जिसने उसे सिखाया कि उसका अंदाज़ा आधा गलत था, और फिर 2013 में सुधरा हुआ विचार: ओयो, जिसने बुनियादी चीज़ों को ठीक करने के लिए गेस्ट हाउसों के साथ मिलकर काम किया — साफ़ चादरें, चालू शावर, सच्ची तस्वीरें — ताकि ओयो का कमरा बुक करने वाले किसी भी मुसाफ़िर को पता रहे कि उसे क्या मिलेगा। उसी साल, नौजवान संस्थापकों के लिए बनी एक ग्लोबल फ़ेलोशिप ने दुनिया भर के आवेदकों में से उसे चुना, और कॉलेज जाने के बजाय अपनी कंपनी खड़ी करने के लिए उसे पैसे दिए।","lang":"hi","body":"At eighteen he moved to Delhi and started up — first a site for listing stays, which taught him his idea was half-wrong, and then, in 2013, the corrected idea: OYO, which worked with guest houses to fix the basics — clean sheets, working shower, honest photos — so a traveller booking an OYO room knew what they would get. That same year, a global fellowship for young founders picked him from applicants around the world, and paid him to build his company instead of going to college.","art":"art/story/sm/ny-oyo.jpg","route":"#/story/ny.oyo|h2","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Naya India — The Builders"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-ny.oyo-3":{"src":"passage:hi:story:ny.oyo:3","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Teenager Who Slept in a Hundred Guest Houses","text":"उस शुरुआत के बाद, ओयो पूरे भारत और उससे भी कहीं आगे हज़ारों छोटे होटलों तक फैल गया, और आगे की राह में नई कंपनियों वाला हर मौसम देखने को मिला — अच्छे साल भी और मुश्किल साल भी। लेकिन शुरुआत की वह बात अपनी जगह कायम है: ओडिशा के एक छोटे से शहर के एक दुकानदार के बेटे ने भारत में सफ़र की सबसे आम परेशानी को देखा और तय किया कि इसे वही सुलझाएगा।","lang":"hi","body":"From that start, OYO spread to thousands of small hotels across India and far beyond, with the road ahead holding the usual weather of young companies — good years and hard ones alike. But the founding itself stands: a shopkeeper’s son from a small Odisha town looked at the most ordinary annoyance in Indian travel and decided it was his to solve.","art":"art/story/sm/ny-oyo.jpg","route":"#/story/ny.oyo|h3","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Naya India — The Builders"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-rah.kiran-0":{"src":"passage:hi:story:rah.kiran:0","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Brewmaster Nobody Would Hire","text":"किरण मजूमदार 1950 और 60 के दशक में बैंगलोर में पली-बढ़ीं। वे एक मुख्य ब्रूमास्टर की बेटी थीं — और उन्हें बीयर से नहीं, बल्कि उसके पीछे के विज्ञान से प्यार हो गया: किण्वन यानी फर्मेंटेशन, वह पुराना हुनर जिसके ज़रिए खमीर और एंज़ाइम जैसे न दिखने वाले सूक्ष्म जीव चुपचाप एक चीज़ को दूसरी चीज़ में बदल देते हैं। वे अच्छी तरह ब्रूइंग की पढ़ाई करने ऑस्ट्रेलिया गईं और अपनी कक्षा में सबसे आगे रहीं।","lang":"hi","body":"Kiran Mazumdar grew up in Bangalore in the 1950s and 60s, the daughter of a head brewmaster — and she fell in love not with beer but with the science underneath it: fermentation, the ancient trick by which invisible living things, yeasts and enzymes, quietly turn one substance into another. She went to Australia to study brewing properly, and finished at the top of her class.","art":"art/story/sm/rah-kiran.jpg","route":"#/story/rah.kiran|h0","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Rah Banane Wale — The Pathbreakers"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-rah.kiran-1":{"src":"passage:hi:story:rah.kiran:1","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Brewmaster Nobody Would Hire","text":"फिर वे अपनी डिग्री लेकर घर लौटीं — और देखा कि उनके काम के सारे दरवाज़े बंद थे। 1970 के दशक के भारत में एक के बाद एक हर ब्रूअरी ने उनसे वही कहा जो वे आज भी याद करती हैं: ब्रूहौस किसी औरत के संभालने की जगह नहीं है। न उनके नंबरों की कोई कद्र थी, न उनकी ट्रेनिंग की। जवाब बस एक ही था — 'ना'।","lang":"hi","body":"Then she came home with her qualification — and found every door in her field closed. Brewery after brewery told her, in the India of the 1970s, what she has retold ever since: the brewhouse was no place to put a woman in charge. Her marks did not matter. Her training did not matter. The answer was simply no.","art":"art/story/sm/rah-kiran.jpg","route":"#/story/rah.kiran|h1","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Rah Banane Wale — The Pathbreakers"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-rah.kiran-2":{"src":"passage:hi:story:rah.kiran:2","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Brewmaster Nobody Would Hire","text":"1978 में इंडस्ट्रियल एंज़ाइम बनाने वाली एक आयरिश कंपनी को भारत में एक साझीदार की तलाश थी, और उन्हें वह ब्रूमास्टर मिल गईं जिन्हें कोई नौकरी नहीं दे रहा था। पच्चीस साल की किरण ने बैंगलोर में अपने किराए के मकान के गैराज में लगभग दस हज़ार रुपयों से 'बायोकॉन इंडिया' की शुरुआत की। शुरुआती दिन लगातार इनकार से भरे थे: बैंक किसी ऐसी युवा महिला को कर्ज़ देने को तैयार नहीं थे, जो एक ऐसे शब्द पर कंपनी चला रही थी — बायोटेक्नोलॉजी — जो किसी बैंक मैनेजर ने कभी सुना ही नहीं था।","lang":"hi","body":"In 1978 an Irish company that made industrial enzymes went looking for an Indian partner, and found the brewmaster nobody would hire. Kiran, twenty-five, started Biocon India in the garage of her rented house in Bangalore, with about ten thousand rupees. The early days were a museum of refusals: banks would not lend to a young woman running a company built on a word — biotechnology — that no bank manager had ever heard.","art":"art/story/sm/rah-kiran.jpg","route":"#/story/rah.kiran|h2","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Rah Banane Wale — The Pathbreakers"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-rah.kiran-3":{"src":"passage:hi:story:rah.kiran:3","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Brewmaster Nobody Would Hire","text":"फिर भी उस गैराज में काम शुरू हुआ, पपीते के फल से एंज़ाइम निकाले गए — और एक ही साल के भीतर, यह नन्हीं कंपनी यूरोप और अमेरिका को एंज़ाइम भेजने लगी, ऐसा करने वाली यह पहली भारतीय कंपनी थी। जिस विज्ञान को भारत की ब्रूअरियों ने ठुकरा दिया था, अब उसे पीपों में भरकर पूरी दुनिया में भेजा जा रहा था।","lang":"hi","body":"The garage got to work anyway, coaxing enzymes out of papaya fruit — and within a year, this tiny company was exporting enzymes to Europe and America, the first Indian company ever to do so. The science India’s breweries had turned away was now being shipped, in barrels, to the world.","art":"art/story/sm/rah-kiran.jpg","route":"#/story/rah.kiran|h3","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Rah Banane Wale — The Pathbreakers"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-rah.kiran-4":{"src":"passage:hi:story:rah.kiran:4","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Brewmaster Nobody Would Hire","text":"फिर एक और बड़ा विचार आया: अगर एंज़ाइम बन सकते हैं, तो दवाइयाँ क्यों नहीं? बायोकॉन ने अपने फरमेंटर्स का रुख़ दवाइयों की तरफ़ मोड़ दिया — ख़ास तौर पर इंसुलिन, वह रोज़ की दवा जिसके बिना डायबिटीज़ से जूझ रहे लाखों भारतीय जी नहीं सकते, जिसे भारतीय स्तर पर और भारतीय दामों में बनाया गया। गैराज से शुरू हुई वह कंपनी भारत की सबसे बड़ी बायोटेक्नोलॉजी कंपनी बन गई। यह गैराज ही तो इस कहानी की असली जान है; और मिले हुए इनकार उसका ईंधन।","lang":"hi","body":"Then came the bigger idea: if enzymes, why not medicines? Biocon turned its fermenters toward pharmaceuticals — above all insulin, the daily medicine millions of Indians with diabetes cannot live without, made at Indian scale and Indian prices. The company from the garage grew into the biggest biotechnology company in India. The garage is the point of the story; the refusals are its fuel.","art":"art/story/sm/rah-kiran.jpg","route":"#/story/rah.kiran|h4","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Rah Banane Wale — The Pathbreakers"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-rah.hansa-0":{"src":"passage:hi:story:rah.hansa:0","title":"Read it in Hindi · All Human Beings","text":"हंसा मेहता 1897 में गुजरात के बड़ौदा के एक विद्वान परिवार में जन्मी थीं, और उन्होंने अपनी पूरी ज़िंदगी शिक्षा के नाम कर दी — उन्होंने गुजराती बच्चों के लिए किताबें लिखीं और अनुवाद कीं, जिनमें 'गुलिवर की यात्राएं' भी शामिल थीं, और स्कूल-कॉलेज बनवाए। वह भारत का संविधान लिखने वाली सभा की महज़ पंद्रह महिलाओं में से एक थीं; और आज़ादी की आधी रात को, 14 अगस्त 1947 के दिन, हंसा मेहता ने ही भारत की महिलाओं की ओर से सभा को राष्ट्रीय ध्वज सौंपा था। यह बात सभा के अपने रिकॉर्ड में दर्ज है।","lang":"hi","body":"Hansa Mehta was born in 1897 into a scholarly family of Baroda, in Gujarat, and spent her life on education — she wrote and translated books for Gujarati children, Gulliver’s adventures among them, and built schools and colleges. She was one of just fifteen women in the assembly that wrote India’s Constitution; and at the midnight hour of independence, 14 August 1947, it was Hansa Mehta who presented the national flag to the assembly on behalf of the women of India. That is in the assembly’s own record.","art":"art/story/sm/rah-hansa.jpg","route":"#/story/rah.hansa|h0","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Rah Banane Wale — The Pathbreakers"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-rah.hansa-1":{"src":"passage:hi:story:rah.hansa:1","title":"Read it in Hindi · All Human Beings","text":"1947 में उन्हें संयुक्त राष्ट्र भेजा गया, उस आयोग में जो दुनिया के लिए एक ऐसी चीज़ का मसौदा तैयार कर रहा था जो पहले कभी नहीं बनी थी: मानवाधिकारों का सार्वभौम घोषणापत्र — धरती के हर इंसान के हक़ के वादों की एक ऐसी सूची, जो उस युद्ध के साए में लिखी जा रही थी जिसने दिखाया था कि जब ऐसे वादे न हों तो क्या होता है। इसकी अध्यक्ष अमेरिका की एलिनॉर रूज़वेल्ट थीं। और इसके सबसे पहले अनुच्छेद के मसौदे की शुरुआत ऐसे हुई थी: “सभी पुरुष स्वतंत्र और समान पैदा होते हैं।”","lang":"hi","body":"In 1947 she was sent to the United Nations, to the commission drafting something the world had never had: the Universal Declaration of Human Rights — a promise-list belonging to every person on Earth, written in the shadow of a war that had shown what happens when such promises do not exist. The chair was Eleanor Roosevelt of America. And the draft of the very first article began: “All men are born free and equal.”","art":"art/story/sm/rah-hansa.jpg","route":"#/story/rah.hansa|h1","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Rah Banane Wale — The Pathbreakers"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-rah.hansa-2":{"src":"passage:hi:story:rah.hansa:2","title":"Read it in Hindi · All Human Beings","text":"कमरे में मौजूद ज़्यादातर लोगों को ये शब्द बिल्कुल ठीक लगे। सबका यही मानना था कि “सभी पुरुषों” का मतलब ज़ाहिर तौर पर हर किसी से है।","lang":"hi","body":"To most of the room, that wording seemed fine. “All men”, everyone agreed, obviously meant everyone.","art":"art/story/sm/rah-hansa.jpg","route":"#/story/rah.hansa|h2","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Rah Banane Wale — The Pathbreakers"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-rah.hansa-3":{"src":"passage:hi:story:rah.hansa:3","title":"Read it in Hindi · All Human Beings","text":"उनकी जीत हुई। जब दिसंबर 1948 में सार्वभौम घोषणापत्र को अपनाया गया, तो उसका पहला अनुच्छेद इस तरह पढ़ा गया — और आज भी पांच सौ से ज़्यादा भाषाओं में पढ़ा जाता है: “सभी मनुष्य गरिमा और अधिकारों के मामले में स्वतंत्र और बराबर पैदा होते हैं।” खुद संयुक्त राष्ट्र यह कहानी सुनाता है कि इन शब्दों पर किसने ज़ोर दिया था: भारत की हंसा मेहता ने। एक सजग पाठक द्वारा बदले गए महज़ दो शब्द, उस वाक्य में जिससे आज पूरी दुनिया शुरुआत करती है।","lang":"hi","body":"She won. When the Universal Declaration was adopted in December 1948, its first article read — and reads today, in over five hundred languages: “All human beings are born free and equal in dignity and rights.” The United Nations itself tells the story of who insisted on those words: Hansa Mehta of India. Two words, changed by one careful reader, in the sentence the whole world now begins with.","art":"art/story/sm/rah-hansa.jpg","route":"#/story/rah.hansa|h3","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Rah Banane Wale — The Pathbreakers"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-rah.hansa-4":{"src":"passage:hi:story:rah.hansa:4","title":"Read it in Hindi · All Human Beings","text":"फिर वह वतन लौटीं और निर्माण के काम में जुटी रहीं। जब 1949 में बड़ौदा की नई यूनिवर्सिटी खुली, तो हंसा मेहता उसकी पहली उप-कुलपति बनीं — एक विदुषी जो उस दौर में एक यूनिवर्सिटी चला रही थीं जब महिलाओं के लिए यह दरवाज़ा भी नहीं खुला था। उन्होंने अपनी ज़िंदगी सिर्फ़ एक पक्के विश्वास के साथ जी, जिसे उन्होंने हर जगह लागू किया: कि हर इंसान को, और उनका मतलब सचमुच 'हर' इंसान से था, सीखने और पढ़ने का सम्मान मिलना ही चाहिए।","lang":"hi","body":"Then she went home and kept building. When Baroda’s new university opened in 1949, Hansa Mehta led it as its first Vice-Chancellor — a scholar running a university at a time when that too was a door not yet open. She spent her life on exactly one conviction, applied everywhere: that every human being, and she did mean every, deserves the dignity of learning.","art":"art/story/sm/rah-hansa.jpg","route":"#/story/rah.hansa|h4","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Rah Banane Wale — The Pathbreakers"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-rah.ela-0":{"src":"passage:hi:story:rah.ela:0","title":"Read it in Hindi · A Bank of Four Thousand Sisters","text":"इला भट्ट अहमदाबाद में एक युवा वकील थीं — धीमी आवाज़ में बोलने वाली, खादी पहनने वाली और अक्सर किसी भी कमरे में सबसे शांत और सौम्य इंसान। वह उस शहर में कपड़ा मिल मज़दूरों की यूनियन के लिए काम कर रही थीं, जिसे गांधी जी ने ठीक इसी तरह के काम के लिए मशहूर किया था। लेकिन मिल के भीतर काम करने वाले मज़दूरों की तो यूनियन थी। इला की नज़र बार-बार मिल के बाहर काम करने वालों पर पड़ जाती: सिर पर कपड़ों के गट्ठर उठाए, हाथगाड़ियाँ खींचती, भोर होने से पहले घर पर पापड़ बेलती और टोकरियों में सब्ज़ियाँ बेचती औरतें। वे दिन भर कड़ी मेहनत करती थीं। और सरकारी तौर पर, उनका कोई वजूद ही नहीं था — न किसी रजिस्टर में उनका नाम था, न कोई कानून उनकी रक्षा करता था, क्योंकि वे किसी फ़ैक्ट्री की मुलाज़िम नहीं थीं।","lang":"hi","body":"Ela Bhatt was a young lawyer in Ahmedabad — soft-spoken, khadi-wearing, the gentlest person in most rooms — working for the textile workers’ union in the city Gandhi had made famous for exactly that kind of work. But the workers inside the mills had a union. Her eye kept catching the workers outside them: women carrying cloth bales on their heads, pulling handcarts, rolling papads at home before dawn, selling vegetables from baskets. They worked every daylight hour. And officially, they did not exist — no register counted them, no law protected them, because no factory owned them.","art":"art/story/sm/rah-ela.jpg","route":"#/story/rah.ela|h0","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Rah Banane Wale — The Pathbreakers"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-rah.ela-1":{"src":"passage:hi:story:rah.ela:1","title":"Read it in Hindi · A Bank of Four Thousand Sisters","text":"\"नियमों की किताबों में ऐसी औरतों के लिए एक शब्द था — स्वरोज़गार — और इसे कुछ न करने का बहाना बना लिया जाता था। इला भट्ट ने इसे दूसरी नज़र से देखा: अगर वे स्वरोज़गार करती हैं, तो वे मज़दूर हैं, और मज़दूरों की अपनी यूनियन हो सकती है। 1972 में उन्होंने 'सेवा' (सेल्फ़-एम्प्लॉयड विमेंस एसोसिएशन) की नींव रखी — एक ऐसी ट्रेड यूनियन, जिसकी नियमों की किताबों ने कभी कल्पना भी नहीं की थी। सदस्यता कार्ड की अहमियत उतनी ही बड़ी थी जितनी यूनियन की जीती हुई किसी भी चीज़ की: काग़ज़ का एक टुकड़ा, जिसने इन औरतों की ज़िंदगी में पहली बार कहा, मैं एक मज़दूर हूँ।\"","lang":"hi","body":"The rulebooks had a phrase for such women — self-employed — and treated it as a reason to do nothing. Ela Bhatt read it the other way: if they are self-employed, they are workers, and workers can have a union. In 1972 she founded SEWA, the Self-Employed Women’s Association — a trade union for women the rulebooks had never imagined. The membership card mattered as much as anything the union ever won: a piece of paper that said, for the first time in these women’s lives, I am a worker.","art":"art/story/sm/rah-ela.jpg","route":"#/story/rah.ela|h1","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Rah Banane Wale — The Pathbreakers"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-rah.ela-2":{"src":"passage:hi:story:rah.ela:2","title":"Read it in Hindi · A Bank of Four Thousand Sisters","text":"फिर पैसों की समस्या सामने आई। यूनियन की सदस्य रोज़ाना सिक्का-सिक्का जोड़कर कमाती थीं, पर एक पैसा भी सुरक्षित रखने की कोई जगह नहीं थी — और बैंक उन्हें अपने यहाँ फटकने नहीं देते थे। कुछ औरतें अपने दस्तख़त तक नहीं कर सकती थीं; किसी के पास भी बैंक की माँगी हुई ज़मीन-जायदाद या कागज़ात नहीं थे; वे कतारें और काउंटर किसी सब्ज़ी बेचने वाली के लिए नहीं बने थे, जो लाइन में खड़े होने भर से अपनी दिन भर की कमाई गँवा देती। और बैंक बदलने वाले नहीं थे।","lang":"hi","body":"Then came the money problem. The members earned coin by coin, daily, with no safe place to keep a paisa of it — and the banks would not have them. Some of the women could not sign their names; none had the papers and property a bank wanted; the queues and the counters were not built for a vegetable seller who loses a day’s income by standing in one. The banks were not going to change.","art":"art/story/sm/rah-ela.jpg","route":"#/story/rah.ela|h2","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Rah Banane Wale — The Pathbreakers"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-rah.ela-3":{"src":"passage:hi:story:rah.ela:3","title":"Read it in Hindi · A Bank of Four Thousand Sisters","text":"इसलिए 1974 में, 'सेवा' की लगभग चार हज़ार सदस्यों ने कुछ ऐसा किया जो अपनी सादगी में बेहद अनोखा था: सबने दस-दस रुपये जमा किए — दस रुपये, उन औरतों से जिन्हें बैंक लायक भी नहीं समझा जाता था — और अपना खुद का बैंक शुरू कर दिया। एक सहकारी बैंक, जिसकी मालिक खुद खाताधारक थीं, जो बोझा ढोने वाली, पापड़ बेलने वाली और ठेला खींचने वाली औरतों के लिए चलाया जाता था; और जो सदस्य दस्तख़त नहीं कर पाती थीं, बैंक ने उनके दस्तख़त की जगह उनकी तस्वीरें इस्तेमाल कीं। समस्या कभी यह थी ही नहीं कि औरतें बैंकिंग के लायक नहीं थीं। समस्या यह थी कि बैंकिंग को कभी उनके लायक बनाया ही नहीं गया था।","lang":"hi","body":"So in 1974, about four thousand SEWA members did something almost cheeky in its simplicity: they put in ten rupees each — ten rupees, from women counted as too poor to bank — and founded their own bank. A cooperative, owned by its account holders, run for headloaders and papad rollers and cart pullers; and for members who could not sign, the bank used photographs instead of signatures. The problem was never that the women did not fit banking. It was that banking had not yet been built to fit them.","art":"art/story/sm/rah-ela.jpg","route":"#/story/rah.ela|h3","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Rah Banane Wale — The Pathbreakers"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-rah.ela-4":{"src":"passage:hi:story:rah.ela:4","title":"Read it in Hindi · A Bank of Four Thousand Sisters","text":"बैंक टिका रहा और यूनियन बढ़ती गई — काम दर काम, शहर दर शहर, यहाँ तक कि 'सेवा' की सदस्यों की गिनती लाखों में पहुँच गई, और यह पूरी दुनिया में कामकाजी औरतों के सबसे बड़े संगठनों में से एक बन गया। जब इला भट्ट ने आखिरकार उनकी कहानी लिखी, तो उन्होंने किताब को एक ऐसा नाम दिया जो इस पूरी अलमारी की सारी किताबों का निचोड़ कह देता है: 'वी आर पुअर बट सो मेनी' (हम गरीब हैं पर हमारी गिनती बहुत है)।","lang":"hi","body":"The bank held, and the union grew — trade by trade, town by town, until SEWA counted its members in the millions, one of the largest organisations of working women anywhere on Earth. When Ela Bhatt finally wrote their story down, she gave the book a title that says everything this shelf could hope to: We Are Poor but So Many.","art":"art/story/sm/rah-ela.jpg","route":"#/story/rah.ela|h4","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Rah Banane Wale — The Pathbreakers"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-jt.golden-goose-0":{"src":"passage:hi:story:jt.golden-goose:0","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Goose Who Gave Gold","text":"एक आदमी की मौत हो गई और पीछे छूट गईं उसकी पत्नी और तीन बेटियाँ, और इसके अलावा लगभग कुछ भी नहीं। वे कपड़े सिलने का काम करने लगीं। वे कम-कम खाकर गुज़ारा करती थीं। घर में किसी ने भी बोलकर यह नहीं कहा कि दिन कितने तंगी भरे होते जा रहे हैं, क्योंकि कहने से कोई फ़ायदा नहीं होता।","lang":"hi","body":"A man died and left behind a wife and three daughters and almost nothing else. They took in sewing. They ate small. Nobody in the house said out loud how thin the year was getting, because saying it would not have helped.","art":"art/story/sm/jt-golden-goose.jpg","route":"#/story/jt.golden-goose|h0","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","More Jataka Tales"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-jt.golden-goose-1":{"src":"passage:hi:story:jt.golden-goose:1","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Goose Who Gave Gold","text":"फिर एक सुबह छत पर एक हंस आकर उतरा — और उसका हर एक पंख सोने का था। असली सोना, भारी वाला, ऐसा जो गिराने पर खनक उठता है।","lang":"hi","body":"Then one morning a goose came down onto the roof — and every feather on him was gold. Real gold, the heavy kind, the kind that rings when you drop it.","art":"art/story/sm/jt-golden-goose.jpg","route":"#/story/jt.golden-goose|h1","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","More Jataka Tales"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-jt.golden-goose-2":{"src":"passage:hi:story:jt.golden-goose:2","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Goose Who Gave Gold","text":"\"मैं इस घर को जानता हूँ,\" हंस ने कहा। \"कैसे, यह मैं नहीं बताऊँगा। यह लो।\" और उसने हिलाकर एक पंख सीढ़ी पर गिरा दिया। \"इसे बेच देना। जब तक तुम्हें मेरी ज़रूरत रहेगी, मैं हर कुछ दिनों में आकर एक और पंख छोड़ जाऊँगा।\"","lang":"hi","body":"\"I know this house,\" said the goose. \"I will not explain how. Here.\" And he shook one feather loose onto the step. \"Sell that. I will come every few days and leave another, for as long as you need me.\"","art":"art/story/sm/jt-golden-goose.jpg","route":"#/story/jt.golden-goose|h2","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","More Jataka Tales"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-jt.golden-goose-3":{"src":"passage:hi:story:jt.golden-goose:3","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Goose Who Gave Gold","text":"और उसने ऐसा ही किया। छत की मरम्मत हो गई। बच्चियों को जूते मिल गए। माँ फिर से बातों पर हँसने लगीं। हर कुछ दिनों में छत पर एक हल्की-सी धप की आवाज़ होती और सीढ़ी पर एक और पंख मिलता, और घर ने जैसे चैन की साँस ली।","lang":"hi","body":"And he did. The roof got mended. The girls got shoes. The mother laughed at things again. Every few days there was a soft thump on the roof and one more feather on the step, and the house breathed out.","art":"art/story/sm/jt-golden-goose.jpg","route":"#/story/jt.golden-goose|h3","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","More Jataka Tales"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-jt.golden-goose-4":{"src":"passage:hi:story:jt.golden-goose:4","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Goose Who Gave Gold","text":"महीने बीतते गए। फिर एक शाम माँ खाली सीढ़ी को देखते हुए बैठी थीं और उनके मन में वही ख़याल आया जो हफ़्तों से धीरे-धीरे उनके दिमाग में घर कर रहा था। उसके पास सैकड़ों पंख हैं। सैकड़ों। और वह हमेशा बस एक ही छोड़ कर जाता है।","lang":"hi","body":"Months went by. Then one evening the mother sat looking at the empty step and thought a thought that had been creeping up on her for weeks. He has hundreds of feathers. Hundreds. And he only ever leaves one.","art":"art/story/sm/jt-golden-goose.jpg","route":"#/story/jt.golden-goose|h4","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","More Jataka Tales"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-jt.golden-goose-5":{"src":"passage:hi:story:jt.golden-goose:5","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Goose Who Gave Gold","text":"\"बस इस एक बार,\" उन्होंने बच्चियों से कहा, \"और फिर हमें कभी कोई चिंता नहीं करनी पड़ेगी।\" सबसे बड़ी बेटी ने कहा, \"माँ, वह अपने आप ही तो आता है।\" पर उसकी माँ असल में सुन ही नहीं रही थीं।","lang":"hi","body":"\"Just this once,\" she told the girls, \"and then we never have to worry again.\" The eldest said, \"Ma, he comes on his own.\" Her mother was not really listening.","art":"art/story/sm/jt-golden-goose.jpg","route":"#/story/jt.golden-goose|h5","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","More Jataka Tales"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-jt.golden-goose-6":{"src":"passage:hi:story:jt.golden-goose:6","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Goose Who Gave Gold","text":"उसने उसे बड़े प्यार से ही पकड़ा। पंख भी उसने बड़े आराम से ही खींचे। और जैसे ही एक-एक पंख उससे अलग हुआ, वह एक मामूली सफ़ेद पंख बन गया — कबूतर के पंख जैसा सादा, जिसकी कोई क़ीमत ही नहीं थी।","lang":"hi","body":"She caught him gently enough. She pulled the feathers out gently enough. And every single one of them, the moment it left him, turned into an ordinary white feather — plain as a pigeon, worth nothing at all.","art":"art/story/sm/jt-golden-goose.jpg","route":"#/story/jt.golden-goose|h6","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","More Jataka Tales"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-jt.golden-goose-7":{"src":"passage:hi:story:jt.golden-goose:7","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Goose Who Gave Gold","text":"हंस ने देर तक उसकी तरफ़ देखा। \"वह एक तोहफ़ा था,\" उसने कहा। \"इसीलिए तो वह सोने का था।\" और क्योंकि वह उड़ नहीं सकता था, वह चलकर छत के किनारे तक गया और सड़क पर आगे बढ़ गया।","lang":"hi","body":"The goose looked at her for a long moment. \"It was a gift,\" he said. \"That is what made it gold.\" And he walked to the edge of the roof, because he could not fly, and went away down the road.","art":"art/story/sm/jt-golden-goose.jpg","route":"#/story/jt.golden-goose|h7","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","More Jataka Tales"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-jt.woodpecker-lion-0":{"src":"passage:hi:story:jt.woodpecker-lion:0","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Bird Who Went Down the Lion's Throat","text":"एक शेर ने अपनी पुरानी आदत के मुताबिक़ बहुत जल्दी-जल्दी खा लिया, और कोई नुकीली चीज़ टेढ़ी होकर गले में फँस गई। न वह निगल पा रहा था, न दहाड़ पा रहा था। आँखों में पानी भरे वह एक पेड़ के नीचे पड़ा रहा और उसके गले से एक हल्की, बेबस सी सीटी जैसी आवाज़ निकलती रही।","lang":"hi","body":"A lion ate too fast, the way he always did, and something sharp went in sideways and stuck. He could not swallow. He could not roar. He lay under a tree with his eyes watering and made a small, undignified, whistling noise.","art":"art/story/sm/jt-woodpecker-lion.jpg","route":"#/story/jt.woodpecker-lion|h0","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","More Jataka Tales"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-jt.woodpecker-lion-1":{"src":"passage:hi:story:jt.woodpecker-lion:1","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Bird Who Went Down the Lion's Throat","text":"एक कठफोड़वा डाली पर फुदककर नीचे आई और उसे देखने लगी। \"वह तो हड्डी है,\" वह बोली। \"अंदर। मुझे उसका सिरा दिख रहा है।\" शेर ने और ज़्यादा छटपटाते हुए फिर वही सीटी जैसी आवाज़ निकाली।","lang":"hi","body":"A woodpecker hopped down a branch and looked at him. \"That is a bone,\" she said. \"In there. I can see the end of it.\" The lion made the whistling noise again, more urgently.","art":"art/story/sm/jt-woodpecker-lion.jpg","route":"#/story/jt.woodpecker-lion|h1","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","More Jataka Tales"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-jt.woodpecker-lion-2":{"src":"passage:hi:story:jt.woodpecker-lion:2","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Bird Who Went Down the Lion's Throat","text":"कठफोड़वा सोचने लगी। उसका पूरा सिर एक शेर के मुँह के अंदर जाना होगा। उसका पूरा सिर। अंदर। मुँह के। एक शेर के।","lang":"hi","body":"The woodpecker considered the situation. Her whole head would have to go inside the mouth of a lion. Her whole head. Inside. The mouth. Of a lion.","art":"art/story/sm/jt-woodpecker-lion.jpg","route":"#/story/jt.woodpecker-lion|h2","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","More Jataka Tales"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-jt.woodpecker-lion-3":{"src":"passage:hi:story:jt.woodpecker-lion:3","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Bird Who Went Down the Lion's Throat","text":"वह फुदककर अंदर गई, हड्डी को पकड़ा, अपने पैर जमाए और उसे खींचकर निकाल लिया। फिर वह बाहर आई, लकड़ी को हटा दिया और डाल पर बैठकर थर-थर काँपने लगी।","lang":"hi","body":"She hopped in, took hold of the bone, braced her feet, and pulled it free. Then she came out, knocked the stick away, and sat on the branch shaking rather a lot.","art":"art/story/sm/jt-woodpecker-lion.jpg","route":"#/story/jt.woodpecker-lion|h3","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","More Jataka Tales"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-jt.woodpecker-lion-4":{"src":"passage:hi:story:jt.woodpecker-lion:4","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Bird Who Went Down the Lion's Throat","text":"शेर उठकर बैठ गया। उसने खाँसा। उसने धीरे से दहाड़ने की कोशिश की और दहाड़ निकल आई। \"हा! अब कुछ ठीक लगा।\" और बिना कुछ और बोले वह उठकर लंबी घास में चला गया।","lang":"hi","body":"The lion sat up. He coughed. He tried a small roar and it worked. \"Ha! That is better.\" And he got up and walked off into the long grass without another word.","art":"art/story/sm/jt-woodpecker-lion.jpg","route":"#/story/jt.woodpecker-lion|h4","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","More Jataka Tales"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-jt.woodpecker-lion-5":{"src":"passage:hi:story:jt.woodpecker-lion:5","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Bird Who Went Down the Lion's Throat","text":"कुछ हफ़्तों बाद कठफोड़वा भूखी थी, और उसने शेर को खाते हुए देखा, तो वह नीचे आई और विनम्रता से एक किनारे खड़ी हो गई। \"दोस्त,\" उसने कहा। \"क्या तुम्हें मैं याद हूँ?\"","lang":"hi","body":"Some weeks later the woodpecker was hungry, and she saw the lion eating, and she came down and stood politely at the edge of it. \"Friend,\" she said. \"Do you remember me?\"","art":"art/story/sm/jt-woodpecker-lion.jpg","route":"#/story/jt.woodpecker-lion|h5","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","More Jataka Tales"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-jt.woodpecker-lion-6":{"src":"passage:hi:story:jt.woodpecker-lion:6","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Bird Who Went Down the Lion's Throat","text":"\"मुझे तुम याद हो,\" बिना ऊपर देखे शेर ने कहा। \"तुमने एक शेर के मुँह में अपना सिर डाला था, और वह सलामत तुम्हारे धड़ पर लगा हुआ ही बाहर निकल आया। तुम्हें और क्या चाहिए? ज़्यादातर जानवरों को तो इतना भी नसीब नहीं होता।\"","lang":"hi","body":"\"I remember you,\" said the lion, not looking up. \"You put your head inside the mouth of a lion, and you came out again with it still attached. What more do you want? Most creatures do not get that.\"","art":"art/story/sm/jt-woodpecker-lion.jpg","route":"#/story/jt.woodpecker-lion|h6","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","More Jataka Tales"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-jt.woodpecker-lion-7":{"src":"passage:hi:story:jt.woodpecker-lion:7","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Bird Who Went Down the Lion's Throat","text":"कठफोड़वा ने इस बात पर सोचा। फिर वह उड़कर अपनी डाल पर जा बैठी और कीड़े ढूँढने के लिए चोंच मारने लगी, जिसमें वह शुरू से ही बहुत माहिर थी।","lang":"hi","body":"The woodpecker thought about that. Then she flew up to her branch and started tapping for grubs, which she had been perfectly good at all along.","art":"art/story/sm/jt-woodpecker-lion.jpg","route":"#/story/jt.woodpecker-lion|h7","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","More Jataka Tales"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-jt.elephant-dog-0":{"src":"passage:hi:story:jt.elephant-dog:0","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Elephant Who Stopped Eating","text":"राजा का हाथी ऐसे हाथीखाने में रहता था जो ज़्यादातर घरों से भी बड़ा था, उसे दिन में दो बार नहलाया जाता था, और घी में पके चावल खाने को मिलते थे। किसी भी नज़र से देखें, तो वह पूरे राज्य का सबसे किस्मत वाला हाथी था।","lang":"hi","body":"The king's elephant lived in a stable bigger than most houses, and was washed twice a day, and was given rice cooked with ghee. He was, by every measure anybody had, the luckiest elephant in the kingdom.","art":"art/story/sm/jt-elephant-dog.jpg","route":"#/story/jt.elephant-dog|h0","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","More Jataka Tales"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-jt.elephant-dog-1":{"src":"passage:hi:story:jt.elephant-dog:1","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Elephant Who Stopped Eating","text":"एक दोपहर एक दुबला-पतला गली का कुत्ता खाने की तलाश में बाड़े में आ गया और उसे हाथी की नाँद के नीचे बचा-खुचा खाना मिल गया। हाथी कुछ देर उसे नीचे देखता रहा। फिर उसने अपने पैर से थोड़ा और चावल किनारे से नीचे धकेल दिया।","lang":"hi","body":"A thin street dog got into the yard one afternoon looking for scraps and found the leftovers under the elephant's trough. The elephant looked down at him for a while. Then he pushed a little more rice over the edge with his foot.","art":"art/story/sm/jt-elephant-dog.jpg","route":"#/story/jt.elephant-dog|h1","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","More Jataka Tales"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-jt.elephant-dog-2":{"src":"passage:hi:story:jt.elephant-dog:2","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Elephant Who Stopped Eating","text":"बस, ऐसे ही शुरुआत हुई। कुत्ता रोज़ आने लगा। वह हाथी के आगे वाले पैरों के बीच सोता था। हाथी उसे अपनी सूँड से बीच से उठाता और इधर-उधर झुलाता, और कुत्ता पैर चलाते हुए भौंकता, जो कि कुत्तों के हँसने का तरीका होता है।","lang":"hi","body":"That was how it started. The dog came every day. He slept between the elephant's front feet. The elephant picked him up by the middle with his trunk and swung him about, and the dog barked with his legs going, which is a dog's way of laughing.","art":"art/story/sm/jt-elephant-dog.jpg","route":"#/story/jt.elephant-dog|h2","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","More Jataka Tales"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-jt.elephant-dog-3":{"src":"passage:hi:story:jt.elephant-dog:3","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Elephant Who Stopped Eating","text":"फिर एक किसान बाड़े से निकला, उसने बिना पट्टे का एक अच्छा-भला कुत्ता देखा और कहा, \"तुम ठीक रहोगे।\" वह उसे उठाकर अपने गाँव ले गया, और महल में किसी ने एक पल के लिए भी इस पर ध्यान नहीं दिया।","lang":"hi","body":"Then a farmer came through the yard, saw a good-looking dog with nobody's rope on him, and said, \"You will do.\" He picked him up and carried him off to his village, and nobody in the palace thought about it for one second.","art":"art/story/sm/jt-elephant-dog.jpg","route":"#/story/jt.elephant-dog|h3","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","More Jataka Tales"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-jt.elephant-dog-4":{"src":"passage:hi:story:jt.elephant-dog:4","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Elephant Who Stopped Eating","text":"हाथी ने उस रात कुछ नहीं खाया। न ही अगले दिन। वह दीवार की तरफ मुँह किए खड़ा रहा। देख-रेख करने वालों ने उसे गन्ना दिया, फिर गुड़, फिर उसका मनपसंद हरा चारा, लेकिन वह पीछे मुड़ा तक नहीं।","lang":"hi","body":"The elephant did not eat that night. Or the next day. He stood facing the wall. The keepers offered him sugarcane, then jaggery, then his favourite green fodder, and he did not turn round.","art":"art/story/sm/jt-elephant-dog.jpg","route":"#/story/jt.elephant-dog|h4","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","More Jataka Tales"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-jt.elephant-dog-5":{"src":"passage:hi:story:jt.elephant-dog:5","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Elephant Who Stopped Eating","text":"राजा ने अपने सबसे समझदार मंत्री को भेजा। मंत्री जी हाथी के चारों तरफ दो बार घूमे और फिर उन्होंने वह किया जो किसी भी देखभाल करने वाले ने नहीं सोचा था। उन्होंने हाथीखाने के लड़कों से पूछा कि क्या बदला था।","lang":"hi","body":"The king sent his wisest minister, who walked round the elephant twice and then did something none of the keepers had thought to do. He asked the stable boys what had changed.","art":"art/story/sm/jt-elephant-dog.jpg","route":"#/story/jt.elephant-dog|h5","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","More Jataka Tales"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-jt.elephant-dog-6":{"src":"passage:hi:story:jt.elephant-dog:6","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Elephant Who Stopped Eating","text":"\"आपका हाथी बीमार नहीं है,\" मंत्री ने राजा से कहा। \"वह अकेला है। हर गाँव में संदेश भेज दीजिए: जिसके पास भी वह कुत्ता है, उसे छोड़ दे। वह कोई लावारिस नहीं है। वह किसी का दोस्त है।\"","lang":"hi","body":"\"Your elephant is not sick,\" the minister told the king. \"He is lonely. Send a message to every village: whoever has that dog, let him go. He is not a stray. He is somebody's friend.\"","art":"art/story/sm/jt-elephant-dog.jpg","route":"#/story/jt.elephant-dog|h6","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","More Jataka Tales"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-jt.elephant-dog-7":{"src":"passage:hi:story:jt.elephant-dog:7","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Elephant Who Stopped Eating","text":"चार दिन बाद वह कुत्ता सड़क से वापस आया, मैला-कुचैला और बेहद खुश। हाथी ने उसे अपनी सूँड से उठाकर अपने सिर पर बिठा लिया, और तभी, जब कुत्ता ऊपर बैठ गया, वह आगे बढ़ा और खाना खाने लगा।","lang":"hi","body":"The dog came back up the road four days later, filthy and delighted. The elephant lifted him with his trunk and set him on his own head, and only then, with the dog sitting up there, did he walk over and start eating.","art":"art/story/sm/jt-elephant-dog.jpg","route":"#/story/jt.elephant-dog|h7","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","More Jataka Tales"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-jt.nandivisala-0":{"src":"passage:hi:story:jt.nandivisala:0","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Ox Who Would Not Be Shouted At","text":"एक आदमी ने एक बछड़े को बचपन से पाला, उसे अपने हाथों से खिलाया और हर वक़्त उससे यूँ ही इधर-उधर की बातें करता रहता। वह बछड़ा बड़ा होकर दरवाज़े जैसे चौड़े कंधों वाला एक बैल बन गया, और वे दोनों एक-दूसरे को बखूबी समझते थे।","lang":"hi","body":"A man raised a calf from a baby, feeding him by hand, talking to him the whole time about nothing in particular. The calf grew into an ox with shoulders like a doorway, and the two of them understood each other perfectly.","art":"art/story/sm/jt-nandivisala.jpg","route":"#/story/jt.nandivisala|h0","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","More Jataka Tales"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-jt.nandivisala-1":{"src":"passage:hi:story:jt.nandivisala:1","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Ox Who Would Not Be Shouted At","text":"\"आपने मुझे बहुत अच्छे से रखा है,\" एक सुबह बैल ने कहा। \"अब मुझे आपका कर्ज़ चुकाने दीजिए। जाइए और शहर के सबसे अमीर सेठ से यह शर्त लगाइए कि मैं एक ही जगह खड़े-खड़े आपस में जुड़ी हुई सामान से भरी सौ गाड़ियाँ खींच सकता हूँ।\"","lang":"hi","body":"\"You have kept me well,\" said the ox one morning. \"Let me pay you back. Go and find the richest merchant in town and bet him that I can pull a hundred loaded carts, all joined together, from a standing start.\"","art":"art/story/sm/jt-nandivisala.jpg","route":"#/story/jt.nandivisala|h1","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","More Jataka Tales"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-jt.nandivisala-2":{"src":"passage:hi:story:jt.nandivisala:2","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Ox Who Would Not Be Shouted At","text":"सेठ इतनी ज़ोर से हँसा कि उसे बैठना ही पड़ गया। \"सौ गाड़ियाँ? हज़ार रुपये की शर्त रही कि यह बीस भी नहीं हिला पाएगा।\" \"मंज़ूर,\" उस आदमी ने कहा, जिसके पास हज़ार रुपये थे ही नहीं और जिसने इस बारे में अभी तक सोचा भी नहीं था।","lang":"hi","body":"The merchant laughed so hard he had to sit down. \"A hundred? A thousand rupees says he cannot shift twenty.\" \"Done,\" said the man, who did not have a thousand rupees and had not thought about that yet.","art":"art/story/sm/jt-nandivisala.jpg","route":"#/story/jt.nandivisala|h2","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","More Jataka Tales"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-jt.nandivisala-3":{"src":"passage:hi:story:jt.nandivisala:3","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Ox Who Would Not Be Shouted At","text":"पूरे गाँव के देखते-देखते उन्होंने सड़क पर गाड़ियाँ कतार में लगा दीं। सबसे आगे वाली गाड़ी में बैल को जोता गया। उसका मालिक ऊपर चढ़ा, छड़ी उठाई — और इतने सारे लोगों के सामने न जाने उसे क्या हो गया।","lang":"hi","body":"They lined the carts up on the road with the whole town watching. The ox was yoked to the front one. His owner climbed up, took the goad — and something got into him, in front of all those people.","art":"art/story/sm/jt-nandivisala.jpg","route":"#/story/jt.nandivisala|h3","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","More Jataka Tales"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-jt.nandivisala-4":{"src":"passage:hi:story:jt.nandivisala:4","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Ox Who Would Not Be Shouted At","text":"\"खींचो, अरे ज़िद्दी जानवर!\" वह चिल्लाया। \"आगे बढ़ो, निकम्मे कहीं के!\"","lang":"hi","body":"\"PULL, you stubborn brute!\" he shouted. \"Get ON with it, you useless animal!\"","art":"art/story/sm/jt-nandivisala.jpg","route":"#/story/jt.nandivisala|h4","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","More Jataka Tales"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-jt.nandivisala-5":{"src":"passage:hi:story:jt.nandivisala:5","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Ox Who Would Not Be Shouted At","text":"बैल अपनी जगह से बाल बराबर भी नहीं हिला। एक खुर तक नहीं। भीड़ शोर मचाती रही और वह दीवार की तरह वहीं खड़ा रहा, और उसके मालिक को उधार माँगकर पूरे हज़ार रुपये चुकाने पड़े और वह बिना किसी की तरफ़ देखे चुपचाप घर लौट गया।","lang":"hi","body":"The ox did not move a hair. Not one hoof. He stood there like a wall while the crowd howled, and his owner paid over a thousand rupees he had to borrow, and walked home not looking at anybody.","art":"art/story/sm/jt-nandivisala.jpg","route":"#/story/jt.nandivisala|h5","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","More Jataka Tales"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-jt.nandivisala-6":{"src":"passage:hi:story:jt.nandivisala:6","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Ox Who Would Not Be Shouted At","text":"उस शाम बैल आया और उसने बाड़े के ऊपर अपना सिर टिका दिया। \"क्या मैंने कभी आपका कोई बर्तन तोड़ा?\" उसने पूछा। \"क्या कभी किसी बच्चे पर पैर रखा? क्या मैं कभी एक बार भी अड़ियल बना?\" \"नहीं,\" आदमी ने कहा। \"तो फिर आपने पूरे गाँव के सामने मुझे ऐसी बातें क्यों कहीं?\"","lang":"hi","body":"That evening the ox came and put his head over the fence. \"Have I ever broken a pot of yours?\" he said. \"Have I ever stepped on a child? Have I ever once been stubborn?\" \"No,\" said the man. \"Then why did you call me those things in front of the whole town?\"","art":"art/story/sm/jt-nandivisala.jpg","route":"#/story/jt.nandivisala|h6","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","More Jataka Tales"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-jt.nandivisala-7":{"src":"passage:hi:story:jt.nandivisala:7","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Ox Who Would Not Be Shouted At","text":"तो उन्होंने फिर से गाड़ियों की कतार लगाई। और इस बार आदमी आगे झुका और हौले से बोला, बिल्कुल वैसे ही जैसे वह तब बोलता था जब बैल बछड़ा था: \"शाबाश मेरे प्यारे, चलो। अब आगे बढ़ते हैं।\"","lang":"hi","body":"So they lined the carts up again. And this time the man leaned forward and said, quietly, the way he had said it when the ox was a calf: \"Come on then, my beauty. Off we go.\"","art":"art/story/sm/jt-nandivisala.jpg","route":"#/story/jt.nandivisala|h7","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","More Jataka Tales"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-jt.nandivisala-8":{"src":"passage:hi:story:jt.nandivisala:8","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Ox Who Would Not Be Shouted At","text":"बैल ने जुए पर ज़ोर लगाया। सौ गाड़ियों की लंबी कतार में एक-एक करके सारी रस्सियाँ तनती चली गईं — और पूरी सड़क ही जैसे आगे बढ़ने लगी।","lang":"hi","body":"The ox leaned into the yoke. The ropes came up tight one by one all down the line, a hundred carts long — and the whole road began to move.","art":"art/story/sm/jt-nandivisala.jpg","route":"#/story/jt.nandivisala|h8","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","More Jataka Tales"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-jt.monkey-gardener-0":{"src":"passage:hi:story:jt.monkey-gardener:0","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Monkeys Who Watered the Garden","text":"राजा के बाग में कतारों में लगे छोटे-छोटे पौधे भरे थे, जिनमें से हर एक लगभग किसी बच्चे जितना लंबा था। माली एक महीने से हर शाम उन्हें पानी दे रहा था, और अब जाकर उनके पत्ते ठीक से संभलने लगे थे।","lang":"hi","body":"The king's pleasure garden was full of young saplings, planted in rows, each one about as tall as a child. The gardener had watered them every evening for a month, and they were just beginning to hold their leaves properly.","art":"art/story/sm/jt-monkey-gardener.jpg","route":"#/story/jt.monkey-gardener|h0","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","More Jataka Tales"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-jt.monkey-gardener-1":{"src":"passage:hi:story:jt.monkey-gardener:1","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Monkeys Who Watered the Garden","text":"फिर एक त्योहार आया, और माली वहां जाना चाहता था। पास ही आम के पेड़ पर बंदरों की एक पूरी टोली रहती थी, जो हर रोज़ उसे काम करते देखती थी। \"सुनो,\" उसने कहा। \"तुमने मुझे यह काम सौ बार करते देखा है। आज शाम इन पौधों को पानी दे देना, तो बदले में तुम सबको बढ़िया फल मिलेंगे।\"","lang":"hi","body":"Then a festival came, and the gardener wanted to go, and there was a whole troop of monkeys living in the mango tree who watched him work every single day. \"You,\" he said. \"You have seen me do it a hundred times. Water the saplings this evening and there is fruit in it for all of you.\"","art":"art/story/sm/jt-monkey-gardener.jpg","route":"#/story/jt.monkey-gardener|h1","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","More Jataka Tales"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-jt.monkey-gardener-2":{"src":"passage:hi:story:jt.monkey-gardener:2","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Monkeys Who Watered the Garden","text":"\"पौधों को पानी देना!\" बंदरों का सरदार खुश होकर चहका। \"यह तो हम कर ही सकते हैं। पानी के काम में तो हम बड़े उस्ताद हैं।\" और माली, जो इतने सस्ते में काम निपटते देख बहुत खुश था, मजे से अपने त्योहार में चला गया।","lang":"hi","body":"\"Water the saplings!\" cried the monkey chief, delighted. \"We can do that. We are extremely good at water.\" And the gardener, who had never wanted a job done so cheaply, went off happily to his festival.","art":"art/story/sm/jt-monkey-gardener.jpg","route":"#/story/jt.monkey-gardener|h2","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","More Jataka Tales"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-jt.monkey-gardener-3":{"src":"passage:hi:story:jt.monkey-gardener:3","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Monkeys Who Watered the Garden","text":"बंदर सारे मटके और चमड़े की बाल्टियां उठा लाए और कतार लगाकर खड़े हो गए। वे बस शुरू करने ही वाले थे कि सरदार ने हाथ उठाकर सबको रोका।","lang":"hi","body":"The monkeys fetched every pot and every leather bucket and lined up along the row, and they were about to start, when the chief held up a hand.","art":"art/story/sm/jt-monkey-gardener.jpg","route":"#/story/jt.monkey-gardener|h3","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","More Jataka Tales"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-jt.monkey-gardener-4":{"src":"passage:hi:story:jt.monkey-gardener:4","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Monkeys Who Watered the Garden","text":"\"रुको,\" उसने कहा। \"पानी बड़ा अनमोल है। बड़े पौधे को थोड़ा-सा पानी देना और छोटे को बहुत सारा, यह तो बर्बादी होगी। हमें हर पौधे को बिल्कुल सही नाप से पानी देना होगा — उसकी जड़ों के हिसाब से।\"","lang":"hi","body":"\"Wait,\" he said. \"Water is precious. It would be wasteful to give a big tree a small drink and a small tree a big one. We must give each sapling exactly the right amount — according to the size of its roots.\"","art":"art/story/sm/jt-monkey-gardener.jpg","route":"#/story/jt.monkey-gardener|h4","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","More Jataka Tales"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-jt.monkey-gardener-5":{"src":"passage:hi:story:jt.monkey-gardener:5","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Monkeys Who Watered the Garden","text":"पूरे झुंड ने सिर हिलाया। बात बड़ी ही समझदारी भरी लगी। बस एक ही मुश्किल थी: जड़ें तो किसी को दिख नहीं रही थीं।","lang":"hi","body":"The whole troop nodded. It sounded extremely wise. There was only one difficulty: nobody could see the roots.","art":"art/story/sm/jt-monkey-gardener.jpg","route":"#/story/jt.monkey-gardener|h5","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","More Jataka Tales"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-jt.monkey-gardener-6":{"src":"passage:hi:story:jt.monkey-gardener:6","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Monkeys Who Watered the Garden","text":"उन्होंने यह काम बड़े ध्यान से किया। एक-एक पेड़ को बाहर निकाला गया, उसकी जड़ों को देखकर नापा-परखा गया, बिल्कुल सही मात्रा में पानी दिया गया, और फिर वापस गड्ढे में दबा दिया गया। करते-करते अंधेरा हो गया। वे अपने आप से बेहद खुश थे।","lang":"hi","body":"They were very thorough about it. Every single tree came up, got its roots inspected and carefully compared, received precisely the correct amount of water, and was pushed back into its hole. It took them until dark. They were extremely pleased with themselves.","art":"art/story/sm/jt-monkey-gardener.jpg","route":"#/story/jt.monkey-gardener|h6","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","More Jataka Tales"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-jt.monkey-gardener-7":{"src":"passage:hi:story:jt.monkey-gardener:7","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Monkeys Who Watered the Garden","text":"अगली सुबह जब माली लौटा, तो बगीचे में बस मुरझाई हुई सूखी टहनियाँ बची थीं। वह काफी देर तक वहीं खड़ा रहा। बंदरों का सरदार नीचे उतरा और उम्मीद भरी आवाज़ में बोला, \"हमने एक-एक को नापा था।\"","lang":"hi","body":"The gardener came back the next morning to a garden of wilted sticks. He stood there a long time. The monkey chief came down and said, hopefully, \"We measured every one.\"","art":"art/story/sm/jt-monkey-gardener.jpg","route":"#/story/jt.monkey-gardener|h7","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","More Jataka Tales"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-jt.crocodile-rock-0":{"src":"passage:hi:story:jt.crocodile-rock:0","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Rock That Answered Back","text":"एक बंदर था जो नदी के एक किनारे रहता था और दूसरे किनारे जाकर खाता था, क्योंकि फलों के सारे पेड़ उस पार थे। वह रोज़ दो बार उसी रास्ते से नदी पार करता: किनारा, बीच की चट्टान, टापू। किनारा, चट्टान, टापू। वह तो आँखें मूँदकर भी यह कर सकता था।","lang":"hi","body":"There was a monkey who lived on one bank of a river and ate on the other, because the fruit trees were all on the far side. He crossed twice a day by the same route: bank, rock in the middle, island. Bank, rock, island. He could have done it with his eyes shut.","art":"art/story/sm/jt-crocodile-rock.jpg","route":"#/story/jt.crocodile-rock|h0","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","More Jataka Tales"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-jt.crocodile-rock-1":{"src":"passage:hi:story:jt.crocodile-rock:1","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Rock That Answered Back","text":"एक मगरमच्छ दो हफ़्तों से उसे ऐसा करते देख रहा था। \"दिन में दो बार,\" उसने अपने आप से कहा। \"उसी चट्टान के ऊपर से। एक बार भी देखता तक नहीं।\"","lang":"hi","body":"A crocodile had been watching him do it for a fortnight. \"Twice a day,\" he said to himself. \"Over the same rock. He never once looks.\"","art":"art/story/sm/jt-crocodile-rock.jpg","route":"#/story/jt.crocodile-rock|h1","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","More Jataka Tales"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-jt.crocodile-rock-2":{"src":"passage:hi:story:jt.crocodile-rock:2","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Rock That Answered Back","text":"तो उस शाम मगरमच्छ चुपचाप तैरकर नदी के बीच पहुँचा और चट्टान पर जा बैठा—नीचा, मटमैला और बिल्कुल शांत। और किनारे से देखने पर ऐसा लगता था मानो वह चट्टान थोड़ी और बड़ी हो गई हो।","lang":"hi","body":"So that evening the crocodile swam quietly to the middle of the river and settled himself on top of the rock, low and grey and absolutely still, and became — as far as anybody could tell from the bank — a slightly larger rock.","art":"art/story/sm/jt-crocodile-rock.jpg","route":"#/story/jt.crocodile-rock|h2","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","More Jataka Tales"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]}});
